# Decision\" Docs/DECISIONS.md | tail -5","description":"Find what Atlas is and where eval A and the 2A report live in the docs"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e872784e-53ea-4f75-b0d7-ff9235e0ab43","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgY35YE2JkDu2R3kUGE8K","requestRef":"94ac9c6a-0869-4b32-adf3-6abc568db66c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd90f4c1-a05f-4be1-a720-de6f6ed3a6b7","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:35:38.948Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"fd90f4c1-a05f-4be1-a720-de6f6ed3a6b7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"f40c2187-e8b4-47d5-9c53-ee1f5c6e6ab4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AQQ1DGqcqHHxrd9Dk9nweB","type":"tool_result","content":"Docs/BRIEF.md:87:**Tinker is the main tool, and the depth goes there.** The others support it with one job each. The data layer is MongoDB Atlas (already set up), not Tiger Data. There is no .tech domain.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:100:- **MongoDB Atlas:** the data layer.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:102:  - Atlas Search with fuzzy matching, because OCR turns \"apparition\" into \"appariiion\".\nDocs/BRIEF.md:103:  - Atlas Vector Search for \"ghosts like this one\", with an open embedding model.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:165:   - Tinker balance and model list. MongoDB Atlas tier and storage limit.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:167:3. **Data layer:** reports into Atlas (geo, fuzzy search, vectors). A second Temporal pass that pulls follow-ups and death notices for the top cases.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:39:  - Atlas: tier, version, storage limit and storage used, and whether Atlas Search and Vector Search indexes can be created (create one of each on a scratch collection, then drop it)\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:46:- A walking skeleton: one real 1850 article (the Stratford, Conn. \"knockings\" report from the first probe) goes into a scratch Atlas collection, out through an API endpoint, and onto a web page that shows the IIIF crop next to the text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:82:- Pydantic models, with Atlas validators generated from them.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:84:- A storage budget built from real document sizes, and a written decision on what goes into Atlas.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:115:- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:120:- Atlas counts match the local counts, and storage is within the limit.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:162:  - eight place-type glyphs in a 19th-century atlas engraving style\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:186:- `render.yaml`, the Atlas network-access change, environment variables, Sentry releases, and a smoke test on the live URL.\n---\n67:- Eval A, with charts:\n---\nARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md\n7:## Next step\n15:## STATUS: Phase 1, scaffolding and environment (2026-10-29)\n52:## Setup before Phase 1 (2026-10-29)\n---","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"46674d21-340b-41d8-8bfc-6563332abfcc","timestamp":"2026-10-30T07:35:39.672Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Docs/BRIEF.md:87:**Tinker is the main tool, and the depth goes there.** The others support it with one job each. The data layer is MongoDB Atlas (already set up), not Tiger Data. There is no .tech domain.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:100:- **MongoDB Atlas:** the data layer.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:102:  - Atlas Search with fuzzy matching, because OCR turns \"apparition\" into \"appariiion\".\nDocs/BRIEF.md:103:  - Atlas Vector Search for \"ghosts like this one\", with an open embedding model.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:165:   - Tinker balance and model list. MongoDB Atlas tier and storage limit.\nDocs/BRIEF.md:167:3. **Data layer:** reports into Atlas (geo, fuzzy search, vectors). A second Temporal pass that pulls follow-ups and death notices for the top cases.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:39:  - Atlas: tier, version, storage limit and storage used, and whether Atlas Search and Vector Search indexes can be created (create one of each on a scratch collection, then drop it)\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:46:- A walking skeleton: one real 1850 article (the Stratford, Conn. \"knockings\" report from the first probe) goes into a scratch Atlas collection, out through an API endpoint, and onto a web page that shows the IIIF crop next to the text.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:82:- Pydantic models, with Atlas validators generated from them.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:84:- A storage budget built from real document sizes, and a written decision on what goes into Atlas.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:115:- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:120:- Atlas counts match the local counts, and storage is within the limit.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:162:  - eight place-type glyphs in a 19th-century atlas engraving style\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:186:- `render.yaml`, the Atlas network-access change, environment variables, Sentry releases, and a smoke test on the live URL.\n---\n67:- Eval A, with charts:\n---\nARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md\n7:## Next step\n15:## STATUS: Phase 1, scaffolding and environment (2026-10-29)\n52:## Setup before Phase 1 (2026-10-29)\n---","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e872784e-53ea-4f75-b0d7-ff9235e0ab43","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":1,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":8},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fd90f4c1-a05f-4be1-a720-de6f6ed3a6b7","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
