{"parentUuid":"e6bc3e2e-451a-47a1-9cd3-08be130c2365","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY3pk3NSpvXe7DN4ssGd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKTguyfmGadHMoNukP9QWu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nEval A: the EDA, what the candidates are, and the lexicon's recall\n\n- make eval (scripts/eval_a.py) writes eval/results/eval_a.json and\n  eight charts to eval/results/eval_a/ in 41 s. The samples are seeded,\n  and a rerun keeps the judgments made by hand.\n- EDA: counts by year, by state (11.2% of candidates have no state) and\n  by term; lengths (median 358 words); OCR quality (median 92.7% of\n  words in the dictionary); and reprint clusters, which leave 801,071\n  distinct stories from 1,050,459 candidates. 20 of 20 sampled cluster\n  pairs are the same story.\n- Composition: 7 of 200 candidates are ghost reports (3.5%, 95%\n  interval 1.7-7.0%), about 36,800 candidates or 22,300 stories. The\n  rest are figurative, fiction, names and titles, religious, social\n  events and other, with 15 OCR accidents among them.\n- Recall: none of 300 near-miss articles and none of 300 non-candidates\n  is a ghost report, so at most 1.26% of each pool. No misses means no\n  lexicon v2.\n- wilson() moves to paperghosts/stats.py. The bar charts size their\n  margin from their labels and give a zero bar a tooltip, and an axis\n  under one gets a step under one.\n- Decision 27.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log -1 --format='%h %s'; git status --short | head -5","description":"Commit the eval A change"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":955,"cache_read_input_tokens":198998,"output_tokens":661,"output_tokens_details":{"thinkin