s hold 330,158 candidates (31.4%), which leaves 801,071 distinct stories. 71,191 clusters span more than one paper.","   - The hand check found 20 of 20 sampled pairs to be the same story.","-  - The largest clusters are syndicated patent-medicine ads (684, 402, 379 and 308 printings), a book ad (487) and a steamer schedule (271).","+  - The largest clusters are syndicated ads, at 684, 402, 379 and 308 printings across 58 to 137 papers. Next come a book ad (487 printings in 2 papers) and the steamer Phantom's schedule (271 in 1 paper).","   - Linking on one shared run chained 6,720 candidates together through Bible verses, so the final method needs two shared runs."," "," ## Composition (200 candidates, drawn uniformly at random, judged by hand)"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ca06d952-d7c8-44c1-906e-1dde4ff8618b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
