{"parentUuid":"db277dce-3223-49bd-8114-cde0df4ced68","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY5W6UtLAbcAFY1V3sAt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015E5qZJbF5oi4qA8HjAXndW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nDrop a masthead date only when it is the issue's, and count scans with no batch path\n\n- The display headline drops a dateline only when its weekday and month\n  are the issue's, and, with no weekday, its day and year too. \"In\" and\n  the paper's place is never a masthead. A number line goes only beside\n  the paper's title or volume.\n- On the same 200 judged lines (headline_drops.py --same) it makes none\n  of the 5 mis-drops and keeps 37 of the 195 correct drops. Precision on\n  the 158 it still drops is 158/158. Over every candidate it drops\n  7,509 lines instead of 10,287, all of them ones the old rule dropped.\n- Eval A counts the candidates whose scan has no batch path, by year:\n  335,907 (32.0%).\n- loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 requests a minute, so crops.get spaces\n  them 3.5 s apart. A probe at one a second was answered 429.\n- Decisions 28 and 29. The second records the stray box of crop 21 as a\n  known limitation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log -1 --format='%h %s' && git push 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" | tail -3","description":"Commit the follow-ups and push the branch","timeout":180000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":929,"cache_read_input_tokens":362205,"output_tokens":635,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":929,"ephemeral_5m_in