{"parentUuid":"ad2fbb75-57d6-410c-b856-0f51bc447c91","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgY5izVLujkiRD4wTmq46","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019itM8LfpyJMeyaMWoBfnPk","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","old_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.","new_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n- The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):\n  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\n  - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.\n  - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.\n- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.\n  - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.\n  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.\n- The reel-to-batch map's hit rate on hidden batches is reported, and every reel with more than one batch is flagged."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_read_input_tokens":376221,"output_tokens":599,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":599,"cache_read_input_tokens":376221,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2300},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019itM8LfpyJMeyaMWoBfnPk":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","old_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.","new_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n- The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):\n  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\n  - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.\n  - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.\n- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.\n  - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.\n  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.\n- The reel-to-batch map's hit rate on hidden batches is reported, and every reel with more than one batch is flagged."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"75b7bc36-7