{"parentUuid":"d278947a-d28d-4696-8614-44fb01e541ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"759d921c-3445-4d20-bf6c-64bf23bda927","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019itM8LfpyJMeyaMWoBfnPk","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"01e0e596-a053-4364-8caf-e503ff4a0bea","timestamp":"2026-10-30T08:10:20.683Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","oldString":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.","newString":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n- The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):\n  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\n  - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.\n  - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.\n- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.\n  - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.\n  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.\n- The reel-to-batch map's hit rate on hidden batches is reported, and every reel with more than one batch is flagged.","originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":84,"oldLines":11,"newStart":84,"newLines":19,"lines":[" - A storage budget built from real document sizes, and a written decision on what goes into Atlas."," - The GeoNames geocoder and its manifest. The LCCN title parser, tested on at least 200 distinct titles."," - The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.","+- The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):","+  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.","+  - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.","+  - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.","+- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.","+  - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.","+  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice."," "," **Gate**"," - Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice."," - The budget is written down."," - Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.","+- The reel-to-batch map's hit rate on hidden batches is reported, and every reel with more than one batch is flagged."," "," ### 2C: the reader"," **Persona:** ML specialist."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d278947a-d28d-4696-8614-44fb01e541ee","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"16c3e6c3163f2ddfed083d6976a1809645aebfad184fbc34701701711af31f4b","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019itM8LfpyJMeyaMWoBfnPk","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","old_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.","new_string":"- The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set.\n- The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):\n  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\n  - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.\n  - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.\n- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.\n  - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.\n  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice.\n\n**Gate**\n- Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice.\n- The budget is written down.\n- Geocoder accuracy is measured on a sample.\n- The reel-to-batch map's hit rate on hidden batches is reported, and every reel with more than one batch is flagged."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
