{"parentUuid":"70cf91ed-bc37-4024-8cc0-db4ddb910381","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"efbe7dae-4a3a-47ef-9f27-91c90fdaed9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01K5uuZgvFaeZBWxGWgSpHvN","type":"tool_result","content":"93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n109:- The cache key is the dataset revision, the lexicon version and the code version. The ingest reads AmericanStories at its 2025-03-26 commit, `77e27fa6`, instead of `main`, so a cached year's input can't change under it.\n120:- All 180 year files, 340.4 GB at revision `77e27fa6`, took 118.6 min on 2026-10-30: an aggregate 47.8 MB/s. Every manifest's `bytes_read` equals the listed size, no year failed, and no partial file was left.\n147:  - The final rule drops 10,287 lines instead of 17,270. The cost is masthead blocks whose title line came out garbled, which now stay in the headline.\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n185:  - All non-candidates: 0 in 300, so at most 1.26%, or at most 4.67 million of 369,263,454. This bound is loose, at 127 times the ghost reports found. Bounding the misses at the 36,800 found would take about 38,600 articles with none among them.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"54e5184e-2adb-42fb-8024-76517b572369","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:14:44.685Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n109:- The cache key is the dataset revision, the lexicon version and the code version. The ingest reads AmericanStories at its 2025-03-26 commit, `77e27fa6`, instead of `main`, so a cached year's input can't change under it.\n120:- All 180 year files, 340.4 GB at revision `77e27fa6`, took 118.6 min on 2026-10-30: an aggregate 47.8 MB/s. Every manifest's `bytes_read` equals the listed size, no year failed, and no partial file was left.\n147:  - The final rule drops 10,287 lines instead of 17,270. The cost is masthead blocks whose title line came out garbled, which now stay in the headline.\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n185:  - All non-candidates: 0 in 300, so at most 1.26%, or at most 4.67 million of 369,263,454. This bound is loose, at 127 times the ghost reports found. Bounding the misses at the 36,800 found would take about 38,600 articles with none among them.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"11eddc3a-6019-42d3-9f98-08ebf4ee871f","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-archive","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"70cf91ed-bc37-4024-8cc0-db4ddb910381","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-429