s of 2 printings, and none of the 157 clusters of 50 or more was checked.","+  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same."," - The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):","   - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.","   - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back."]},{"oldStart":101,"oldLines":12,"newStart":103,"newLines":14,"lines":[" ### 2C: the reader"," **Persona:** ML specialist."," 1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.","+   - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way."," 2. Build the labelling page."," 3. Label the gold set before seeing any model output."," 4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing."," 5. Baselines: a keyword rule, and base 4B both zero-shot and few-shot."," 6. LoRA training on Tinker, iterating on the dev split until improvements stop. Each iteration is recorded."," 7. Eval B, ablations B1 to B10, and edge-case slices E1 to E14.","+   - Eval B also has the reader screen the random reservoirs, for a recall bound that doesn't rest on flag words (decision 30). The Tinker credit check sets how many it reads."," 8. The failure log, and `eval/MODEL_CARD.md`."," 9. The local export and the offline proof."," 10. The full pass over all triaged candidates."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"577e4d36-6331-4665-9ce9-2a421e4b6f6d","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Do