{"parentUuid":"1447d147-59f7-4f75-9782-660e577400bb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"efbe7dae-4a3a-47ef-9f27-91c90fdaed9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CasyhXNnHejQoL644P5xFu","type":"tool_result","content":"14:The disk has 37 GB free, and the largest year alone is 7.6 GB.\n67:`data/` stays local except `data/manifests/` and `data/counts/`. The counts are small JSON files, and keeping them in git lets Phase 2A diff a reproduced run against the committed one.\n110:- Manifests and counts are in git, but candidates and samples are not, so a fresh clone skipped every year and had no candidates. Each manifest now records every output's sha256, and a year is skipped only when every output on disk matches. A size check would miss a damaged file.\n111:- The tarballs are never cached (decision 3): 340 GB won't fit on the disk, and a full re-read costs about 75 minutes and nothing else.\n117:The SDK's default identity is `pid@hostname`, and Temporal keeps it in every workflow's history, which the kill test's screenshots show. Like Sentry's `server_name` (decision 15), the worker, `make ingest` and `make smoke` use `pid@paperghosts-{role}` instead.\n125:  - One clean run gives one wall time and clean kill-test evidence.\n129:  - Kill test 1's SIGKILL cost 1881–1884 their first attempts (`eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md`).\n131:- 1850 reproduces. With its candidates file moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the same sha256 as the committed manifest.\nstep-1.1.md\nstep-1.2.md\nstep-1.3.md\nstep-1.4.md\nstep-1.5.md\nstep-1.6.md\nstep-1.7.md\nstep-1.8.md\nstep-2A.1.md\nstep-2A.2.md\nstep-2A.3.md\nstep-2A.4.md\nstep-2A.5-follow-ups.md\nstep-2A.5.md\nstep-2A.6.md\n1.3G\tdata/candidates\n956K\tdata/counts\n 44K\tdata/crop-check\n7.6M\tdata/crops\n720K\tdata/manifests\n565M\tdata/samples\n 76K\tdata/skeleton\n2.0M\tdata/temporal\nfree: 39Gi","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"92e908d3-d3a6-42b0-8d24-6d1e524506da","