ut my spirits took a gloomy fall, az the thought passed through my mind, that in all probability I would, before its setting, be numbered with the dead. 1\n39\tWINDOW: a lighted fire-brand approached to kindle it. AS she came fully with. in my reach l gave her a kick in the stomach, with all the force l could exert, knocking her back, where she doubled up like a jack. knife, and for anything l know l may have killed her, as she was carried into a tent. This was\n40\t\n41\t=== c-008 | 1896-02-13 | The Indianapolis journal. [volume] (Indianapolis [Ind.]) 1867-1904 | 1096 words | flags: midnight\n42\tHEADLINE: Proceedings in Nature of an Injunc- / ion-CaII ON the Governor /  /  / Next Week. /  / AN EIGHT-HOUR SESSION /  / COMMITTEE CONSIDERABLY d. /  /  / VIDED AS TO PROCEDURE. /  / Resolutions Adopted Late\n43\tOPENING: The Republican State central committee decided at midnight to make last effort to get Governor Matthews to call special session of the Legislature for the purpose of passing a new apportionment law. and in the event that this effort fall suit will be instituted Immediately to set aside the law of 1885 and test all preceding apportionment laws. This conclusion was reached after considering the matter for eight hours i\n44\tWINDOW: The Republican State central committee decided at midnight to make last effort to get Governor Matthews to call special session of the Legislature for the purpose of passing a new apportionment law. and in the event that this effort fall suit will be instituted Immediately to set aside the law of 18\n45\t\n46\t=== c-009 | 1902-08-08 | The Owosso times. (Owosso, Mich.) 1897-1926 | 105 words | flags: midnight\n47\tHEADLINE: COLLIDED ON LAKE ERIE. /  / Steamer Venice Sent to the Bottom /  /  / and Three Persons Drowned.\n48\tOPENING: Cleveland, o., Aug. CAS- a result Of a collision on Lake Erie between the steamer City of Venice, ore laden, and the steamer Seguin, steel lumDer vessel, off Rondeau, Canada, Mon day midnight. the fo