nce and composure as they advance in age which is very much more important TO them than the ability to sit back and saw nothing.\n132\t\n133\t=== c-025 | 1900-07-21 | The Intermountain Catholic. (Salt Lake City [Utah] ;) 1899-1920 | 415 words | flags: spiritual\n134\tHEADLINE: CATHEDRALS.\n135\tOPENING: The word cathedral is derived from the Latin word cathedra, which means chair. and is so called because in the cathedral is erected the episcopal throne. which is located on one side of che choir. usually the gospel side. The chair of St. Peter in Rome has a special attraction for all visitors there. being the one in which St. Peter, Prince OF the Apostles sat. 1t is enclosed in a bronze covering. In every diocese th\n136\tWINDOW: ts in the city in which he is to reside one of the churches for his cathedral, or will build a suitable edifice for that purpose. Here is erected his spiritual throne, from which he judges that tribe of Is rael entrusted to his charge. His SUI pervision extends to all the parishes and faithful of hi\n137\tWINDOW: at tribe of Is rael entrusted to his charge. His SUI pervision extends to all the parishes and faithful of his diocese, and he is bound to supply the spiritual wants of his people, should pastor fail in lis duty to do so. The relations of the bishop to the Catholic Church are ever the same. New pari\n138\t\n139\t=== c-026 | 1922-05-01 | The New York herald. | 387 words | flags: spirit\n140\tHEADLINE: By United States Naval Radio.\n141\tOPENING: Agwibay 10 Hatteras 30th. Albert z Waits 90 w Havana goth. Ario 100 NNE Jupiter 30th. Baldhill 26o Sc Galveston Goth. Bannack $40 Cape May Both. Carriage 1876 South Pass Goth. hester Sun 220 SIC Sabine Bar 10Th. Comus - S Hatteras 10th. Concho 749 u Galveston Both. Currier 170 Il Sabine Bar Goth. Dean Emery 81 = by S Sand Key S0th. Il Il Bedford % n Jupiter 30th. Eastern Dawn 665 \" Ambrose l. 90th. Eastern Glade 2I\n142\tWINDOW: cket L goth. San Jose 2o5 3 New Orleans goth San Pablo 506 iHa