{"parentUuid":"367b4caf-f68a-4105-92ac-823032bf3198","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYaneVJ9yhM8dVcyCHRX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Next is the Phase 2A STATUS block for `Docs/RESUME.md`, newest first, citing the EM's spot check. The \"Next step\" section moves to 2B."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":362373,"output_tokens":3569,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1738},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3569,"cache_read_input_tokens":362373,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"7f5a84df-bb22-4de7-b19a-6c13cb046632","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYandTY12nq428ubJCwZ","requestRef":"a6de453d-a749-4e48-9749-a829ef207c68","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"99df0f70-38e8-4a5a-ae53-d4337277af65","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:31:39.035Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"99df0f70-38e8-4a5a-ae53-d4337277af65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYaneVJ9yhM8dVcyCHRX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FHse65zdVht7CUgu7HJAZP","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/RESUME.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold_next = \"\"\"## Next step\n\n**Phase 2A: the archive read and EDA** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #1 is merged.\n\"\"\"\nnew_next = \"\"\"## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #2 is merged. Lexicon v2 (decision 30) waits on the EM. If it is accepted, its re-read runs before anything is loaded into Atlas.\n\"\"\"\nblock = \"\"\"## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read and EDA (2026-10-30)\n\nBranch `phase-2a-archive`, PR #2.\n\nBuilt:\n- Lexicon v1, with OCR variants, and the near-miss lexicon (decisions 19–21). `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`, which skip a year only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24).\n- The full read of all 180 AmericanStories year files at revision `77e27fa6` (decision 25).\n- Crops, one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28).\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 42 s, 4.0 GB at peak). It produces the EDA, the candidates' composition, the lexicon's recall and eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30).\n\nMeasured:\n- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages, giving 1,050,459 candidates (2,837 per million) and 6,872,539 near-miss articles.\n- The read took 118.6 min for 340.4 GB, at 47.8 MB/s with four years at a time.\n- 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800. Reprints put 31.4% of candidates in 80,770 clusters, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories.\n- Lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the ghost reports, and at least 27%. That rests on 4 reports found among 38,900 non-candidates (decision 30).\n- The crop check passes 48 of 50 (86.5–98.9%). The display headline drops 7,509 lines at 158 of 158 precision on the judged sample (97.6–100%).\n- 32.0% of candidates have no batch path, and 92.4% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decision 29).\n\nGate:\n- All 180 years are done, and none failed. Six ran twice: 1872 and 1889 lost their streams, and kill test 1 cost 1881–1884 their first attempts (decision 25).\n- Disk: the outputs take 1.94 GB (`data/candidates` 1.3 GB, `data/samples` 565 MB, counts 956 KB, manifests 720 KB), and 39 GiB are free.\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the committed manifest.\n- Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md`, with Temporal UI screenshots from before and after (`kill-test-1-*.png`).\n- Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 is AmericanStories' stray box, recorded as a known limitation (decision 29), and #50 is a 1964 page with no loc.gov item.\n- The EM's spot check, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:\n  - every candidate's term is in its text\n  - none of the 10 non-candidates is a report\n  - 1 of the 20 candidates is a report, in line with 3.5%\n\nRisks and open questions:\n- **Lexicon v2 is the EM's call** (decision 30). Spiritualist terms would add about 161,000 candidates (+15%) and catch 3 of the 4 missed reports. Adding them takes a full re-read: 118.6 min and 340.4 GB.\n- The recall estimate rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Its screen would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports once their lexicon terms are masked.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle delusions, hallucinations, spirit control and a felt presence of the dead.\n- 25,595 candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\n\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old_next) == 1 and s.count(\"## STATUS: Phase 1\") == 1\ns = s.replace(old_next, new_next)\ns = s.replace(\"## STATUS: Phase 1\", block + \"## STATUS: Phase 1\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"^## \" Docs/RESUME.md","description":"Write the Phase 2A STATUS block into RESUME.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_read_input_tokens":362373,"output_tokens":3569,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1738},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3569,"cache_read_input_tokens":362373,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1326},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FHse65zdVht7CUgu7HJAZP":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && python3 - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/RESUME.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nold_next = \"\"\"## Next step\n\n**Phase 2A: the archive read and EDA** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #1 is merged.\n\"\"\"\nnew_next = \"\"\"## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #2 is merged. Lexicon v2 (decision 30) waits on the EM. If it is accepted, its re-read runs before anything is loaded into Atlas.\n\"\"\"\nblock = \"\"\"## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read and EDA (2026-10-30)\n\nBranch `phase-2a-archive`, PR #2.\n\nBuilt:\n- Lexicon v1, with OCR variants, and the near-miss lexicon (decisions 19–21). `IngestArchiveWorkflow` and `make ingest`, which skip a year only while every output's hash matches (decisions 22–24).\n- The full read of all 180 AmericanStories year files at revision `77e27fa6` (decision 25).\n- Crops, one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline without its masthead lines (decisions 26 and 28).\n- Eval A (`make eval`, 42 s, 4.0 GB at peak). It produces the EDA, the candidates' composition, the lexicon's recall and eight charts (decisions 27, 29 and 30).\n\nMeasured:\n- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages, giving 1,050,459 candidates (2,837 per million) and 6,872,539 near-miss articles.\n- The read took 118.6 min for 340.4 GB, at 47.8 MB/s with four years at a time.\n- 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800. Reprints put 31.4% of candidates in 80,770 clusters, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories.\n- Lexicon v1 finds about 49% of the ghost reports, and at least 27%. That rests on 4 reports found among 38,900 non-candidates (decision 30).\n- The crop check passes 48 of 50 (86.5–98.9%). The display headline drops 7,509 lines at 158 of 158 precision on the judged sample (97.6–100%).\n- 32.0% of candidates have no batch path, and 92.4% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decision 29).\n\nGate:\n- All 180 years are done, and none failed. Six ran twice: 1872 and 1889 lost their streams, and kill test 1 cost 1881–1884 their first attempts (decision 25).\n- Disk: the outputs take 1.94 GB (`data/candidates` 1.3 GB, `data/samples` 565 MB, counts 956 KB, manifests 720 KB), and 39 GiB are free.\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the committed manifest.\n- Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md`, with Temporal UI screenshots from before and after (`kill-test-1-*.png`).\n- Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 is AmericanStories' stray box, recorded as a known limitation (decision 29), and #50 is a 1964 page with no loc.gov item.\n- The EM's spot check, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:\n  - every candidate's term is in its text\n  - none of the 10 non-candidates is a report\n  - 1 of the 20 candidates is a report, in line with 3.5%\n\nRisks and open questions:\n- **Lexicon v2 is the EM's call** (decision 30). Spiritualist terms would add about 161,000 candidates (+15%) and catch 3 of the 4 missed reports. Adding them takes a full re-read: 118.6 min and 340.4 GB.\n- The recall estimate rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Its screen would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports once their lexicon terms are masked.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle delusions, hallucinations, spirit control and a felt presence of the dead.\n- 25,595 candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\n\n\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old_next) == 1 and s.count(\"## STATUS: Phase 1\") == 1\ns = s.replace(old_next, new_next)\ns = s.replace(\"## STATUS: Phase 1\", block + \"## STATUS: Phase 1\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngrep -n \"^## \" Docs/RESUME.md","description":"Write the Phase 2A STATUS block into RESUME.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"7f5a84df-bb22-4de7-b19a-6c13cb046632","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgYandTY12nq428ubJCwZ","requestRef":"a6de453d-a749-4e48-9749-a829ef207c68","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionSkill":"superpowers:dispatching-parallel-agents","attributionPlugin":"superpowers","type":"assistant","uuid":"8f32fbd9-ec5a-4d0d-ad76-e37f4d034606","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:31:51.276Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
