14:31:56.875Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-archive","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a593fc89-0285-4934-9591-3c606da2274e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"efbe7dae-4a3a-47ef-9f27-91c90fdaed9c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0144ACEiPYQ9xrDXKrVRREoi","type":"tool_result","content":"75:**16. The smoke activity resumes after its last heartbeat.**\n78:**17. The environment facts measure the download and the parse in one pass, in two processes.**\n81:**18. Crops use the scan's own pixels, and loc.gov names the batch when the record doesn't.**\n88:**19. Lexicon v1 counts the 1850s spirit noises as ghost terms, and reads through common OCR damage.**\n93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n221:**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about hal","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f233a81c-33e3-4668-a5fb-69710277a6d1","timestamp":"2026-10-30T14:31:57.579Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"75:**16. The smoke activity resumes after its last heartbeat.**\n78:**17. The environment facts measure the download and the parse in one pass, in two processes.**\n81:**18. Crops use the scan's own pixels, and loc.gov names the batch when the record doesn't.**\n88:**19. Lexicon v1 counts the 1850s spirit noises as ghost terms, and reads through common OCR damage.**\n93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n221:**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about hal","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"f6e09eb7-1b00-4aad-afa9-52f98bbab2c0","context":{"git_state":