{"parentUuid":"dfb9fb51-8735-4b85-a987-9ba7a9a950d0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYc5pAYxVPvZCWkkPU6r","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C2mbReqKyScysbUtRfBMU6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add paperghosts/ingest/lexicon.py tests/test_lexicon.py && git diff --cached > $S/staged.diff && python3 $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged.diff && echo \"machine name: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged.diff)\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nLexicon v2: the spiritualist words of the reports v1 missed\n\n- Four new ghost terms: spiritualism (spiritualist, spiritualistic),\n  seance, spirit_phrase (spirit world, control of spirits, disembodied,\n  spirits of the dead and more) and ouija (ouija, planchette).\n- spirit+medium, a term whose two words need only share the article,\n  as a medium's report spreads them out.\n- Each candidate's terms name the rules that matched it, so a rule can\n  be dropped later by filtering. v1's terms come first in the matcher,\n  so v2 only adds candidates.\n- The near-miss lexicon is unchanged. Its spiritualism and seance terms\n  now fire only inside candidates, which skip it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 | cat && uv run python -c \"from paperghosts.ingest.year import code_version; print('code_version', code_version())\"","description":"Scan and commit lexicon v2, and print the code version"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2747,"cache_read_input_tokens":444475,"output_tokens":827,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":91},"serve