s critically i'll, az his home, on Prince street. Mr.. William N McVeigb, of this city, is | quite sick in Richmond, where he is visit | ing Mr.. G. Powell Hill. Miss Anna Leadbeater has returned from a visit to Philadelphia. I Mrs. o. F. Carter has gone to Orange | n. j., to visit her mother. | Mr.. stephen Cowling, who has been under treatment in this city for some time, has | returned to his home, at Anandale. | William Motley, colored, was taken into custody yesterday afternoon by Officers Sherwood. Beach, .and Proctor, and is de | tanned at the police station for exa nina tion as to his mental condition. \n\n##### 4-025 | 1924-08-30 | The broad ax. [volume] (Salt Lake City, Utah) 1895-19?? | terms ['spirit_phrase', 'spiritualism']\nHEADLINE: \nballot is the. instrument placed i'll the hands Of American citizens with which to protect that rights. their lives, their property, real and personal. and with out the ballot we are helpless. There would Be more protection III our country and lynching would be sent direct to hades where il belonged if orr peopie could only vote down home and have all say in the making Of legislators. congressman and the like, then if we had some say about who shall be governor. Get the ballot i'll your hand and you have good weapon. Ii will do more good than a thousand automatics. take pleasure in saying this. But l have been knocking around Chicago a long time and when you read this letter | will be shaking some Of the Chicago dust off Of my feet and headed another way, and you can't stop me and there is no need OF you trying. There is no need Of you calling on dear spirit to stop me. Speaking Of Dear Spirit\" l find that they continue to manufacture damphules and it is being done right here in Chicago. A few days ago, c. L. Webb, that wonderful shorthand writer from Tuskegee, came and got me to take a ride with him, and you put it down that | accepted the inyitation. He toted me around by a tea room and we were invited to come back Sunday evening, and it was accepted. When it was made known, then Mrs. Evie L. Stewart, said she would like to 60, and this was followed by Mrs. Elizabeth Scott, and 10 and behold Mr. Webbs sister, who is the wife Of the tooth dentist doctor, DR.. Garnett, said she would like to 60, hence the party was formed, and we went at it, We did not all 60 together, for Mr.. Webb, his sister and two other ladies went out in their automobile car car riage and got Mrs. Stewart, and ! went for Mrs. Scott, and her husband was on hand and-he decided to 60 too. Believe me they had some fine sing ing, and when this was over, man with voice charming and sweet, made lecture on Spiritualism. He delivered a message from the people who lived in Mars. Neptune, and some other worlds. He said that they were in daily communication with them. They had visits from them. He told about their civilization, about their habits, their dress, and how near they were to God. ! just had to sit up and take notice. tell you honey, when you hear this kind Of stuff, it just makes you feel like saying-well / don't know what to call it, for think it is almost name less. 1t sounds like lot OF damphuleishness. but ! just listened. He told Of the wonderful things accomplished through his religion. He said that men were trying to do what they were doing daily, getting in touch with the people in Mars, and them other worlds 1t makes me want to say why in the hell\" don't they bring them down here and let Us see them. stood all this. and like in any 9TH er church, they took up a collection, although the speaker said that they did not ask anything from anybody. / put in the collection, and then an other collection was raised for charity. and ! put in that | said | was going to be dead game once. Next came the healing business. While the choir sang some selection, some women dressed in white, looked like they were robed for bed, walked in carrying a pitcher in one hand, towels and something else in the other. and took their places behind chairs, and the sick were asked to take seats in the chairs, and everybody were requested to hold up their right hand SO as to assist the healing spirit in doing his work. OF course T held ID my right hand with the rest. They went through some kind Of stuff, and then the persons would get Up and 60 about their business rejoicing. When this was all over, then the house was made dark, and We were told that we would get messages from the other world-not from he'll, for they said that there was no such place A. hell, but from the spirit land. All was still as a mouse, and in the room where was seated the chief woman, came a voice sound. She spoke UP and said that there was message for a woman had gone and","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5543ed49-0efd-4d25-a193-8e34ca518689","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":363,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dda99f0f-511c-4160-af52-361689f1374f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab6