ed in passing.\"),\n    \"4-003\": (False, \"1872, from a Vermont paper: an elder's daughter, a writing medium, prays to know spiritualism's parent and writes 'The Devil' in trance. A moral joke about the devil, not a sitting told as news.\"),\n    \"4-006\": (True, \"1873, Wilmington: an account of a spiritualists' excursion whose circle materialized spirits: a Quaker lady's dead brother, a young woman dead of consumption with two wreaths, and Owen Lovejoy among others. A seance told as having happened.\"),\n    \"4-018\": (False, \"1893: a squib about a spiritualist periodical claiming exclusive communications from Shakespeare's spirit. A joke, with no communication told.\"),\n    \"4-021\": (True, \"1869, Muskingum County, Ohio: a spiritualist family say the spirit world has told them each will inherit $50,000 from a Jersey City estate, and one has gone to claim it. A claimed spirit message, like eval A's 1878 medium.\"),\n    \"4-023\": (False, \"1897, Alexandria: a woman in a trance under a spiritualist doctor's hypnotism prophesies an eruption and a tidal wave. A trance prophecy, with no spirit of the dead.\"),\n    \"4-025\": (True, \"1924, Chicago, in a Salt Lake City paper: the writer goes to a spiritualist meeting where, in the dark, a voice sounds and the chief woman passes on a message from the spirit land. A seance told mockingly, but as having happened.\"),\n    \"4-028\": (False, \"1890: a news digest item. Spiritualists are arrested in Chicago for obtaining money under false pretences, with no seance or manifestation told.\"),\n    \"4-040\": (True, \"1859, Plymouth, Mass.: at a spiritualist convention its president says Washington's and Lafayette's spirits went through a Masonic rehearsal in his presence, and that a medium's warning saved Louis Napoleon from an assassin. Claimed manifestations, told in a news report.\"),\n    \"4-043\": (False, \"1908: the canonization of St. Seraphim and the Tsar's heir. Prayer to a saint, which is religious, with no spirit manifestation.\"),\n    \"4-047\": (False, \"1891, Economy, Pa.: a woman claiming to be a spiritualist preaches a hollow-earth doctrine to the Harmony Society. No spirit communication is told.\"),\n    # negatives the readers noted as near\n    \"1-024\": (False, \"1870: the Chinese Feast of the Dead, and the belief that spirits linger at graves. A custom, with no manifestation.\"),\n    \"1-026\": (False, \"1906: Scottish deathbed and burial customs, among them bread and water left for the departed's spirit. Folk belief in general, like decision 30's dead baby's spirit.\"),\n    \"1-040\": (False, \"1902: Maupassant's occult hobby is said to have driven him mad. No vision or manifestation is told.\"),\n    \"1-045\": (False, \"1922, New York: a spiritualist church's leader is tried over $500 of 'concentration' advice to win a husband. No spirit is claimed.\"),\n    \"3-007\": (False, \"1924, Birmingham: a puff for Houdini's lecture exposing fraud mediums, with no particular seance.\"),\n    \"3-035\": (False, \"1884, Savannah: a sorceress's love charm fails after she is paid to 'set the spirits to work'. A fraud suit, with no manifestation claimed.\"),\n    \"3-040\": (False, \"1904: a dispute over whether the Fox sisters died spiritualists, with no phenomena.\"),\n    \"3-049\": (True, \"Borderline. 1907, Winnemucca: an editorial on psychical research reports that members of the Society for Psychical Research claim the dead Professor Hodgson has communicated with them, as he promised. A claimed communication from a named dead person, told within a general essay.\"),\n}\nmine = {ids[k]: v for k, v in mine.items()}\nassert not set(mine) & sample\nitems = json.loads(added.read_text())\nassert all(i[\"ghost_report\"] is None for i in items) and len(items) == len(first)\nfor item in items:\n    a = item[\"article_id\"]\n    item[\"first\"], item[\"note\"] = first[a][:2]\n    item[\"rejudged\"] = \"full\" if a in mine else \"sample\" if a in sample else None\n    item[\"ghost_report\"], item[\"note\"] = mine.get(a, (False, item[\"note\"]))\n    assert item[\"first\"] == \"no\" or a in mine\nadded.write_text(json.dumps(items, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\nprint(sum(i[\"ghost_report\"] for i in items), \"reports;\", sum(i[\"rejudged\"] == \"full\" for i in items), \"read in full;\",\n      sum(i[\"rejudged\"] == \"sample\" for i in items), \"sample\", len(items))\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0bac3b10-c31d-4c83-bf0b-4a7230ca360f","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
