{"parentUuid":"205e534a-ad0a-4d62-88da-623a789664b8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4acd64b9-626e-4904-824b-5a9167cf4217","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F87qkCZ1zUCXRAciNVfAxB","type":"tool_result","content":"Docs/RESUME.md:9:**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #2 is merged. Lexicon v2 (decision 30) waits on the EM. If it is accepted, its re-read runs before anything is loaded into Atlas.\nDocs/RESUME.md:26:- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages, giving 1,050,459 candidates (2,837 per million) and 6,872,539 near-miss articles.\nDocs/RESUME.md:28:- 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800. Reprints put 31.4% of candidates in 80,770 clusters, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories.\nDocs/RESUME.md:45:- **Lexicon v2 is the EM's call** (decision 30). Spiritualist terms would add about 161,000 candidates (+15%) and catch 3 of the 4 missed reports. Adding them takes a full re-read: 118.6 min and 340.4 GB.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:71:- Prefilter recall: the random-sample bound and the near-miss pool. If misses are found, lexicon v2 and a re-run.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:121:- 370,313,913 articles gave 1,050,459 candidates. The outputs take 1.94 GB (candidates 1.34 GB, samples 0.59 GB), and the highest peak memory was 535 MB (1910).\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:160:  - 80,770 clusters hold 31.4% of candidates, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories. 71,191 of the clusters span more than one paper.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:181:  - The reader's job is 1,050,459 candidates, or 801,071 if it reads one printing per cluster.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:187:- No misses means no shared vocabulary to add, so there is no lexicon v2. A re-read would take 118.6 min and 340.4 GB of downloads at four processes (decision 25).\nARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4b9dea29-2841-4928-8a29-a3cf0ef12a05","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:06:59.688Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"Docs/RESUME.md:9:**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), once PR #2 is merged. Lexicon v2 (decision 30) waits on the EM. If it is accepted, its re-read runs before anything is loaded into Atlas.\nDocs/RESUME.md:26:- 370,313,913 articles in 16,887,460 pages, giving 1,050,459 candidates (2,837 per million) and 6,872,539 near-miss articles.\nDocs/RESUME.md:28:- 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports (1.7–7.0%), about 36,800. Reprints put 31.4% of candidates in 80,770 clusters, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories.\nDocs/RESUME.md:45:- **Lexicon v2 is the EM's call** (decision 30). Spiritualist terms would add about 161,000 candidates (+15%) and catch 3 of the 4 missed reports. Adding them takes a full re-read: 118.6 min and 340.4 GB.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:71:- Prefilter recall: the random-sample bound and the near-miss pool. If misses are found, lexicon v2 and a re-run.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:121:- 370,313,913 articles gave 1,050,459 candidates. The outputs take 1.94 GB (candidates 1.34 GB, samples 0.59 GB), and the highest peak memory was 535 MB (1910).\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:160:  - 80,770 clusters hold 31.4% of candidates, which leaves 801,071 distinct stories. 71,191 of the clusters span more than one paper.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:181:  - The reader's job is 1,050,459 candidates, or 801,071 if it reads one printing per cluster.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:187:- No misses means no shared vocabulary to add, so there is no lexicon v2. A re-read would take 118.6 min and 340.4 GB of downloads at four processes (decision 25).\nARCHITECTURE.md\nBRIEF.md\nBUILD-PLAN.md\nDECISIONS.md\nIDEAS.md\nPRD.md\nRESUME.md\nSRS.md\nUI-IDEAS.md","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"577aa087-79a8-4e78-9126-180343b8ca96","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/Hacktob