{"parentUuid":"da7a9bee-7683-4279-897d-d566065368c7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4acd64b9-626e-4904-824b-5a9167cf4217","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dk7am1xdWdoeWKmmASmymj","type":"tool_result","content":"eval/results/eval_a.json ['by_state', 'by_year', 'code_version', 'composition', 'generated_at', 'lengths', 'lexicon_version', 'no_state', 'ocr_quality', 'recall', 'reprints', 'terms', 'totals']\neval/results/eval_a_v2.json ['by_state', 'by_year', 'code_version', 'generated_at', 'lengths', 'lexicon_version', 'no_state', 'ocr_quality', 'reprints', 'terms', 'totals']\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:216:- These candidates sit on 19,115 reels. 92.4% of them are on a reel whose batch another candidate's batch path names, and the service is built from the batch, LCCN, reel, issue and sequence. That leaves 25,595 candidates on 1,292 reels needing a lookup: about 75 minutes at one lookup per reel.\nDocs/RESUME.md:31:- 32.0% of candidates have no batch path, and 92.4% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decision 29).\nDocs/RESUME.md:48:- 25,595 candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:90:  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:93:- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"9f0ca9c9-cc5e-40d8-95c1-3d3effa7db68","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:07:23.043Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"eval/results/eval_a.json ['by_state', 'by_year', 'code_version', 'composition', 'generated_at', 'lengths', 'lexicon_version', 'no_state', 'ocr_quality', 'recall', 'reprints', 'terms', 'totals']\neval/results/eval_a_v2.json ['by_state', 'by_year', 'code_version', 'generated_at', 'lengths', 'lexicon_version', 'no_state', 'ocr_quality', 'reprints', 'terms', 'totals']\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:216:- These candidates sit on 19,115 reels. 92.4% of them are on a reel whose batch another candidate's batch path names, and the service is built from the batch, LCCN, reel, issue and sequence. That leaves 25,595 candidates on 1,292 reels needing a lookup: about 75 minutes at one lookup per reel.\nDocs/RESUME.md:31:- 32.0% of candidates have no batch path, and 92.4% of those are on reels whose batch is known (decision 29).\nDocs/RESUME.md:48:- 25,595 candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:90:  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 310,000 candidates.\nDocs/BUILD-PLAN.md:93:- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 25,595 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"0d8baf2e-5bc5-4ed3-86d1-dcae458dd88c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":363,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Clau