`make test`: 176 passed. `make lint`: exit 0.","new_string":"- `7c928e8` decision 31, the STATUS block and the plan items\n- `f4c7600` each rule's marginal yield in `lexicon_v2.json`, test first\n- `c2813d8` the marginal yield in decision 31 and the STATUS block\n\n## Checks\n\n- `make test`: 177 passed. `make lint`: exit 0."}},"serverClassifierRequest":"f65b2927-4820-4926-9d4c-6e12241162fa","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgYoUbeR5X5NgUmRK2EEd","requestRef":"9cb9150c-1c9a-441d-8f62-1a8997414d4f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"73f4362e-dc09-42b9-ad30-44b1a162b065","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:17:57.934Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"73f4362e-dc09-42b9-ad30-44b1a162b065","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"53915d29-3b9f-4873-b1be-8f20126b960f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KzvnbMaCviDqwBjqV2yY3y","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/pr-body.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"a11d553d-078b-4335-b7aa-a38deb49b6fb","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:17:57.960Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/pr-body.md","oldString":"- `7c928e8` decision 31, the STATUS block and the plan items\n\n## Checks\n\n- `make test`: 176 passed. `make lint`: exit 0.","newString":"- `7c928e8` decision 31, the STATUS block and the plan items\n- `f4c7600` each rule's marginal yield in `lexicon_v2.json`, test first\n- `c2813d8` the marginal yield in decision 31 and the STATUS block\n\n## Checks\n\n- `make test`: 177 passed. `make lint`: exit 0.","originalFile":"Step 2A.8 (decision 31). Lexicon v2 adds five spiritualist rules to v1. Each candidate's `terms` records them by name: `spiritualism`, `seance`, `spirit_phrase`, `ouija` and `spirit+medium` (spirit and medium in one article).\n\n## The EM's conditions\n\n1. **v1 is kept.** Its candidates and samples were moved, not deleted, to `data/archive/lexicon-v1/`, with copies of its counts and manifests. `make eval-v1` reproduces `eval_a.json` and its charts byte for byte, apart from `generated_at`. No hand judgment was redone.\n2. **Each candidate records its rules.** So a rule can be dropped later by filtering on `terms`, with no re-read.\n3. **The re-read covered all 180 years at four processes.** It took 120.6 min for 340.4 GB, and every year finished at the first attempt.\n   - All 180 manifests share one code version, `2d6ff0faaf81`.\n   - v1 ⊆ v2: none of v1's 1,050,459 candidates is lost, and none of the 185,663 added holds a v1 term.\n   - 1850 reproduces. With its candidates moved aside, the rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the manifest's sha256.\n   - Disk: the archive and v2's outputs take 4.1 GB, within the 10 GB budget.\n4. **The new rules, measured on fresh data:** 200 added candidates drawn at random (seed \"eval A v2 added\"), judged with the 2A.7 protocol.\n   - **14 are reports: 7.0% (4.2–11.4%), so v2 gains about 13,000 reports (7,830–21,200).** 2 of them are borderline. Without those, 12 give 6.0% (3.5–10.2%).\n   - The 4 reading agents' first reading was 169 no, 21 close calls and 10 reports.\n   - I agreed with all 17 of the seeded negatives I re-judged blind.\n   - I read every close call and report in full. I also read in full the 8 negatives the agents' notes called near, which goes beyond the protocol. One of those is a report.\n\n   | Rule | Added | Added holding only it | In the 200 | Reports | Rate (95%) |\n   |---|---|---|---|---|---|\n   | spiritualism | 68,183 | 54,411 | 82 | 8 | 9.8% (5.0–18.1%) |\n   | seance | 30,466 | 21,656 | 38 | 4 | 10.5% (4.2–24.1%) |\n   | spirit_phrase | 35,695 | 24,537 | 37 | 4 | 10.8% (4.3–24.7%) |\n   | spirit+medium | 72,856 | 57,676 | 67 | 3 | 4.5% (1.5–12.4%) |\n   | **ouija** | 5,855 | 5,124 | 6 | **0** | 0% (0–39.0%) |\n\n   - **ouija is flagged:** no report in its 6. Dropping it is your call, and it takes 5,124 candidates away by filtering.\n   - A candidate can hold several rules, so the rows overlap.\n\n   **Marginal yield**, which you asked for after this opened. It counts the reports in the 200 that only one rule catches, so it is what dropping that rule alone loses. No rule was tuned or narrowed on the 200.\n\n   | Rule | Only it catches, of the 200 | Reports among the added | Its sampled articles holding only it | Their rate (95%) |\n   |---|---|---|---|---|\n   | spiritualism | 4: 2.0% (0.78–5.0%) | ~3,710 (1,450–9,340) | 64 | 6.3% (2.5–15.0%) of 54,411 |\n   | seance | 2: 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 (510–6,630) | 28 | 7.1% (2.0–22.6%) of 21,656 |\n   | spirit_phrase | 2: 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 (510–6,630) | 24 | 8.3% (2.3–25.9%) of 24,537 |\n   | spirit+medium | 2: 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 (510–6,630) | 57 | 3.5% (0.97–11.9%) of 57,676 |\n   | ouija | 0: 0% (0–1.9%) | at most 3,500 | 3 | 0% (0–56.2%) of 5,124 |\n\n   - Unlike in 2A.7's screen, spirit+medium alone catches 2 reports here: 1857 Middlebury and 1859 Plymouth.\n   - The 2 borderline reports are each caught by one rule. Without them, spirit_phrase alone catches 1 and spiritualism alone catches 3.\n5. **Recall, in-sample: 84%, and at least 48%.** v1's screen of 38,900 articles was read again with v2. v2 catches 3 of its 4 reports, and 1 in 38,883 is still missed, about 9,500 articles. v2's rules were chosen from those misses, so this figure is optimistic. 2C's eval B gives the independent one.\n6. **Eval A's EDA charts are regenerated on v2.** There are six, in `eval/results/eval_a_v2/`, and I rendered and checked each in light and dark.\n7. **Close-out:**\n   - decision 31\n   - the Phase 2A STATUS block in `RESUME.md`, with v2's numbers and the in-sample caveat\n   - v2's numbers in the 2B and 2C plan items: the reader's job grows to 1,236,122 candidates (+17.7%), and 27,817 candidates need loc.gov\n\n## Commits\n\n- `72ef622` lexicon v2 and its tests\n- `ca57e25` eval A on either lexicon, and `scripts/lexicon_v2.py`\n- `0101271` the counts and manifests of the re-read, v2's EDA, `lexicon_v2.json` and `added.json`\n- `7c928e8` decision 31, the STATUS block and the plan items\n\n## Checks\n\n- `make test`: 176 passed. `make lint`: exit 0.\n- Each commit's staged diff was scanned for `.env` values, with none found and no machine name.\n- No loc.gov requests, and nothing spent.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":51,"oldLines":10,"newStart":51,"newLines":12,"lines":[" - `ca57e25` eval A on either lexicon, and `scripts/lexicon_v2.py`"," - `0101271` the counts and manifests of the re-read, v2's EDA, `lexicon_v2.json` and `added.json`"," - `7c928e8` decision 31, the STATUS block and the plan items","+- `f4c7600` each rule's marginal yield in `lexicon_v2.json`, test first","+- `c2813d8` the marginal yield in decision 31 and the STATUS block"," "," ## Checks"," ","-- `make test`: 176 passed. `make lint`: exit 0.","+- `make test`: 177 passed. `make lint`: exit 0."," - Each commit's staged diff was scanned for `.env` values, with none found and no machine name."," - No loc.gov requests, and nothing spent."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"73f4362e-dc09-42b9-ad30-44b1a162b065","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
