{"parentUuid":"b57891d2-3845-4bae-8fad-2097c17ef09e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYoWmBh7Q1ENn4d8kWut","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2A.8 addendum: DONE. Each new rule's marginal yield is now in PR #3: https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts/pull/3, as commits `f4c7600` and `c2813d8`. That's the reports in the 200 that one rule catches and nothing else does, which is what dropping that rule alone would lose.\n\n| Rule | Reports only it catches | Implied among the added |\n|---|---|---|\n| spiritualism | 4 of 200, 2.0% (0.78–5.0%) | ~3,710 |\n| seance | 2, 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 |\n| spirit_phrase | 2, 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 |\n| spirit+medium | 2, 1.0% (0.27–3.6%) | ~1,860 |\n| ouija | 0, 0% (0–1.9%) | at most 3,500 |\n\n- **spirit+medium:** unlike in 2A.7's screen, it alone catches two reports here, the 1857 Middlebury and 1859 Plymouth ones. Its articles that hold no other rule are reports at 3.5%, v1's own rate.\n- **Borderline calls:** both are caught by a single rule. Without them, spirit_phrase alone catches 1 and spiritualism alone catches 3.\n- **Nothing else moved:** no rule was changed, and every other number in `lexicon_v2.json` is the same.\n\nTests (177) and lint pass. CI shows 1 check passing and 2 pending."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":209,"cache_read_input_tokens":344716,"output_tokens":519,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":209,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":519,"cache_read_input_tokens":344716,"cache_creation_input_tokens":209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":209},"type":"message"}],"speed":