hree Search indexes as static mappings in code. Run it twice, and show that the second run changes nothing. Never touch `sample_mflix` or any other database.\n5. The budget from real sizes:\n   - Build full `reports` documents for a seeded 1,000 of v2's candidates. Use real text and printings from their clusters, the embedding as BinData, and the reader's fields at realistic sizes.\n   - Measure their BSON bytes, and Atlas's own data and index sizes on a loaded probe. Remove every probe document and collection you created.\n   - Write `Docs/BUDGET.md`:\n     - the free space, with and without `sample_mflix`\n     - the bytes per report, with each rule-6 lever on and off\n     - how many reports fit with full text, at the top of decisions 30–31's intervals: about 95,000 printings, as stories by v1's printings-to-stories ratio, and in the worst case of one story per printing\n   - If they don't fit, list the options for the owner. Don't cut the text or the search to fit.\n\nGate: tests and lint pass; db-init runs twice cleanly; the BinData neighbours match numpy; BUDGET.md holds measured numbers. Keys stay in `.env`: never printed, logged or committed. Then report back, before 2B.2 (geocoder and LCCN parser).","hostInjected":true},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":32},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2a-lexicon-v2","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
