{"parentUuid":"f8212d58-ae18-4fe6-ba75-299552db916f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYp5By75DB9dej9WbFR1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Haeq8VB66jkvCNGCW3BjG6","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/.claude/worktrees/paperghosts-week4-kickoff-b83282/handoff/ATLAS-PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3281,"cache_read_input_tokens":346805,"output_tokens":264,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3281,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":264,"cache_read_input_tokens":346805,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3281,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3281},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Haeq8VB66jkvCNGCW3BjG6":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/.claude/worktrees/paperghosts-week4-kickoff-b83282/handoff/ATLAS-PLAN.md"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5021f933-6b51-4daf-9599-7fbd2024f1c3","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYp5B7kQHY3jqXC1YCqM","requestRef":"442745c4-2af0-48e3-b91f-30484fb4fe7a","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"71ec8f22-e368-4032-a35c-de9ecea46466","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:25:37.578Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"71ec8f22-e368-4032-a35c-de9ecea46466","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfc7125e-bacb-48e4-917e-c396bc7253de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Haeq8VB66jkvCNGCW3BjG6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Atlas plan for 2B and 2D (EM notes, 2026-10-30)\n2\t\n3\tThese notes feed the 2B and 2D prompts. They extend ARCHITECTURE.md section 4 and don't replace it.\n4\t\n5\t## Verified free-tier limits (MongoDB docs, checked 2026-10-30)\n6\t- **Storage:** 0.5 GB, a hard limit. It counts uncompressed BSON plus indexes, and `sample_mflix` already uses about 239 MB.\n7\t- **Search indexes:** 3 in total, Search and Vector Search combined. The plan uses exactly 3: Search on `reports`, Vector Search on `reports`, and autocomplete on `places`.\n8\t- **Throughput:** 100 operations per second, throttled above that.\n9\t- **Network:** 10 GB in and 10 GB out per rolling 7 days.\n10\t- **Other:** 500 collections, and a 32 MB limit on in-memory sorts.\n11\t\n12\t## Rules\n13\t1. **Atlas is the serving index, not the archive.** The 340 GB is streamed and never stored. Candidates, samples and reader labels stay in local per-year files. Atlas holds stories, places, cases and stats only.\n14\t2. **Partition the pipeline by year.** The year is the Temporal activity, the unit of retry and the cache key. The static export is partitioned by state and then town, plus one file per calendar day for \"Printed on this night\".\n15\t3. **One collection per entity, never one per year.** Per-year collections would multiply indexes, break the town drawer's queries across years, and can't all have Search indexes under the cap of 3.\n16\t4. **Category fields get no index of their own:** outcome, kind, place_type, precision, decade and state. Make them token or facet fields in the Search index and filter fields in the vector index. Precompute the reel's counts into `stats`. Use a partial index on `case_id` for the 30–60 investigated stories only.\n17\t5. **Atlas Search uses static mappings, not dynamic.** Map the fields that are searched and the fields that are filtered, and nothing else (no `printings` or quotes).\n18\t6. **Keep heavy fields small:**\n19\t   - Store embeddings as BinData vectors (float32 or int8), never as an array of doubles. A 384-dimension embedding takes about 4.8 KB as an array, 1.5 KB as float32 and 0.4 KB as int8. 2B must check that BinData ingestion works on the free tier.\n20\t   - Derive crop URLs from the scan location and box at read time instead of storing them.\n21\t   - Printings are compact references embedded in their story.\n22\t7. **Loading:**\n23\t   - one activity per year\n24\t   - `bulk_write` with `ReplaceOne(upsert=True)` on stable `_id`s, `ordered=False`, about 1,000 documents per batch, with retry on throttling\n25\t   - indexes built after the load, then wait until the Search and Vector indexes are queryable before running `db-verify`\n26\t8. **The budget comes from measurement.** 2B measures real bytes per story. The budget divided by that number says how many stories fit with full text. Use the free levers in rule 6 first; dropping `sample_mflix` is the owner's call. Never cut quality to fit. If full-text fuzzy search over every story still won't fit, take the options to the owner (for example the Flex tier, which costs money and needs their yes) rather than shrinking search to excerpts.\n27\t9. **To weigh in 2B and 2C:** cluster reprints before the reader, read one printing per cluster, and split gold, dev and train by cluster. The aim is less reader work and no leakage.\n28\t\n29\t## 2B carry-overs from 2A\n30\t- **Reel-to-batch map:** 32.0% of candidates (335,907) have no batch path, and 92.4% of those sit on reels whose batch other pages name. Validate the map by hiding the known batch and seeing how often it comes back, and flag reels that span batches. Resolve the remaining 25,595 through loc.gov (20 JSON requests a minute, cached), and only for those that become reports.\n31\t- **Missing state:** some papers have neither a state nor a place in their title (Daily Camera, Waterbury Democrat). Geocode through the LoC title record by LCCN, cached and throttled.\n32\t- **States are modern:** the metadata gives today's state, so 1835 Charlestown, Va. shows as West Virginia. The display copy needs \"now W.Va.\" handling.\n33\t- **Base rate (eval A, ba247a0):**\n34\t  - 7 of 200 uniform candidates are ghost reports: 3.5% (95% interval 1.7–7.0%). That's about 36,800 candidates (17,900–74,000).\n35\t  - Counting each printing as 1/k of a k-printing cluster gives about 22,300 stories. This is rough, because 3 of the 7 reports are reprinted. Size the Atlas budget for the upper end of the interval, not the point estimate.\n36\t  - Reprint clustering leaves 801,071 distinct stories from 1,050,459 candidates.\n37\t- **Reprint evaluation set:**\n38\t  - Sample per candidate as well as per cluster. Eval A drew clusters uniformly, so none of the 157 clusters of 50 or more printings was checked.\n39\t  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining.\n40\t- **Recall (2A.7, decision 30):**\n41\t  - 4 ghost reports turned up in 38,900 non-candidates, all of them spiritualist, so v1 finds about 49% of reports (at least 27%).\n42\t  - Lexicon v2 was approved on 2026-10-30 as 2A.8. It adds about 161,000 candidates (+15%), and in-sample about 18% of them are reports, so roughly 28,000 more report candidates.\n43\t  - Size the Atlas budget and the reader's job for v2, using 2A.8's held-out 200 rather than the in-sample figure.\n44\t- **v2 read (2A.8, checked by EM 2026-10-30):**\n45\t  - 1,236,122 candidates (+185,663, +17.7%). All 180 years ran on code 2d6ff0faaf81, which equals the hash of the committed 72ef622. Every v1 term's count is unchanged.\n46\t  - Each new rule's articles (all matches / matched by this rule alone): spirit+medium 79,374 / 57,676; spiritualism 74,516 / 54,411; spirit_phrase 42,186 / 24,537; seance 34,206 / 21,656; ouija 6,389 / 5,124.\n47\t  - EM's unofficial read of 24 v2-only candidates (seed \"EM spot-check 2A.8\", 11 years; not the formal held-out 200):\n48\t    - About 1 or 2 reports, both séance accounts from 1874.\n49\t    - spirit+medium: 0 of 6. The hits were \"circulating medium\", \"through the medium of\", and market reports where spirits means liquor and medium a grade.\n50\t    - 12% of the seance-only hits are French-language, where séance means a session (Louisiana council minutes).\n51\t  - Decide keep or drop per rule from the held-out 200's marginal yields. Narrowing a rule is a filter over the stored text and needs no re-read, but tune it on a fresh draw, never on the 200.\n52\t- **2A.8 held-out 200 (PR #3, decision 31; EM re-ran it byte-identical):**\n53\t  - 14 of 200 added candidates are reports: 7.0% (4.2–11.4%), about 13,000 (7,830–21,200).\n54\t  - Marginal reports per rule (caught by no other rule): spiritualism 4, seance 2, spirit_phrase 2, spirit+medium 2, ouija 0 of 6.\n55\t  - spirit+medium's articles that hold only it are reports at 3.5%, v1's own rate.\n56\t- **EM call (2026-10-30): keep all five rules.** Each of the other four catches reports no other rule does.\n57\t  - ouija costs 5,124 candidates, 0.4% of the reader's job. Its 0 of 6 rules nothing out (0–39%), so 2C's term strata measure it.\n58\t  - The reader handles precision; the rule tags allow a per-stratum threshold.\n59\t- **Atlas sizing for 2B:** the reports total about 36,800 + 13,000 ≈ 49,800 printings, or up to about 95,000 at the top of both intervals. Using v1's ratio of printings to stories (0.61, rough), that's about 58,000 stories at the upper end. Size for that.\n60\t\n61\t## Caching\n62\t- **Ingest:** the cache key is the pinned dataset revision `77e27fa`, plus the lexicon version and the code hash, with a sha256 check on each output. The tarballs are not cached.\n63\t- **2C:** cache every teacher and student call by a hash of the model, adapter, prompt version and input, so the ablations reuse the teacher labels.\n64\t- **3A:** keep a persistent cache of SerpApi, Wikipedia and Ultramarine responses keyed by request. It doubles as provenance (the retrieval date) and protects the 210 SerpApi searches.\n65\t- **Site:** static JSON, cached crops and cache headers (API-3).\n66\t"}]},"uuid":"444fbec9-73d0-484e-851c-57116c43461c","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:25:37.607Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/.claude/worktrees/paperghosts-week4-kickoff-b83282/handoff/ATLAS-PLAN.md","content":"# Atlas plan for 2B and 2D (EM notes, 2026-10-30)\n\nThese notes feed the 2B and 2D prompts. They extend ARCHITECTURE.md section 4 and don't replace it.\n\n## Verified free-tier limits (MongoDB docs, checked 2026-10-30)\n- **Storage:** 0.5 GB, a hard limit. It counts uncompressed BSON plus indexes, and `sample_mflix` already uses about 239 MB.\n- **Search indexes:** 3 in total, Search and Vector Search combined. The plan uses exactly 3: Search on `reports`, Vector Search on `reports`, and autocomplete on `places`.\n- **Throughput:** 100 operations per second, throttled above that.\n- **Network:** 10 GB in and 10 GB out per rolling 7 days.\n- **Other:** 500 collections, and a 32 MB limit on in-memory sorts.\n\n## Rules\n1. **Atlas is the serving index, not the archive.** The 340 GB is streamed and never stored. Candidates, samples and reader labels stay in local per-year files. Atlas holds stories, places, cases and stats only.\n2. **Partition the pipeline by year.** The year is the Temporal activity, the unit of retry and the cache key. The static export is partitioned by state and then town, plus one file per calendar day for \"Printed on this night\".\n3. **One collection per entity, never one per year.** Per-year collections would multiply indexes, break the town drawer's queries across years, and can't all have Search indexes under the cap of 3.\n4. **Category fields get no index of their own:** outcome, kind, place_type, precision, decade and state. Make them token or facet fields in the Search index and filter fields in the vector index. Precompute the reel's counts into `stats`. Use a partial index on `case_id` for the 30–60 investigated stories only.\n5. **Atlas Search uses static mappings, not dynamic.** Map the fields that are searched and the fields that are filtered, and nothing else (no `printings` or quotes).\n6. **Keep heavy fields small:**\n   - Store embeddings as BinData vectors (float32 or int8), never as an array of doubles. A 384-dimension embedding takes about 4.8 KB as an array, 1.5 KB as float32 and 0.4 KB as int8. 2B must check that BinData ingestion works on the free tier.\n   - Derive crop URLs from the scan location and box at read time instead of storing them.\n   - Printings are compact references embedded in their story.\n7. **Loading:**\n   - one activity per year\n   - `bulk_write` with `ReplaceOne(upsert=True)` on stable `_id`s, `ordered=False`, about 1,000 documents per batch, with retry on throttling\n   - indexes built after the load, then wait until the Search and Vector indexes are queryable before running `db-verify`\n8. **The budget comes from measurement.** 2B measures real bytes per story. The budget divided by that number says how many stories fit with full text. Use the free levers in rule 6 first; dropping `sample_mflix` is the owner's call. Never cut quality to fit. If full-text fuzzy search over every story still won't fit, take the options to the owner (for example the Flex tier, which costs money and needs their yes) rather than shrinking search to excerpts.\n9. **To weigh in 2B and 2C:** cluster reprints before the reader, read one printing per cluster, and split gold, dev and train by cluster. The aim is less reader work and no leakage.\n\n## 2B carry-overs from 2A\n- **Reel-to-batch map:** 32.0% of candidates (335,907) have no batch path, and 92.4% of those sit on reels whose batch other pages name. Validate the map by hiding the known batch and seeing how often it comes back, and flag reels that span batches. Resolve the remaining 25,595 through loc.gov (20 JSON requests a minute, cached), and only for those that become reports.\n- **Missing state:** some papers have neither a state nor a place in their title (Daily Camera, Waterbury Democrat). Geocode through the LoC title record by LCCN, cached and throttled.\n- **States are modern:** the metadata gives today's state, so 1835 Charlestown, Va. shows as West Virginia. The display copy needs \"now W.Va.\" handling.\n- **Base rate (eval A, ba247a0):**\n  - 7 of 200 uniform candidates are ghost reports: 3.5% (95% interval 1.7–7.0%). That's about 36,800 candidates (17,900–74,000).\n  - Counting each printing as 1/k of a k-printing cluster gives about 22,300 stories. This is rough, because 3 of the 7 reports are reprinted. Size the Atlas budget for the upper end of the interval, not the point estimate.\n  - Reprint clustering leaves 801,071 distinct stories from 1,050,459 candidates.\n- **Reprint evaluation set:**\n  - Sample per candidate as well as per cluster. Eval A drew clusters uniformly, so none of the 157 clusters of 50 or more printings was checked.\n  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining.\n- **Recall (2A.7, decision 30):**\n  - 4 ghost reports turned up in 38,900 non-candidates, all of them spiritualist, so v1 finds about 49% of reports (at least 27%).\n  - Lexicon v2 was approved on 2026-10-30 as 2A.8. It adds about 161,000 candidates (+15%), and in-sample about 18% of them are reports, so roughly 28,000 more report candidates.\n  - Size the Atlas budget and the reader's job for v2, using 2A.8's held-out 200 rather than the in-sample figure.\n- **v2 read (2A.8, checked by EM 2026-10-30):**\n  - 1,236,122 candidates (+185,663, +17.7%). All 180 years ran on code 2d6ff0faaf81, which equals the hash of the committed 72ef622. Every v1 term's count is unchanged.\n  - Each new rule's articles (all matches / matched by this rule alone): spirit+medium 79,374 / 57,676; spiritualism 74,516 / 54,411; spirit_phrase 42,186 / 24,537; seance 34,206 / 21,656; ouija 6,389 / 5,124.\n  - EM's unofficial read of 24 v2-only candidates (seed \"EM spot-check 2A.8\", 11 years; not the formal held-out 200):\n    - About 1 or 2 reports, both séance accounts from 1874.\n    - spirit+medium: 0 of 6. The hits were \"circulating medium\", \"through the medium of\", and market reports where spirits means liquor and medium a grade.\n    - 12% of the seance-only hits are French-language, where séance means a session (Louisiana council minutes).\n  - Decide keep or drop per rule from the held-out 200's marginal yields. Narrowing a rule is a filter over the stored text and needs no re-read, but tune it on a fresh draw, never on the 200.\n- **2A.8 held-out 200 (PR #3, decision 31; EM re-ran it byte-identical):**\n  - 14 of 200 added candidates are reports: 7.0% (4.2–11.4%), about 13,000 (7,830–21,200).\n  - Marginal reports per rule (caught by no other rule): spiritualism 4, seance 2, spirit_phrase 2, spirit+medium 2, ouija 0 of 6.\n  - spirit+medium's articles that hold only it are reports at 3.5%, v1's own rate.\n- **EM call (2026-10-30): keep all five rules.** Each of the other four catches reports no other rule does.\n  - ouija costs 5,124 candidates, 0.4% of the reader's job. Its 0 of 6 rules nothing out (0–39%), so 2C's term strata measure it.\n  - The reader handles precision; the rule tags allow a per-stratum threshold.\n- **Atlas sizing for 2B:** the reports total about 36,800 + 13,000 ≈ 49,800 printings, or up to about 95,000 at the top of both intervals. Using v1's ratio of printings to stories (0.61, rough), that's about 58,000 stories at the upper end. Size for that.\n\n## Caching\n- **Ingest:** the cache key is the pinned dataset revision `77e27fa`, plus the lexicon version and the code hash, with a sha256 check on each output. The tarballs are not cached.\n- **2C:** cache every teacher and student call by a hash of the model, adapter, prompt version and input, so the ablations reuse the teacher labels.\n- **3A:** keep a persistent cache of SerpApi, Wikipedia and Ultramarine responses keyed by request. It doubles as provenance (the retrieval date) and protects the 210 SerpApi searches.\n- **Site:** static JSON, cached crops and cache headers (API-3).\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"71ec8f22-e368-4032-a35c-de9ecea46466","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
