{"parentUuid":"0fc220d0-e00c-4fe7-94dc-ff167d3b00f5","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfc7125e-bacb-48e4-917e-c396bc7253de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014w9QUXkBSKySCawWpYPcaQ","type":"tool_result","content":"31:| RDR-1 | The gold set has 150–300 articles, stratified by decade and term. It is frozen and hashed before training, and the split is committed. | `eval/gold/split.json` and `eval/gold/HASH`, unchanged in git history after the freeze |\n32:| RDR-2 | The label schema covers: `kind` (report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other); place, people, seen and outcome (unexplained, explained, hoax, unknown); and, for walks, specific place, place type (house, church, cemetery, inn or hotel, road or bridge, public building, ship, other) and precision. Each value carries a verbatim quote. | Schema tests |\n87:| WEB-1 | The pages are: front page, town drawer, case, the reel, the method page, a 404 (\"This page was never filed.\"), and walks if they are built. | Playwright e2e |\n133:- **Dates** are ISO 8601. `month_day` is `MM-DD`, used by \"Printed on this night\".\n140:| `GET /api/places?q=&state=` | Matching towns: `{place_id, name, state, report_count, years}` |\n141:| `GET /api/towns/{place_id}` | The drawer: the place, its count line, and its reports `{id, date, paper, label, outcome, precision, location}` |\n143:| `GET /api/search?q=&state=&decade=&page=` | Text-search hits with a snippet, and the misread spellings each hit matched, e.g. `{scanned: \"appariiion\", term: \"apparition\"}` |\n147:| `GET /api/stats/reel` | Per-year and per-state series |\n148:| `GET /api/walks/{place_id}` | A walk (P2 only) |\n181:| B8 | Slices by decade | Language drift from 1774 to 1963 |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3b24380e-e8c3-4481-820c-7226e95c85fe","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:29:24.494Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"31:| RDR-1 | The gold set has 150–300 articles, stratified by decade and term. It is frozen and hashed before training, and the split is committed. | `eval/gold/split.json` and `eval/gold/HASH`, unchanged in git history after the freeze |\n32:| RDR-2 | The label schema covers: `kind` (report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other); place, people, seen and outcome (unexplained, explained, hoax, unknown); and, for walks, specific place, place type (house, church, cemetery, inn or hotel, road or bridge, public building, ship, other) and precision. Each value carries a verbatim quote. | Schema tests |\n87:| WEB-1 | The pages are: front page, town drawer, case, the reel, the method page, a 404 (\"This page was never filed.\"), and walks if they are built. | Playwright e2e |\n133:- **Dates** are ISO 8601. `month_day` is `MM-DD`, used by \"Printed on this night\".\n140:| `GET /api/places?q=&state=` | Matching towns: `{place_id, name, state, report_count, years}` |\n141:| `GET /api/towns/{place_id}` | The drawer: the place, its count line, and its reports `{id, date, paper, label, outcome, precision, location}` |\n143:| `GET /api/search?q=&state=&decade=&page=` | Text-search hits with a snippet, and the misread spellings each hit matched, e.g. `{scanned: \"appariiion\", term: \"apparition\"}` |\n147:| `GET /api/stats/reel` | Per-year and per-state series |\n148:| `GET /api/walks/{place_id}` | A walk (P2 only) |\n181:| B8 | Slices by decade | Language drift from 1774 to 1963 |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"65e0eb80-040b-4413-9b94-fa0295c22e86","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_re