{"parentUuid":"3b24380e-e8c3-4481-820c-7226e95c85fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYpN6kYpQsWcXbRxPLKR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CZTA2M2a4tN29gqKUQDWaR","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/SRS.md","offset":125,"limit":30},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9766,"cache_read_input_tokens":381613,"output_tokens":137,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9766,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":137,"cache_read_input_tokens":381613,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9766,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9766},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CZTA2M2a4tN29gqKUQDWaR":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/SRS.md","offset":125,"limit":30}},"serverClassifierRequest":"1912bbe2-6fdd-4f73-a95b-27a039737d78","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgYpN5hnWe71S9CmoTTBu","requestRef":"3fc7a0d4-a7b2-4782-b6e2-1f8ee041a9f8","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cb475ec7-2742-4411-bba9-82853ffa3cd3","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:29:27.616Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"cb475ec7-2742-4411-bba9-82853ffa3cd3","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfc7125e-bacb-48e4-917e-c396bc7253de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZTA2M2a4tN29gqKUQDWaR","type":"tool_result","content":"125\t\n126\t## 5. Data requirements\n127\t- **Schemas:** `ARCHITECTURE.md` section 4. Pydantic is the source; Atlas validators are generated from it.\n128\t- **Stable IDs:**\n129\t  - A report is `r_` plus its primary article ID.\n130\t  - A case is `c_` plus its report ID.\n131\t  - A place is its GeoNames ID.\n132\t- **Every derived record** carries the versions that made it (lexicon, prompt, model or adapter, code SHA).\n133\t- **Dates** are ISO 8601. `month_day` is `MM-DD`, used by \"Printed on this night\".\n134\t- **Text:** the OCR text is stored as printed and is never corrected in place. A cleaned transcription, if one is shown, is stored separately and labelled.\n135\t\n136\t## 6. API contract (read-only)\n137\t| Method and path | Returns |\n138\t|---|---|\n139\t| `GET /api/health` | `{ok, atlas, version}` |\n140\t| `GET /api/places?q=&state=` | Matching towns: `{place_id, name, state, report_count, years}` |\n141\t| `GET /api/towns/{place_id}` | The drawer: the place, its count line, and its reports `{id, date, paper, label, outcome, precision, location}` |\n142\t| `GET /api/reports/{id}` | The full case page payload: the report, plus its case if one exists |\n143\t| `GET /api/search?q=&state=&decade=&page=` | Text-search hits with a snippet, and the misread spellings each hit matched, e.g. `{scanned: \"appariiion\", term: \"apparition\"}` |\n144\t| `GET /api/near?lat=&lon=&km=` | Reports near a rounded point. The coordinates are never logged. |\n145\t| `GET /api/reports/{id}/similar?k=` | Vector-search neighbours |\n146\t| `GET /api/tonight?md=MM-DD` | Reports printed on that month and day |\n147\t| `GET /api/stats/reel` | Per-year and per-state series |\n148\t| `GET /api/walks/{place_id}` | A walk (P2 only) |\n149\t\n150\tErrors take the form `{\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}}`. The core path is mirrored as static JSON (`ARCHITECTURE.md` section 3.6), so the site works while the API sleeps.\n151\t\n152\t## 7. Evaluation specifications\n153\tResults are saved as JSON plus a chart under `eval/results/`, and each is produced by one command.\n154\t"}]},"uuid":"f6741066-36cd-4292-9085-86e6575add2b","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:29:27.640Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/SRS.md","content":"\n## 5. Data requirements\n- **Schemas:** `ARCHITECTURE.md` section 4. Pydantic is the source; Atlas validators are generated from it.\n- **Stable IDs:**\n  - A report is `r_` plus its primary article ID.\n  - A case is `c_` plus its report ID.\n  - A place is its GeoNames ID.\n- **Every derived record** carries the versions that made it (lexicon, prompt, model or adapter, code SHA).\n- **Dates** are ISO 8601. `month_day` is `MM-DD`, used by \"Printed on this night\".\n- **Text:** the OCR text is stored as printed and is never corrected in place. A cleaned transcription, if one is shown, is stored separately and labelled.\n\n## 6. API contract (read-only)\n| Method and path | Returns |\n|---|---|\n| `GET /api/health` | `{ok, atlas, version}` |\n| `GET /api/places?q=&state=` | Matching towns: `{place_id, name, state, report_count, years}` |\n| `GET /api/towns/{place_id}` | The drawer: the place, its count line, and its reports `{id, date, paper, label, outcome, precision, location}` |\n| `GET /api/reports/{id}` | The full case page payload: the report, plus its case if one exists |\n| `GET /api/search?q=&state=&decade=&page=` | Text-search hits with a snippet, and the misread spellings each hit matched, e.g. `{scanned: \"appariiion\", term: \"apparition\"}` |\n| `GET /api/near?lat=&lon=&km=` | Reports near a rounded point. The coordinates are never logged. |\n| `GET /api/reports/{id}/similar?k=` | Vector-search neighbours |\n| `GET /api/tonight?md=MM-DD` | Reports printed on that month and day |\n| `GET /api/stats/reel` | Per-year and per-state series |\n| `GET /api/walks/{place_id}` | A walk (P2 only) |\n\nErrors take the form `{\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}}`. The core path is mirrored as static JSON (`ARCHITECTURE.md` section 3.6), so the site works while the API sleeps.\n\n## 7. Evaluation specifications\nResults are saved as JSON plus a chart under `eval/results/`, and each is produced by one command.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":125,"totalLines":216}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb475ec7-2742-4411-bba9-82853ffa3cd3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
