/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"5ce90247-55c2-4021-862c-585d64218b82","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfc7125e-bacb-48e4-917e-c396bc7253de","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XPqt1vAFMNRKkcYbN3CGuN","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Atlas Search index size count toward M0 free tier storage limit mongot shared cluster\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Atlas Free Cluster Limits - Atlas - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/free-shared-limitations/\"},{\"title\":\"Atlas Search M0 (Free Cluster), M2, and M5 Limitations - MongoDB Atlas\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-search/limitations/\"},{\"title\":\"Atlas Service Limits - Atlas - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/atlas-limits/\"},{\"title\":\"FAQ: Storage - Atlas - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/faq/storage/\"},{\"title\":\"Pricing\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/pricing\"},{\"title\":\"Request limit in the free tier - MongoDB Atlas - MongoDB Community Hub\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/request-limit-in-the-free-tier/9804\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cloud - Atlas - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/google-gcp/\"},{\"title\":\"Free Your Genius With MongoDB Atlas Free Tier\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/blog/post/free-your-genius-on-mongodb-atlas-free-tier\"},{\"title\":\"Review MongoDB Search Metrics - Atlas - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/review-atlas-search-metrics/\"},{\"title\":\"MongoDB Search Compatibility & Limitations - MongoDB Search - MongoDB Docs\",\"url\":\"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-search/shared-tier-limitations/\"}]\n\nThe search didn't settle whether Atlas Search index size counts toward the M0 storage limit, and it didn't mention mongot on shared clusters at all.\n\n- **Storage limit:** The M0 (now called Free) storage cap is 0.5 GB. The main limits page defines the cap as covering uncompressed document bytes plus regular index bytes, and it doesn't mention search indexes. Free clusters limit the maximum total data storage space as follows: Free clusters: 0.5 GB\n- **Hard cap:** The storage FAQ says the M0 cap cannot be exceeded, and that upgrading to M10+ is the way to get more space. For Free clusters (formerly known as M0) and Flex clusters, the maximum storage is a hard limit and cannot be exceeded. You can add additional storage by upgrading to a dedicated cluster (M10+).\n- **How usage is measured:** Atlas calculates allocated storage from the dbStats command. Atlas calculates allocated storage using metrics returned by the dbStats command. Search index usage isn't obviously part of that, but the docs don't confirm it either way.\n- **Search metrics unavailable:** Search index size metrics don't exist for Free clusters. Free clusters (formerly known as M0) don't support these metrics.\n- **Index count limit:** Free clusters allow 3 search indexes, whether search or vector. You cannot create more than: 3 indexes (regardless of the type, search or vector) on Free clusters.\n- **Search nodes:** Free clusters don't support dedicated search nodes, which are the nodes that would run mongot separately. Atlas Free clusters don't support configuring dedicated analytics nodes, search nodes, or other workload-isolation nodes. You can configure dedicated nodes only on M10+ clusters.\n\nThe sources don't say how mongot's index files on a shared cluster are counted against the 0.5 GB cap. If you need a definitive answer, check the MongoDB Search docs for shared tiers or contact MongoDB support.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"51e8b680-5416-4000-bd69-b74b23077e4f","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:48:15.268Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Atlas Search index size count toward M0 free tier storage limit mongot shared cluster","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01EYK5im17KP7mytx8w4MVie","content":[{"title":"Atlas Free Cluster Limits - Atlas - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/free-shared-limitations/"},{"title":"Atlas Search M0 (Free Cluster), M2, and M5 Limitations - MongoDB Atlas","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-search/limitations/"},{"title":"Atlas Service Limits - Atlas - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/atlas-limits/"},{"title":"FAQ: Storage - Atlas - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/faq/storage/"},{"title":"Pricing","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/pricing"},{"title":"Request limit in the free tier - MongoDB Atlas - MongoDB Community Hub","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/community/forums/t/request-limit-in-the-free-tier/9804"},{"title":"Google Cloud - Atlas - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/reference/google-gcp/"},{"title":"Free Your Genius With MongoDB Atlas Free Tier","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/blog/post/free-your-genius-on-mongodb-atlas-free-tier"},{"title":"Review MongoDB Search Metrics - Atlas - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/review-atlas-search-metrics/"},{"title":"MongoDB Search Compatibility & Limitations - MongoDB Search - MongoDB Docs","url":"https://www.mongodb.com/docs/atlas/atlas-search/shared-tier-limitations/"}]},"The search didn't settle whether Atlas Search index size counts toward the M0 storage limit, and it didn't mention mongot on shared clusters at all.\n\n- **Storage limit:** The M0 (now called Free) storage cap is 0.5 GB. The main limits page defines the cap as covering uncompressed document bytes plus regular index bytes, and it doesn't mention search indexes. Free clusters limit the maximum total data storage space as follows: Free clusters: 0.5 GB\n- **Hard cap:** The storage FAQ says the M0 cap cannot be exceeded, and that upgrading to M10+ is the way to get more space. For Free clusters (formerly known as M0) and Flex clusters, the maximum storage is a hard limit and cannot be exceeded. You can add additional storage by upgrading to a dedicated cluster (M10+).\n- **How usage is measured:** Atlas calculates allocated storage from the dbStats command. Atlas calculates allocated storage using metrics returned by the dbStats command. Search index usage isn't obviously part of that, but the docs don't confirm it either way.\n- **Search metrics unavailable:** Search index size metrics don't exist for Free clusters. Free clusters (formerly known as M0) don't support these metrics.\n- **Index count limit:** Free clusters allow 3 search indexes, whether search or vector. You cannot create more than: 3 indexes (regardless of the type, search or vector) on Free clusters.\n- **Search nodes:** Free clusters don't support dedicated search nodes, which are the nodes that would run mongot separately. Atlas Free clusters don't support configuring dedicated analytics nodes, search nodes, or other workload-isolation nodes. You can configure dedicated nodes only on M10+ clusters.\n\nThe sources don't say how mongot's index files on a shared cluster are counted against the 0.5 GB cap. If you need a definitive answer, check the MongoDB Search docs for shared tiers or contact MongoDB support."],"durationSeconds":6.518458792001009,"searchCount":1},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5fc4b70f-1b38-4fa7-9441-fadfb216a5e4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":3,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":1},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghost