{"parentUuid":"c69cc6fa-3dc5-4483-a9a8-527415edf43d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYqvbuFHfAsQfktKKz8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the probe finishes, I'm writing the parts of decision 33 that don't depend on its numbers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":531695,"output_tokens":1585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":198},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1585,"cache_read_input_tokens":531695,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":699},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"1c5cd5a8-13ed-43ba-895d-cf8c2883d4b4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYqvaxhF7ELMuHiGq93d","requestRef":"678bb60d-bd07-456c-a10d-fb721f5adecd","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"0e37e7d0-f1f9-4163-abef-3c2fd41958da","timestamp":"2026-10-30T17:49:56.752Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"0e37e7d0-f1f9-4163-abef-3c2fd41958da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYqvbuFHfAsQfktKKz8V","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EBZreP372bowpxzk7Mxy22","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat >> Docs/DECISIONS.md <<'EOF'\n\n**33. The data layer is built: models, validators generated from them, BinData embeddings and `make db-init`. M0's third Search index waits on the owner.**\n- **Models** (`paperghosts/schemas`): `Report`, `Place`, `Case` and `Stat`, as ARCHITECTURE section 4 now gives them.\n  - **No nulls:** a document is stored without its empty fields.\n  - **IDs:** the model checks SRS section 5's, which a validator can't: a report is `r_` plus its primary article, and a case is `c_` plus its report.\n  - **`versions`:** every record carries the code's SHA and whichever lexicon, model, adapter and prompt made it. It replaces section 4's `reader`.\n  - **Embeddings:** an embedding must be a float32 or int8 BinData vector of 384 dimensions.\n  - **Scan pages:** a printing's edition and page are optional. In 1910, a third of candidates' scan records have neither, and half more give the page as \"na\".\n- **Validators** (`paperghosts/store/validators.py`): generated from the models.\n  - Atlas reads draft 4 with `bsonType`, so references are inlined, `const` becomes `enum`, integers become int or long, and a tuple becomes `items` with `additionalItems: false`.\n  - A keyword Atlas lacks raises an error.\n  - The collections validate strictly, with errors.\n  - **Tests:** 23 invalid documents cover required fields, enums, GeoJSON, an embedding stored as an array, and stored crop URLs. The model, an offline checker in the tests and Atlas itself each reject every one, Atlas with error 121 (the test marked `atlas`). The valid documents pass all three.\n- **BinData vectors work on M0** (`scripts/bindata_check.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/bindata_check.json`):\n  - The test set: 2,000 vectors of 384 dimensions, in 40 clusters, each stored as float32 and as int8, under one Vector Search index.\n  - **Exact search:** for both types, Atlas returns numpy's 10 nearest neighbours in the same order for all 20 queries. Its scores are within 1e-7 of (1 + cos)/2.\n  - **Approximate search:** recall is 1.0 at 200 candidates.\n  - **Sizes:** an embedding takes 4,898 BSON bytes as an array of doubles, 1,554 as float32 and 402 as int8.\n  - **Cleanup:** the index was queryable in 28 s. The scratch collection and its index were then removed.\n- **`make db-init`** (`paperghosts/store/db_init.py`):\n  - It builds the four collections, their validators, section 4's indexes and the three Search indexes, as static mappings in code.\n  - It touches only database `paperghosts`, and in it only the collections in the plan. Phase 1's `skeleton` is left as it is.\n  - A run updated the two validators that `Printing` changed. The run after it printed \"nothing to change\".\n- **The third Search index can't be created yet.**\n  - M0's cap of three counts every database in the cluster, and `sample_mflix.movies` holds a Search index named `default`. So `places_search` isn't created.\n  - `make db-init` names the index it couldn't create, and exits 1 instead of stopping halfway.\n  - Freeing the slot is the owner's call, as dropping `sample_mflix` is (decision 32, rule 8).\n  - The cluster also holds a database `cubby`, with one collection, which isn't this project's. Nothing here touches it.\nEOF\ntail -n 2 Docs/DECISIONS.md","description":"Append the first part of decision 33"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":699,"cache_read_input_tokens":531695,"output_tokens":1585,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":198},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0