{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"4a5dd16ed0380f36165281cb1f22ab7cb5cead3792cc8ed7aa50ebf8325e6c15","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Next, section 4's printing and reader-field bullets get the location fields and the two cross-field rules."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015NLKEKc9WUrGTEPjzGszi3","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","old_string":"- `printings[]`: compact references (decision 32, rule 6). Each has:\n  - article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state and date\n  - edition and page, when the scan record has them\n  - the page's IIIF `service`, once it is known\n  - `bbox_list`\n\n  Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own.","new_string":"- `printings[]`: compact references (decision 32, rule 6), built by `paperghosts/store/printings.py`. Each has:\n  - article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state and date\n  - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.\n  - page, from the scan record only, when it has one\n  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).\n  - `bbox_list`\n\n  Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HPd9WKp9JtQHhkvpFdgQt5","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","old_string":"- `date` (the earliest printing's), `year`, `month_day` and `decade`","new_string":"- `date` (the earliest printing's