{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"56845056-d2c3-4110-8395-4f0134fdc23a","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:01:47.843Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"a22c8545-8fff-4f7f-ad52-c76c4ea857b7","keep":471,"tail":["1dbe0e8d455f5f3811f108242ac56fc10628674f289907298fe985618dab1584","aaeadf8262cf81832ce04a76e2b00a510f0e64c475cda696115cd7398f43ae77"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",472,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"a01f2e803b5c6403f2ace285f981f05d7c374ff0f3044f674a8484c1b4641f69"}
{"parentUuid":"5e3767d0-aa3a-4cf0-8251-ce362e39a569","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYrqLtLfcs5Vq4ci4Zcg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013w4Cr4hmEZ1GQ2yLhN8XW6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\npath = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\")\ntext = path.read_text()\nreplacements = [\n    (\n        '''  - **Scan pages:** a printing's edition and page are optional. In 1910, a third of candidates' scan records have neither, and half more give the page as \"na\".\n''',\n        '''  - **Cross-field rules:** the model also checks three more.\n    - A stated value needs a quote that verified. Atlas's validator enforces this one too.\n    - A report's year, month_day and decade must be its date's.\n    - A printing's issue must be its date and its edition.\n- **Printings** (`paperghosts/store/printings.py`), checked over all 1,236,122 v2 candidates (the EM's review):\n  - **Location:** a printing is located by its member name, as `1910-04-12_p8_sn84022472_0029586686A_1910041201_0396.json` shows. That gives the date, a page token, the LCCN, the reel, the issue (the date and a two-digit edition) and the frame.\n    - Every member name parses, and every issue is its date and two digits.\n    - So edition, reel, issue and frame are required.\n  - **LCCN:** 10,871 records (0.88%) have none, and those take the member's. Every record that has one agrees with its member name.\n  - **Page:** the page comes from the scan record only, and it is a number in 19.9% of them. It's never taken from the member's page token, which matches the scan's page for only 28.5% of 1910's candidates (the EM's count).\n  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396.\n    - Example: the member `…_1910021001_0164` and the jp2 `sn82016187/100493962/1910021001/0163.jp2`.\n    - So a page located without a batch path can be the wrong one. Its crop waits for a check, whose error 2B's reel-map validation measures (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n''',\n    ),\n    (\n        \"  - **Tests:** 23 invalid documents cover required fields, enums, GeoJSON, an embedding stored as an array, and stored crop URLs.\",\n        \"  - **Tests:** 27 invalid documents cover required fields, enums, GeoJSON, a printing with no frame, a stated value with no verified quote, an embedding stored as an array, and stored crop URLs.\",\n    ),\n    (\n        '''  - A run updated the two validators that `Printing` changed. The run after it printed \"nothing to change\".\n''',\n        '''  - Each change to the models made one run update the validators it changed. The run after printed \"nothing to change\", which was true of the final model too.\n''',\n    ),\n    (\n        '''  - Freeing the slot is the owner's call, as dropping `sample_mflix` is (decision 32, rule 8).\n''',\n        '''  - Freeing the slot is the owner's call, as dropping `sample_mflix` is (decision 32, rule 8). The EM is taking it to the owner with the budget.\n  - `places_search` stays in the code, so db-init creates it once there's a slot. Until then, it's pending.\n''',\n    ),\n]\nfor old, new in replacements:\n    assert old in text, old[:60]\n    text = text.replace(old, new)\npath.write_text(text)\nprint(\"ok\")\nPY","description":"Revise decision 33 for the EM's fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1698,"cache_read_input_tokens":596955,"output_tokens":1268,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemer