{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"9390a1b78a385eda602a5c211d6911c172b4c0ce3a658f8a77dbfa999f5e8557","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The parts check is a tautology, because \"the rest\" is defined as whatever remains. It now checks that every part, the rest included, is positive, which would catch double counting."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CqmaqNCpE9hRUPVr38acwe","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/tests/test_budget_probe.py","old_string":"    assert sum(parts(doc).values()) == base","new_string":"    assert all(found > 0 for found in parts(doc).values())  # no part counted twice"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ft6D34TQ86GEdYbSBnU96K","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run pytest tests/test_budget_probe.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 1 && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && /usr/bin/time -l uv run python scripts/budget_probe.py > $S/budget-probe.log 2>&1; echo \"exit $?\" >> $S/budget-probe.log","description":"Retest, then run the full budget probe","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
