{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"0b31729d-0730-410d-9b7f-a80381e515b4","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:09:27.043Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"8a0585d5-b687-4210-91c0-0e6bedc867ee","keep":511,"tail":["c6c8190b55a660580bb279b7ce0397b3f2757df7d559b4ac6718f725f30dc34e","ce156667d6c9fe7b198271bb3cb1eaf758717ae425e84e81a34d0fe73d8e83bf"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",512,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"ac9c4445e5421d52661a9a208e612eca0fe38a66c34d7ed3767806ea9ee67d57"}
{"parentUuid":"33fa3cd2-fb94-41d2-a307-2ac2e026ba48","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYsRC7vzpyGFjuYEnu2x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2B.1: RUNNING. The branch is pushed, the budget probe is rerunning with your levers and the judged reports, and `BUDGET.md` follows.\n\n1. **Push:** you were right. I pushed before committing `1254820` and didn't push again. Now `git ls-remote` shows origin at `1254820`, the same as local. I'll check with `ls-remote` before saying \"pushed\" from now on.\n2. **Levers:** all measured offline with `bson.encode` on the final model:\n   - bytes by part: text, headlines, printings with `bbox_list` on its own, reader fields, the embedding, and the rest\n   - `bbox_list` packed as int16 and as int32 BinData\n   - paper, place and state moved to a title lookup by LCCN, with that lookup's own size\n   - `display_headline` derived at read time\n   - the embedding as int8 or float32\n3. **Judged reports:** 24 of the 25 are v2 candidates and get the same measurements, printings included. The 25th, the 1918 scout, isn't a candidate, so it would never be stored. The budget will use whichever of the two samples is larger.\n4. **Index sizes:** the probe's last run on `reports` gave unusable index sizes, because the collection kept index pages from an earlier run. This run measures on a fresh scratch collection with the same validator and indexes, then drops it.\n5. **What counts:** the docs define M0 storage as data size plus index size, as `dbStats` reports them. Search indexes aren't in `dbStats`, and Free clusters have no Search size metrics. The docs don't say outright whether they count, and I'll state it that way, with the sources.\n\nOn the final model, a sampled story averages 8,486 bytes, each printing 446 of them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":341,"c