el":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"71e984d1-e5ca-4a9e-b5e1-b67e3f2df9f1","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:19:07.864Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"file-history-delta","messageId":"66f6aac6-eb60-4519-9365-a57c3264fb1d","snapshotMessageId":"fa9e06ba-ee0e-47ae-b821-eb76f7248503","trackingPath":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.1.md","backup":{"backupFileName":null,"version":1,"backupTime":"2026-10-30T18:19:09.005Z","realParentDir":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e"},"timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:19:09.005Z"}
{"parentUuid":"66f6aac6-eb60-4519-9365-a57c3264fb1d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"73ffbdbe-91de-482a-8537-c4fc06ab0338","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTtA4JZVScigbhQ7aYKd3R","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.1.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"eeef773f-6ff5-4e17-b624-194ebb8c3a9a","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:19:09.012Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.1.md","content":"# Step 2B.1: DONE (`places_search` pending a Search slot)\n\nOn `phase-2b-data-layer`, from `main` at `718de62`. I checked origin with `git ls-remote`: it shows `f6de6bc`, the same as local.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `f304d71` | decision 31: you keep all five v2 rules |\n| `462e73b` | the models for the four collections, and their generated validators |\n| `2294853` | the BinData check on M0 |\n| `5eb0f7e` | `make db-init` |\n| `1254820` | your fixes: printing location, and the cross-field rules |\n| `0680870` | the budget probe, with `budget.json` |\n| `f6de6bc` | decisions 32 and 33, ARCHITECTURE section 4, `BUDGET.md`, the plan and the resume |\n\nNo PR yet. Phase 2B's PR comes at the end of 2B, unless you want one now.\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Tests and lint:** `make test` gives 237 passed, the live `atlas` test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- **db-init twice:** each change to the models made one run update the validators it changed, and the run after printed \"nothing to change\". The final model's last run also printed \"nothing to change\".\n  - `make db-init` exits 1 only to name `places.places_search` as not created. M0's cap of three Search indexes counts the whole cluster, and `sample_mflix.movies` holds one, named `default`.\n  - `places_search` stays in the code, pending. I didn't touch `sample_mflix`.\n- **BinData:** for both float32 and int8, at 384 dimensions, exact search returns numpy's 10 nearest neighbours in the same order for all 20 queries. Scores are within 1e-7, and approximate recall is 1.0. The scratch collection and its index are removed (`bindata_check.json`).\n- **BUDGET.md:** measured numbers only, from `budget.json`.\n- **State now:** database `paperghosts` holds `reports`, `places`, `cases` and `stats`, all empty, with strict validators, plus Phase 1's `skeleton`. No scratch collection is left.\n\n## Your fixes\n\n1. **Push:** done, and checked with `ls-remote`. The earlier \"pushed\" was wrong for `1254820`. I'd pushed before committing it.\n2. **Location from the member name:** checked over all 1,236,122 v2 candidates.\n   - Every member parses, and every issue is its date and two digits. So edition, reel, issue and frame are required, and the model checks the issue against the date and edition.\n   - The 10,871 records with no LCCN (0.88%) take the member's. Every record with one agrees with its member name.\n   - The page comes from the scan record only. In 1910, the article ID and the member name differ only in the page token (18,082 of 25,346). There the member gives an unconfirmed page number where the scan says \"na\" or nothing.\n   - `paperghosts/store/printings.py` builds a printing. The 2D loader will use the same code.\n3. **Frame hazard:** the service comes from the batch path only. Where a candidate has both, the member's frame is off in 20,643 of 841,054 (2.5%), and its reel in 396. Checking a page located without a batch path, and measuring that check's error, is now a 2B plan item.\n4. **Verified quotes:** a stated value needs a quote that verified. The model and Atlas's validator (`anyOf`/`not`) both enforce it, and Atlas rejects all 27 invalid test documents.\n5. **Dates:** the model checks year, month_day and decade against the date.\n6. **Search slot:** handled as you said (see the gate above).\n7. **Budget on the final model:** yes. A printing grew from 382 to 446 bytes on average, so I reran the probe.\n\n## Budget (BUDGET.md)\n\n- **What counts:** M0 counts data size plus B-tree index size from `dbStats`. Search indexes aren't in `dbStats`, and Free clusters have no Search size metrics, so by the docs they don't count. No page says so outright. Sources are linked in the doc.\n- **Free space:** planned against 500,000,000 bytes, 350.5 MB is free with `sample_mflix` and 499.4 MB without it. Atlas counts `sample_mflix` as 148.9 MB, not the 239 MB on disk.\n- **A story's size:** 6,199 bytes before its printings, from the 1,000; 454 per printing, from the reports; and 508 of indexes.\n- **The judged reports:** 24 of the 25 are v2 candidates. The 1918 scout isn't, so it's never stored. They are shorter than candidates in general (1,891 bytes of text against 2,555), and reprinted about as often (33% against 29%).\n- **Bytes by part, for the 1,000 (mean):**\n\n  | Part | Bytes |\n  |---|---|\n  | text | 2,555 |\n  | headlines | 102 |\n  | printings, apart from their boxes | 1,801 |\n  | boxes | 502 |\n  | reader fields | 1,335 |\n  | embedding | 1,554 |\n  | the rest | 637 |\n\n- **The levers, at the top of the range:**\n\n  | Lever | Saving |\n  |---|---|\n  | int16 boxes | 6.9 MB |\n  | title lookup (3,336 LCCNs, 0.35 MB) | 7.0 MB |\n  | derived headline | 3.1 MB |\n  | those three, together | 17.1 MB |\n  | int8 embedding | 66.5 MB |\n\n  - The largest box coordinate is 12,274, so int16 holds every box.\n- **Does it fit?** The top of the range is 95,203 printings.\n  - At v1's ratio (57,744 stories) it needs 430.5 MB as stored. That fits only without `sample_mflix`, or with every lever including int8 (346.9 MB, with 3.6 MB to spare).\n  - At one story per printing it needs 681.8 MB, and 552.9 MB in its smallest form, so M0 can't hold it.\n  - The point estimates (30,183 stories) need 225 MB, which fits either way.\n- **Owner options** (text and search stay whole):\n  1. Drop `sample_mflix`, which also frees the Search slot.\n  2. Take the lossless levers.\n  3. Size from the reader's real count in 2C, before 2D's load.\n  4. A paid tier, such as Flex or M10, which needs the owner's yes.\n\n## Measurement notes\n\n- **Index sizes:** `reports` kept its index pages after the first probe run, so the second run's index sizes on it were useless. The final run measures on a fresh scratch collection and drops it. `paperghosts` now counts 0.6 MB of those retained pages, which `BUDGET.md` notes.\n- **Secret scan:** on `0680870` it named `SENTRY_PROJECT`, but that was a false positive. The one match is the made-up adapter name `paperghosts-reader-lora-v1` in `budget_probe.py`, which shares the 12-character prefix `paperghosts-` with the public Sentry project slug. I checked this without printing the value. All the other commits' scans are clean, and the machine name appears 0 times.\n- **Data found by the model:**\n  - In 1910, a third of scan records have no edition or page, and half more give the page as \"na\".\n  - 0.88% of records have no LCCN, and 0.9% have no paper title. 2B.2's title records fill that in.\n\n## Plan items added\n\n- **2B:** check the page of a printing that has no batch path, and measure that check's error.\n- **2D:** check int8's neighbours against float32's on real embeddings, and note that `places_search` is pending.\n- **2C:** the gold set's term strata include ouija.\n\n## Also\n\n- The cluster holds a database `cubby`, which isn't ours. I read its size only and touched nothing.\n- `make eval`, the ingest and the Temporal workers weren't run in this step. No loc.gov requests, and nothing spent.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"66f6aac6-eb60-4519-9365-a57c3264fb1d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"c