{"parentUuid":"5eaf43df-7f85-44c2-8594-b89de6cdb6e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYtNPow2zDTH9qeJoef3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pjcbr6R7uDZ3oPLd7jfJvC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat .gitignore && sed -n 20,130p paperghosts/ingest/crops.py && grep -n \"^\\*\\*29\\.\" -A 12 Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -30","description":"Show the ignore rules, the loc.gov helper and decision 29"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_read_input_tokens":677717,"output_tokens":8968,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":8253},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":8968,"cache_read_input_tokens":677717,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1572},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Pjcbr6R7uDZ3oPLd7jfJvC":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat .gitignore && sed -n 20,130p paperghosts/ingest/crops.py && grep -n \"^\\*\\*29\\.\" -A 12 Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -30","description":"Show the ignore rules, the loc.gov helper and decision 29"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"5c39a514-aecc-415c-91c8-38a7105891ba","apiBlockIndex":4,"requestId":"req_011CgYtNNtcvAWxcH9xvbPo4","requestRef":"df32ca7c-ec42-4054-91d5-13a8690971a9","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"573aa3af-7384-4b19-9bfb-7aef44c9099b","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:23:20.745Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"573aa3af-7384-4b19-9bfb-7aef44c9099b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"fdb4383a-0e1d-45d1-a3f9-1b2691993af6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pjcbr6R7uDZ3oPLd7jfJvC","type":"tool_result","content":"# secrets\n.env\n.env.*\n!.env.example\n\n# planning notes that stay private\nDocs/IDEAS.md\n\n# environments and caches\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.pytest_cache/\nnode_modules/\n.DS_Store\n*.log\n\n# bulk data stays local; the small manifests and per-year counts are committed\ndata/*\n!data/manifests/\n!data/counts/\n    r\"_(?P<issue>\\d{10})_(?P<seq>\\d+)(?:\\.json)?$\"\n)\nCROPS = Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"data\" / \"crops\"\nUSER_AGENT = (\n    \"PaperGhosts/0.1 (a Hacktoberfest ghost-story map; github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts)\"\n)\nCLIENT = httpx.Client(timeout=60, follow_redirects=True)\nlast_request = 0.0  # monotonic time of the last request to the Library of Congress\nBUSY = {429, 500, 502, 503, 504}\n# seconds between requests: loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 a minute and blocks for an hour past\n# that, and its image services allow 150 a minute\nGAPS = {\"www.loc.gov\": 3.5}\n\n\ndef service_id(raw_data_loc: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from the batch path AmericanStories records for its scan.\"\"\"\n    path = BATCH_PATH.search(raw_data_loc)\n    if path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"raw_data_loc is not a Chronicling America batch path\")\n    awardee = path[\"batch\"].split(\"_\")[0]\n    return (\n        f\"service:ndnp:{awardee}:batch_{path['batch']}:data:\"\n        f\"{path['lccn']}:{path['reel']}:{path['issue']}:{path['seq']}\"\n    )\n\n\ndef crop_urls(service: str, boxes: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"One crop per box, in the scan's own pixels at half size, in bbox_list's order, which\n    is the order the article is read in. One crop over every box would take in the columns\n    between them.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        f\"{IIIF}/{service}/{b['x0']},{b['y0']},{b['x1'] - b['x0']},{b['y1'] - b['y0']}\"\n        \"/pct:50/0/default.jpg\"\n        for b in boxes\n    ]\n\n\ndef get(url, **params):\n    \"\"\"A GET to the Library of Congress: at most one a second, or one in 3.5 s to loc.gov's\n    JSON API, naming the project, and asked again after a pause while the server is busy.\n    tile.loc.gov can answer a crop it hasn't made yet with a 503.\"\"\"\n    global last_request\n    gap = GAPS.get(httpx.URL(url).host, 1.0)\n    for pause in (5, 20, None):\n        sleep(max(0.0, last_request + gap - monotonic()))\n        last_request = monotonic()\n        try:\n            response = CLIENT.get(\n                url, params=params, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT}\n            )\n        except httpx.TransportError:\n            if pause is None:\n                raise\n        else:\n            if response.status_code not in BUSY or pause is None:\n                response.raise_for_status()\n                return response\n        sleep(pause)\n\n\ndef page_service(member: str, scan: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from its batch path, or else from the loc.gov item that\n    lists the page, since some scans have no batch path (decision 18).\"\"\"\n    if scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n        return service_id(scan[\"raw_data_loc\"])\n    page = MEMBER.search(member)\n    if page is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"{member} is not a faro page name\")\n    url = f\"https://www.loc.gov/item/{page['lccn']}/{page['date']}/ed-{int(page['issue'][-2:])}/\"\n    try:\n        item = get(url, fo=\"json\").text\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404:\n            raise\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov has no item for {member}\") from exc\n    found = re.search(\n        rf\"service:ndnp:[a-z]+:batch_\\w+?:data:{page['lccn']}:{page['reel']}\"\n        rf\":{page['issue']}:{page['seq']}\",\n        item,\n    )\n    if found is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov lists no IIIF service for {member}\")\n    return found[0]\n\n\ndef batch(service: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The LoC batch that holds the page, from its IIIF service.\"\"\"\n    return re.search(r\":batch_(\\w+?):data:\", service)[1]\n\n\ndef crop(url: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The crop at url, from the cache, which is keyed by the URL, or fetched once into it.\"\"\"\n    path = CROPS / f\"{hashlib.sha256(url.encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}.jpg\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        response = get(url)\n        if not response.headers.get(\"content-type\", \"\").startswith(\"image/\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"tile.loc.gov sent no image for {url}\")\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        partial = path.with_name(f\"{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.partial\")\n        partial.write_bytes(response.content)\n        partial.replace(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef crops_for(member: str, scan: dict, boxes: list[dict], service: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service and its crops, one per box. A batch path can name a batch\n    that LoC has since reissued (ver01 where it now serves ver02), so when a crop from it is\n    missing, loc.gov names the page's current service.\"\"\"\n    service = service or page_service(member, scan)\n    try:\n        return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n211-- 335,907 candidates (32.0%) have a scan with no batch path, so the IIIF service for their page has to come from somewhere other than `raw_data_loc`. The count for each year is in `eval_a.json` (`by_year[].no_batch_path`). By decade, the share runs from 15% in the 1820s to 37% in the 1850s. It is between 24% and 37% in every decade from the 1840s on.\n212-- The fallback (decision 18) asks loc.gov for each page. In the crop check, it named the service for 12 of the 13 picks with no batch path. The 13th was the 1964 Arizona Tribune, which has no loc.gov item.\n213-- loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 requests a minute and blocks an address for an hour past that ([Working Within Limits](https://www.loc.gov/apis/json-and-yaml/working-within-limits/)). Its image services allow 150 a minute.\n214-  - A probe of 100 such pages, at one request a second, was answered 429 within its first minute, on 2026-10-30 at 04:03. Its script is deleted.\n215-  - `crops.get` now spaces loc.gov JSON requests 3.5 s apart. At that rate, a lookup for each of the 283,546 pages would take 11.5 days.\n216-- These candidates sit on 19,115 reels. 92.4% of them are on a reel whose batch another candidate's batch path names, and the service is built from the batch, LCCN, reel, issue and sequence. That leaves 25,595 candidates on 1,292 reels needing a lookup: about 75 minutes at one lookup per reel.\n217-  - 220 reels hold more than one batch. For 57 of them that's a batch and its reissue (decision 26). The other 163 are split between batches, so the reel alone doesn't settle which batch a page is in.\n218-  - A reel-to-batch map isn't built yet. It needs a crop check of its own.\n219-- **Known limitation, not fixed:** AmericanStories can give an article a box that belongs to the item above it. In the crop check, #21's first box is the last line of the letter above, its address and signature. The crop shows that line and the OCR doesn't.\n220-\n221-**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about half the reports, and lexicon v2 is proposed but not run.**\n222-- The draw (`make eval`, seed \"eval A screen\"):","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"15c612fa-ac0f-495c-8ede-84b2b5e6c3d0","timestamp":"2026-10-30T18:23:21.550Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# secrets\n.env\n.env.*\n!.env.example\n\n# planning notes that stay private\nDocs/IDEAS.md\n\n# environments and caches\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.pytest_cache/\nnode_modules/\n.DS_Store\n*.log\n\n# bulk data stays local; the small manifests and per-year counts are committed\ndata/*\n!data/manifests/\n!data/counts/\n    r\"_(?P<issue>\\d{10})_(?P<seq>\\d+)(?:\\.json)?$\"\n)\nCROPS = Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"data\" / \"crops\"\nUSER_AGENT = (\n    \"PaperGhosts/0.1 (a Hacktoberfest ghost-story map; github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts)\"\n)\nCLIENT = httpx.Client(timeout=60, follow_redirects=True)\nlast_request = 0.0  # monotonic time of the last request to the Library of Congress\nBUSY = {429, 500, 502, 503, 504}\n# seconds between requests: loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 a minute and blocks for an hour past\n# that, and its image services allow 150 a minute\nGAPS = {\"www.loc.gov\": 3.5}\n\n\ndef service_id(raw_data_loc: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from the batch path AmericanStories records for its scan.\"\"\"\n    path = BATCH_PATH.search(raw_data_loc)\n    if path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"raw_data_loc is not a Chronicling America batch path\")\n    awardee = path[\"batch\"].split(\"_\")[0]\n    return (\n        f\"service:ndnp:{awardee}:batch_{path['batch']}:data:\"\n        f\"{path['lccn']}:{path['reel']}:{path['issue']}:{path['seq']}\"\n    )\n\n\ndef crop_urls(service: str, boxes: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"One crop per box, in the scan's own pixels at half size, in bbox_list's order, which\n    is the order the article is read in. One crop over every box would take in the columns\n    between them.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        f\"{IIIF}/{service}/{b['x0']},{b['y0']},{b['x1'] - b['x0']},{b['y1'] - b['y0']}\"\n        \"/pct:50/0/default.jpg\"\n        for b in boxes\n    ]\n\n\ndef get(url, **params):\n    \"\"\"A GET to the Library of Congress: at most one a second, or one in 3.5 s to loc.gov's\n    JSON API, naming the project, and asked again after a pause while the server is busy.\n    tile.loc.gov can answer a crop it hasn't made yet with a 503.\"\"\"\n    global last_request\n    gap = GAPS.get(httpx.URL(url).host, 1.0)\n    for pause in (5, 20, None):\n        sleep(max(0.0, last_request + gap - monotonic()))\n        last_request = monotonic()\n        try:\n            response = CLIENT.get(\n                url, params=params, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT}\n            )\n        except httpx.TransportError:\n            if pause is None:\n                raise\n        else:\n            if response.status_code not in BUSY or pause is None:\n                response.raise_for_status()\n                return response\n        sleep(pause)\n\n\ndef page_service(member: str, scan: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from its batch path, or else from the loc.gov item that\n    lists the page, since some scans have no batch path (decision 18).\"\"\"\n    if scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n        return service_id(scan[\"raw_data_loc\"])\n    page = MEMBER.search(member)\n    if page is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"{member} is not a faro page name\")\n    url = f\"https://www.loc.gov/item/{page['lccn']}/{page['date']}/ed-{int(page['issue'][-2:])}/\"\n    try:\n        item = get(url, fo=\"json\").text\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404:\n            raise\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov has no item for {member}\") from exc\n    found = re.search(\n        rf\"service:ndnp:[a-z]+:batch_\\w+?:data:{page['lccn']}:{page['reel']}\"\n        rf\":{page['issue']}:{page['seq']}\",\n        item,\n    )\n    if found is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov lists no IIIF service for {member}\")\n    return found[0]\n\n\ndef batch(service: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The LoC batch that holds the page, from its IIIF service.\"\"\"\n    return re.search(r\":batch_(\\w+?):data:\", service)[1]\n\n\ndef crop(url: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The crop at url, from the cache, which is keyed by the URL, or fetched once into it.\"\"\"\n    path = CROPS / f\"{hashlib.sha256(url.encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}.jpg\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        response = get(url)\n        if not response.headers.get(\"content-type\", \"\").startswith(\"image/\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"tile.loc.gov sent no image for {url}\")\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        partial = path.with_name(f\"{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.partial\")\n        partial.write_bytes(response.content)\n        partial.replace(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef crops_for(member: str, scan: dict, boxes: list[dict], service: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service and its crops, one per box. A batch path can name a batch\n    that LoC has since reissued (ver01 where it now serves ver02), so when a crop from it is\n    missing, loc.gov names the page's current service.\"\"\"\n    service = service or page_service(member, scan)\n    try:\n        return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n211-- 335,907 candidates (32.0%) have a scan with no batch path, so the IIIF service for their page has to come from somewhere other than `raw_data_loc`. The count for each year is in `eval_a.json` (`by_year[].no_batch_path`). By decade, the share runs from 15% in the 1820s to 37% in the 1850s. It is between 24% and 37% in every decade from the 1840s on.\n212-- The fallback (decision 18) asks loc.gov for each page. In the crop check, it named the service for 12 of the 13 picks with no batch path. The 13th was the 1964 Arizona Tribune, which has no loc.gov item.\n213-- loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 requests a minute and blocks an address for an hour past that ([Working Within Limits](https://www.loc.gov/apis/json-and-yaml/working-within-limits/)). Its image services allow 150 a minute.\n214-  - A probe of 100 such pages, at one request a second, was answered 429 within its first minute, on 2026-10-30 at 04:03. Its script is deleted.\n215-  - `crops.get` now spaces loc.gov JSON requests 3.5 s apart. At that rate, a lookup for each of the 283,546 pages would take 11.5 days.\n216-- These candidates sit on 19,115 reels. 92.4% of them are on a reel whose batch another candidate's batch path names, and the service is built from the batch, LCCN, reel, issue and sequence. That leaves 25,595 candidates on 1,292 reels needing a lookup: about 75 minutes at one lookup per reel.\n217-  - 220 reels hold more than one batch. For 57 of them that's a batch and its reissue (decision 26). The other 163 are split between batches, so the reel alone doesn't settle which batch a page is in.\n218-  - A reel-to-batch map isn't built yet. It needs a crop check of its own.\n219-- **Known limitation, not fixed:** AmericanStories can give an article a box that belongs to the item above it. In the crop check, #21's first box is the last line of the letter above, its address and signature. The crop shows that line and the OCR doesn't.\n220-\n221-**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about half the reports, and lexicon v2 is proposed but not run.**\n222-- The draw (`make eval`, seed \"eval A screen\"):","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5c39a514-aecc-415c-91c8-38a7105891ba","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"573aa3af-7384-4b19-9bfb-7aef44c9099b","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"8141562deef2b2acaeae252664798b7174949ca5fdcf41c83bdb0dd03bc5e484","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Phase 2B.2 has six parts: a third budget scenario, the title parser, LoC title records, then-and-now states, the GeoNames geocoder and its accuracy. I'll start by reading the existing loc.gov helper and the ignore rules, since the title records and the GeoNames dump both build on them."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Re1HckrR3WGxuzozhxmD5d","name":"mcp__ccd_session__mark_chapter","input":{"title":"Phase 2B.2 titles and geocoder","summary":"Title parser, LoC title records, then-and-now states, the GeoNames geocoder and its accuracy"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01J8z88a5TpYFN9NviuB1yac","name":"mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan","input":{"items":[{"content":"Budget: stories per printing from judged reports","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Title parser, with 200 hand-checked titles","status":"pending"},{"content":"LoC title records for titles with no place","status":"pending"},{"content":"Then and now: printed beside modern state","status":"pending"},{"content":"GeoNames US dump, manifest and geocoder","status":"pending"},{"content":"Geocoder accuracy: 200 pairs and 24 reports","status":"pending"},{"content":"Decision, docs, commit, push, report","status":"pending"}],"scope":"continuation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pjcbr6R7uDZ3oPLd7jfJvC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && cat .gitignore && sed -n 20,130p paperghosts/ingest/crops.py && grep -n \"^\\*\\*29\\.\" -A 12 Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -30","description":"Show the ignore rules, the loc.gov helper and decision 29"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"5618e3aab46d2eea50c13ea5dcae42d099860942ce9d132ab9ddcfaadfc400a4","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Re1HckrR3WGxuzozhxmD5d","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Chapter marked: \"Phase 2B.2 titles and geocoder\". Continue your current work."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J8z88a5TpYFN9NviuB1yac","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan shown (7 steps)."}]},{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pjcbr6R7uDZ3oPLd7jfJvC","type":"tool_result","content":"# secrets\n.env\n.env.*\n!.env.example\n\n# planning notes that stay private\nDocs/IDEAS.md\n\n# environments and caches\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n.pytest_cache/\nnode_modules/\n.DS_Store\n*.log\n\n# bulk data stays local; the small manifests and per-year counts are committed\ndata/*\n!data/manifests/\n!data/counts/\n    r\"_(?P<issue>\\d{10})_(?P<seq>\\d+)(?:\\.json)?$\"\n)\nCROPS = Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"data\" / \"crops\"\nUSER_AGENT = (\n    \"PaperGhosts/0.1 (a Hacktoberfest ghost-story map; github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts)\"\n)\nCLIENT = httpx.Client(timeout=60, follow_redirects=True)\nlast_request = 0.0  # monotonic time of the last request to the Library of Congress\nBUSY = {429, 500, 502, 503, 504}\n# seconds between requests: loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 a minute and blocks for an hour past\n# that, and its image services allow 150 a minute\nGAPS = {\"www.loc.gov\": 3.5}\n\n\ndef service_id(raw_data_loc: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from the batch path AmericanStories records for its scan.\"\"\"\n    path = BATCH_PATH.search(raw_data_loc)\n    if path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"raw_data_loc is not a Chronicling America batch path\")\n    awardee = path[\"batch\"].split(\"_\")[0]\n    return (\n        f\"service:ndnp:{awardee}:batch_{path['batch']}:data:\"\n        f\"{path['lccn']}:{path['reel']}:{path['issue']}:{path['seq']}\"\n    )\n\n\ndef crop_urls(service: str, boxes: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"One crop per box, in the scan's own pixels at half size, in bbox_list's order, which\n    is the order the article is read in. One crop over every box would take in the columns\n    between them.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        f\"{IIIF}/{service}/{b['x0']},{b['y0']},{b['x1'] - b['x0']},{b['y1'] - b['y0']}\"\n        \"/pct:50/0/default.jpg\"\n        for b in boxes\n    ]\n\n\ndef get(url, **params):\n    \"\"\"A GET to the Library of Congress: at most one a second, or one in 3.5 s to loc.gov's\n    JSON API, naming the project, and asked again after a pause while the server is busy.\n    tile.loc.gov can answer a crop it hasn't made yet with a 503.\"\"\"\n    global last_request\n    gap = GAPS.get(httpx.URL(url).host, 1.0)\n    for pause in (5, 20, None):\n        sleep(max(0.0, last_request + gap - monotonic()))\n        last_request = monotonic()\n        try:\n            response = CLIENT.get(\n                url, params=params, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT}\n            )\n        except httpx.TransportError:\n            if pause is None:\n                raise\n        else:\n            if response.status_code not in BUSY or pause is None:\n                response.raise_for_status()\n                return response\n        sleep(pause)\n\n\ndef page_service(member: str, scan: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from its batch path, or else from the loc.gov item that\n    lists the page, since some scans have no batch path (decision 18).\"\"\"\n    if scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n        return service_id(scan[\"raw_data_loc\"])\n    page = MEMBER.search(member)\n    if page is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"{member} is not a faro page name\")\n    url = f\"https://www.loc.gov/item/{page['lccn']}/{page['date']}/ed-{int(page['issue'][-2:])}/\"\n    try:\n        item = get(url, fo=\"json\").text\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404:\n            raise\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov has no item for {member}\") from exc\n    found = re.search(\n        rf\"service:ndnp:[a-z]+:batch_\\w+?:data:{page['lccn']}:{page['reel']}\"\n        rf\":{page['issue']}:{page['seq']}\",\n        item,\n    )\n    if found is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov lists no IIIF service for {member}\")\n    return found[0]\n\n\ndef batch(service: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The LoC batch that holds the page, from its IIIF service.\"\"\"\n    return re.search(r\":batch_(\\w+?):data:\", service)[1]\n\n\ndef crop(url: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The crop at url, from the cache, which is keyed by the URL, or fetched once into it.\"\"\"\n    path = CROPS / f\"{hashlib.sha256(url.encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}.jpg\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        response = get(url)\n        if not response.headers.get(\"content-type\", \"\").startswith(\"image/\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"tile.loc.gov sent no image for {url}\")\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        partial = path.with_name(f\"{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.partial\")\n        partial.write_bytes(response.content)\n        partial.replace(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef crops_for(member: str, scan: dict, boxes: list[dict], service: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service and its crops, one per box. A batch path can name a batch\n    that LoC has since reissued (ver01 where it now serves ver02), so when a crop from it is\n    missing, loc.gov names the page's current service.\"\"\"\n    service = service or page_service(member, scan)\n    try:\n        return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n211-- 335,907 candidates (32.0%) have a scan with no batch path, so the IIIF service for their page has to come from somewhere other than `raw_data_loc`. The count for each year is in `eval_a.json` (`by_year[].no_batch_path`). By decade, the share runs from 15% in the 1820s to 37% in the 1850s. It is between 24% and 37% in every decade from the 1840s on.\n212-- The fallback (decision 18) asks loc.gov for each page. In the crop check, it named the service for 12 of the 13 picks with no batch path. The 13th was the 1964 Arizona Tribune, which has no loc.gov item.\n213-- loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 requests a minute and blocks an address for an hour past that ([Working Within Limits](https://www.loc.gov/apis/json-and-yaml/working-within-limits/)). Its image services allow 150 a minute.\n214-  - A probe of 100 such pages, at one request a second, was answered 429 within its first minute, on 2026-10-30 at 04:03. Its script is deleted.\n215-  - `crops.get` now spaces loc.gov JSON requests 3.5 s apart. At that rate, a lookup for each of the 283,546 pages would take 11.5 days.\n216-- These candidates sit on 19,115 reels. 92.4% of them are on a reel whose batch another candidate's batch path names, and the service is built from the batch, LCCN, reel, issue and sequence. That leaves 25,595 candidates on 1,292 reels needing a lookup: about 75 minutes at one lookup per reel.\n217-  - 220 reels hold more than one batch. For 57 of them that's a batch and its reissue (decision 26). The other 163 are split between batches, so the reel alone doesn't settle which batch a page is in.\n218-  - A reel-to-batch map isn't built yet. It needs a crop check of its own.\n219-- **Known limitation, not fixed:** AmericanStories can give an article a box that belongs to the item above it. In the crop check, #21's first box is the last line of the letter above, its address and signature. The crop shows that line and the OCR doesn't.\n220-\n221-**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about half the reports, and lexicon v2 is proposed but not run.**\n222-- The draw (`make eval`, seed \"eval A screen\"):","is_error":false}]}}
