een Charles Foster. the spiritual medium. and tho\nEVAL A 6_1904-05-28_p1_sn84020358_00271744432_1904052801_1153.json 1904-05-28 The daily morning journal and courier. Connecticut\n   note: a defendant in court points at a spectre, which the paper calls imaginary\n   context: 7.-Choking and gasp ing, and with eyes rolling. John Mahn- ken, accused of fraudulentIy Identify ing the body of Mrs. Frank R. Green wald, an Iroquois fire victim, in order to steal her money. suddenly jumped to his feet in Judge lClifford's court room to-day and pointed frantlcally at an imaginary spectre which he thought stood confronting him. While the spec tators looked ,on in terror the man frothed at the lips and waved his arms wildly. He was overpowered and thrown to the floor. where it took half a dozen police officers to hold him. Paroxysm after paroxysm shook him, and he had to be ma\nEVAL A 1_1911-07-27_pna_sn92053934_00202198326_1911072701_0413.json 1911-07-27 Rock Island Argus. (Rock Island, Ill.) 1893-1920 Illinois\n   note: Anne Boleyn's headless coach at Blickling, on the anniversary of her execution\n   context: Ghost. Without Heads. Speaking Of ghosts. the London Chronicle Says that \"headless coaches\" are fairly numerous in England. The most famous is the one that drives once a year. on the anniversary Of Anne Roieyn's execution. up the ave nue. at Blickling. her Norfolk home The coachman and the four horses have not a head between them. and Anne's own is not upon her shoulders. but she holds it in her lap as she sits in the coach all in white At the hall door the whole appArition vanishes. Anne's father. Sir Thomas. also rides in coach drawn by headless horses once year. and his ride is much more\nEVAL A 6_1911-12-15_pna_sn86058226_00271744924_1911121501_0691.json 1911-12-15 The Richmond palladium and sun-telegram. [volume] (Richmond, Ind.) 1907-1939 Indiana\n   note: lights moving in a cemetery, followed by a party that set out to investigate\n   context: GHOSTS! POSSIBLY: LIGHTS IN CEMETERY SILVER LAKE, Ind, Dec. 10 Mysterious lights have been seen NOV ing about the cemetery for several nights. The lights were first seen ear ly in the evening and were noticed fit ting from place to place as the night advanced. Thinking there was some mischief afoot a party was formed to investigate. AS they came into the cemetery the lights were seen to move ahead of them, keeping always dis lance of several rods away. Nothing lights. yet all saw them plainly. Whether it is the old \"will-o'-the- wisp\" or some peculiar atmospheric phenomenon Is puzzling the l\nEVAL A 14_1916-12-09_p5_sn84024055_00280761072_1916120901_0525.json 1916-12-09 The broad ax. None\n   note: the American legation in Peking haunted by the shade of an officer killed in the Boxer massacres\n   context: CHINESE HAVE PLAN TO RID HOUSE OF GHOSTS Urge Novel Method Of Taking Haunt From American Legation. Washington.-A legend has gone around Peking that the American le- cation Is haunted; that the shade Of an officer who lost his life during the Boxer massacres Of white men In 1900 is In the habit Of occasionally visiting his old quarters In the legation, greatly to the discomfort Of the occupants. This aroused considerable interest among the Chinese In Peking. Their own spooks, being daily or rather night \" companions, do not excite much at tention. But a foreign ghost is quite a new thing\nSCREEN 3_1856-10-29_pna_sn85026466_0020219798A_1856102901_1069.json 1856-10-29 Grand River times. [volume] (Grand Haven, Mich.) 1851-18??\n   note: 1856, Bordentown: spiritualists marry a dead man's corpse to his fiancée, on directions they say his spirit gave. A claimed communication from the dead, like eval A's 1878 medium.\nSCREEN 8_1898-01-20_pNone_sn84029386_00295871477_1898012001_0669.json 1898-01-20 Abilene weekly reflector.\n   note: Borderline. 1898: a wife murderer's defence is to be that he was under the control of spirits, with spiritualist mediums to testify. Counted like eval A's 1904 courtroom spectre.\nSCREEN 9_1918-04-21_p1_sn83030214_00206532257_1918042102_0461.json 1918-04-21 New-York tribune. [volume] (New York [N.Y.]) 1866-1924\n   note: Borderline. 1918: an Australian scout writes that he has felt a touch on the shoulder with no one by, and thinks the spirits of the unburied dead in No Man's Land hover near.\nSCREEN 11_1919-11-15_p22_sn83030214_00206532452_1919111501_0468.json 1919-11-15 New-York tribune.\n   note: 1919: Mrs. Curran says the spirit Patience speaks through her as a medium, and gives verses at a sitting.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"8da343e0-32b7-4262-9cc1-3fee2487e949","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":2,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":6},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8d7630d8-2333-4f17-9edc-e1fb25011a51","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
