{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"9f7fedc0734044d1846eb82b9a46030770e475a6e5002e60607c75f36aad9262","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Confirmed both cases: #61 shows Bloomington as Muscatine's old name, and #126 reveals the parser mishandles a bracket that starts with a state—it treats it as a place and misses the nested `i.e.`, when it should only supply a state. I'll write a test against this real title first.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NT1zFqPQzWSrPkEW6FqzRt","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/tests/test_titles.py","old_string":"        (\"Boise news. (Bannock City, I.T. [Idaho City, Idaho]) 1863-1864\",\n         {\"place\": \"Bannock City\", \"state\": \"I.T.\", \"supplied_place\": \"Idaho City\", \"supplied_state\": \"Idaho\"}),","new_string":"        (\"Boise news. (Bannock City, I.T. [Idaho City, Idaho]) 1863-1864\",\n         {\"place\": \"Bannock City\", \"state\": \"I.T.\", \"supplied_place\": \"Idaho City\", \"supplied_state\": \"Idaho\"}),\n        # a bracket after the state that starts with a state supplies only a state, with i.e. inside\n        (\"The Hot Springs star. (Hot Spings [Hot Springs], Dakota [Dakota Territory, i.e. S.D.]) 1886-189?\",\n         {\"place\": \"Hot Spings\", \"state\": \"Dakota\", \"supplied_place\": \"Hot Springs\", \"supplied_state\": \"S.D.\"}),"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CNAUtVJ1jDHpvRXMQZV4CF","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run pytest tests/test_titles.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 3","description":"Run the title tests to see the new case fail"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
