{"parentUuid":"00aba069-f204-478c-a7a3-77d738e50acc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c21d421-8439-4ef3-a792-2ee8b64888f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QuWfe8gWs1uf83HUFA2qxK","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\nindex 6d4add1..e4c1030 100644\n--- a/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\n+++ b/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\n@@ -107,7 +107,12 @@ Temporal runs only on the owner's machine, through the CLI dev server. The live\n - **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n \n ### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n-- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n+- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source.\n+- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n+  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n+  - what the cataloguer supplied\n+  - its state today\n+  The site shows a state that has changed beside the printed one: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n - Printings of the same story are grouped. Counts on the site say which they count: stories or printings.\n - Stories get one embedding each, from the earliest legible printing.\n - The loader upserts by stable IDs, so re-running it is safe.\ndiff --git a/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md b/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\nindex 5ba3579..f6cb886 100644\n--- a/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\n+++ b/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\n@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ How the build runs: five phases, each split into milestones, each milestone with\n    - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n    - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found.\n    - And decision 31's two borderline kinds: a claim inside a narrative whose truth is doubtful, and a particular claim told inside a general essay. It confirms or overrules counting a first-person claim of communication with a named dead person, made in a lecture or an interview.\n+   - The reader's place field takes the story's state wherever it's printed. In decision 34's look at the 24 judged reports, only 3 gave a town and a state together, and 9 gave a town alone.\n 2. Build the labelling page.\n 3. Label the gold set before seeing any model output.\n 4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing.\n@@ -135,6 +136,13 @@ How the build runs: five phases, each split into milestones, each milestone with\n - Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\n   - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.\n   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.\n+  - Measure the geocoder's fixes on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200:\n+    - GeoNames' \"(historical)\" places outside class P\n+    - the first of two towns joined by \"and\"\n+    - a rule for big cities' datelines\n+    - the paper's own state, for local stories only\n+    - GeoNames' own dumps for Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands\n+  - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever.\n - `make db-verify` runs geo, fuzzy and vector queries and checks their expected results and latencies.\n - The top-case rule, and the follow-up harvest as a second Temporal pass.\n \ndiff --git a/Docs/RESUME.md b/Docs/RESUME.md\nindex c744f54..3a17723 100644\n--- a/Docs/RESUME.md\n+++ b/Docs/RESUME.md\n@@ -7,10 +7,11 @@ Hard date: the site must be live on Oct 31.\n ## Next step\n \n **Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), on branch `phase-2b-data-layer`.\n-- **Step 2B.1 is built**, and waits on the EM's review (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n+- **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n   - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.\n   - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.\n-- **Step 2B.2,** the geocoder and LCCN parser, follows the review.\n+- **Step 2B.2 is built**, and waits on the EM's review (decision 34): the title parser, the loc.gov title records, the title lookup and the GeoNames geocoder.\n+- **Step 2B.3,** the reel-to-batch map and the page check, follows.\n - Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31).\n \n Needs the owner's yes when we get there:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51b513b9-506c-4ae2-a481-8479c6bc726d","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:21:27.776Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --git a/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\nindex 6d4add1..e4c1030 100644\n--- a/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\n+++ b/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\n@@ -107,7 +107,12 @@ Temporal runs only on the owner's machine, through the CLI dev server. The live\n - **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n \n ### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n-- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n+- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source.\n+- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n+  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n+  - what the cataloguer supplied\n+  - its state today\n+  The site shows a state that has changed beside the printed one: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n - Printings of the same story are grouped. Counts on the site say which they count: stories or printings.\n - Stories get one embedding each, from the earliest legible printing.\n - The loader upserts by stable IDs, so re-running it is safe.\ndiff --git a/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md b/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\nindex 5ba3579..f6cb886 100644\n--- a/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\n+++ b/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\n@@ -110,6 +110,7 @@ How the build runs: five phases, each split into milestones, each milestone with\n    - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.\n    - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found.\n    - And decision 31's two borderline kinds: a claim inside a narrative whose truth is doubtful, and a particular claim told inside a general essay. It confirms or overrules counting a first-person claim of communication with a named dead person, made in a lecture or an interview.\n+   - The reader's place field takes the story's state wherever it's printed. In decision 34's look at the 24 judged reports, only 3 gave a town and a state together, and 9 gave a 