{"parentUuid":"6315b15b-d224-4161-8913-b7ce886429a4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYxxe5qL1Cf3SkL88yfn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No title names a territory beyond Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands, so those two dumps cover item 4. Now the plan notes for 2C and 2D."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":192841,"output_tokens":2539,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1158},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1087,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2539,"cache_read_input_tokens":192841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1087},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"58f9702f-824e-4aa6-a2bf-7c1be640beb7","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgYxxdAmf2sXCyMN6N6mc","requestRef":"12555cda-2bc2-4ffc-9d7c-5412e4140c14","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2dc0da29-15dd-41dc-b3cc-36f5608069a2","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:22:19.842Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2dc0da29-15dd-41dc-b3cc-36f5608069a2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYxxe5qL1Cf3SkL88yfn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JnGvSAZGWnSLnjfrVcEiUY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\n\ndef swap(old, new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n\nswap('''   - The reader's place field takes the story's state wherever it's printed. In decision 34's look at the 24 judged reports, only 3 gave a town and a state together, and 9 gave a town alone.\n''', '''   - A story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved. It never falls back on the paper's state, which put 2 of decision 34's 9 towns in the wrong place. Measure the rule on the gold set.\n''')\nswap('''  - Measure the geocoder's fixes on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200:\n    - GeoNames' \"(historical)\" places outside class P\n    - the first of two towns joined by \"and\"\n    - a rule for big cities' datelines\n    - the paper's own state, for local stories only\n    - GeoNames' own dumps for Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands\n  - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever.\n''', '''  - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.\n  - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.\n  - Measure any further geocoder fix on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one.\n  - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever.\n''')\np.write_text(s)\n\np = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nswap('''- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its state today\n  The site shows a state that has changed beside the printed one: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n''', '''- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its place as its loc.gov title record catalogues it today, where the record was fetched\n  - its state today\n- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\", \"Bloomington, Iowa (now Muscatine)\".\n- A paper's point is its printed place, checked against its title record's county (`paperghosts/geo/papers.py`). A place outside that county gives way to the record's place. Where nothing agrees with the record, there is no point.\n''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit diff --stat Docs/","description":"Write the 2C and 2D plan notes and the architecture bullet"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1087,"cache_read_input_tokens":192841,"output_tokens":2539,"output_token