ed printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.\n  - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.\n  - Measure any further geocoder fix on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one.\n  - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever.\n''')\np.write_text(s)\n\np = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nswap('''- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its state today\n  The site shows a state that has changed beside the printed one: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n''', '''- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its place as its loc.gov title record catalogues it today, where the record was fetched\n  - its state today\n- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\", \"Bloomington, Iowa (now Muscatine)\".\n- A paper's point is its printed place, checked against its title record's county (`paperghosts/geo/papers.py`). A place outside that county gives way to the record's place. Where nothing agrees with the record, there is no point.\n''')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngit diff --stat Docs/","description":"Write the 2C and 2D plan notes and the architecture bullet"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"58f9702f-824e-4aa6-a2bf-7c1be640beb7","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgYxxdAmf2sXCyMN6N6mc","requestRef":"12555cda-2bc2-4ffc-9d7c-5412e4140c14","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5faba3c4-6693-449e-978b-b143b61eb638","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:22:29.112Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
