{"parentUuid":"5faba3c4-6693-449e-978b-b143b61eb638","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3c21d421-8439-4ef3-a792-2ee8b64888f0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JnGvSAZGWnSLnjfrVcEiUY","type":"tool_result","content":" Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |  7 ++++++\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |  5 ++++\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n Docs/RESUME.md       |  5 ++--\n 4 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e1025050-d6b9-4bf9-ab62-4300669002ba","timestamp":"2026-10-30T19:22:29.853Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":" Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |  7 ++++++\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |  5 ++++\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 67 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n Docs/RESUME.md       |  5 ++--\n 4 files changed, 82 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":107,"oldLines":12,"newStart":107,"newLines":14,"lines":[" - **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\"."," "," ### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load","-- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source.","+- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them."," - The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:","   - each paper's title, place and state as printed","   - what the cataloguer supplied","+  - its place as its loc.gov title record catalogues it today, where the record was fetched","   - its state today","-  The site shows a state that has changed beside the printed one: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.","+- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\", \"Bloomington, Iowa (now Muscatine)\".","+- A paper's point is its printed place, checked against its title record's county (`paperghosts/geo/papers.py`). A place outside that county gives way to the record's place. Where nothing agrees with the record, there is no point."," - Printings of the same story are grouped. Counts on the site say which they count: stories or printings."," - Stories get one embedding each, from the earliest legible printing."," - The loader upserts by stable IDs, so re-running it is safe."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":110,"oldLines":7,"newStart":110,"newLines":7,"lines":["    - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.","    - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found.","    - And decision 31's two borderline kinds: a claim inside a narrative whose truth is doubtful, and a particular claim told inside a general essay. It confirms or overrules counting a first-person claim of communication with a named dead person, made in a lecture or an interview.","-   - The reader's place field takes the story's state wherever it's printed. In decision 34's look at the 24 judged reports, only 3 gave a town and a state together, and 9 gave a town alone.","+   - A story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved. It never falls back on the paper's state, which put 2 of decision 34's 9 towns in the wrong place. Measure the rule on the gold set."," 2. Build the labelling page."," 3. Label the gold set before seeing any model output."," 4. Teacher labels for the training pool, with the leakage check passing."]},{"oldStart":136,"oldLines":12,"newStart":136,"newLines":9,"lines":[" - Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.","   - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.","   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.","-  - Measure the geocoder's fixes on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200:","-    - GeoNames' \"(historical)\" places outside class P","-    - the first of two towns joined by \"and\"","-    - a rule for big cities' datelines","-    - the paper's own state, for local stories only","-    - GeoNames' own dumps for Puerto Rico and the Virgin Islands","+  - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.","+  - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.","+  - Measure any further geocoder fix on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one.","   - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever."," - `make db-verify` runs geo, fuzzy and vector queries and checks their expected results and latencies."," - The top-case rule, and the follow-up harvest as a second Temporal pass."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"58f9702f-824e-4aa6-a2bf-7c1be640beb7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":13,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":4},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5faba3c4-6693-449e-978b-b143b61eb638","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
