{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","hash":"ab55d8c07967ec115059b6f7f8d8d36cba8bd4c44b520cddeddff447008eb449","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Two commits are in, for GeoNames and for the lookup's catalogued place. Before the third, I'm noting the case the check can't settle in the record-check module's docstring."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YNQuMJCfGsZL1dBXpwPJA7","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/paperghosts/geo/papers.py","old_string":"Without a record, the printed place stands unchecked. That's so for most papers until 2D asks\nfor the records of the papers it stores (BUILD-PLAN.md).","new_string":"A record that names no county GeoNames has in its state, as for Alaska's and Connecticut's\nplaces, can't check one: the printed place stands, or where that resolves to nothing, the\nrecord's own place, unchecked. Without a record, the printed place stands unchecked too. That's\nso for most papers until 2D asks for the records of the papers it stores (BUILD-PLAN.md)."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Pg69Vyi7as2pJRjoHySk2v","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && uv run ruff check -q paperghosts/geo/papers.py && uv run ruff format --check -q paperghosts/geo/papers.py && uv run pytest tests/test_papers.py -q 2>&1 | tail -n 1 && git add paperghosts/geo/papers.py && git diff --cached > $S/staged.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/staged.diff; echo \"machine-name matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/staged.diff)\"","description":"Recheck and restage the record-check module"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
