{"parentUuid":"7f6127cb-7a1d-4231-a141-15929e59353c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgYyGsAPP9DwH9fBg89Ad","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XrkGp8itwEWRMpqy9R8TUH","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nstart = s.index(\"- **Accuracy on the papers**\")\nend = s.index(\"- **The 24 judged reports' story places,**\")\nold_block = s[start:end]\nassert \"These 200 didn't tune the geocoder.\" in old_block\nnew_block = \"\"\"- **Accuracy on the papers** (`scripts/geocode_check.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/geocoder.json`, answers in `geocoder_expected.json`):\n  - The draw: 200 distinct (place, state) pairs, by walking the papers in seeded order (seed \"2B geocoder\"). I checked each by hand.\n  - Each pair is geocoded twice: by its printed place alone, and with the record check against its paper's record.\n  - **Without the record check, {{N_WITHOUT}} are right: {{P_WITHOUT}}.**\n    - Ponce, P.R. is right now, because the Puerto Rico dump is an input.\n    - Before the dump, 193 were right (96.5%). Before the parser fix the draw prompted, 192 were (96.0%).\n  - **With the record check, {{N_WITH}} are right: {{P_WITH}}.** {{WRONG_PINS}}\n  - What the records made of the 200: {{RECORD_OUTCOMES}}\n  - Some are right under an old name or a merger: Allegheny is Pittsburgh, and Daytona is Daytona Beach. Fort Wrangel, Sumterville, North Yakima and Langston City are old names their towns list.\n  - **The failures, by kind:**\n\n    | Kind | Without the check | With it | Cases |\n    |---|---|---|---|\n    | merged into a town that doesn't list its name | 3 | {{MERGED}} | East Saginaw into Saginaw; Lardo into McCall; New Oregon into Cresco |\n    | renamed, with its old name now another town's | 1 | {{RENAMED}} | Bloomington, Iowa, Muscatine's name until 1849. Without the check, it's a wrong pin, on a living Bloomington elsewhere |\n    | two towns named as one place | 1 | {{TWO}} | \"Norfolk and Portsmouth, Va.\" |\n    | a ghost town filed outside populated places | 1 | {{GHOST}} | Clifton, S.D., which GeoNames has as \"Clifton (historical)\" in class S |\n    | outside GeoNames' US dump | 0 | 0 | Ponce, P.R., right since the Puerto Rico dump became an input |\n\n  - **These 200 are in-sample for the check.** Its fixes come from their failures, through the EM's review, and so does the Alaska rule. 2D measures any further fix on a fresh draw (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n\"\"\"\ns = s[:start] + new_block + s[end:]\nold = \"\"\"  - So 2C's reader should take a story's state wherever it's printed. A big city's dateline, and the paper's state, need rules of their own.\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1\ns = s.replace(old, \"\"\"  - **So a story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved, and it never falls back on the paper's state** (the EM's review). 2C measures the rule on its gold set, and 2D applies it (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\"\"\")\np.write_text(s)\nPY\ngrep -o \"{{[A-Z_]*}}\" Docs/DECISIONS.md | sort | uniq | tr '\\n' ' '; echo; ls data/loc/titles | wc -l; tail -n 2 /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/titles-run.log","description":"Draft the accuracy section and the story-place rule"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3806,"cache_read_input_tokens":217460,"output_tokens":2893,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1439},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3806,"ephemeral_5m_inpu