{"parentUuid":"c20a7e12-d225-4e9c-adb8-4a36307b206d","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/paperghosts/geo/papers.py","snippet":"1\t\"\"\"Where each paper was printed (decision 34): its printed place geocoded, then checked against\n2\tits loc.gov title record where it has one.\n3\t\n4\t1. The printed place is geocoded in its modern state: the cataloguer's bracketed place first,\n5\t   then the printed one.\n6\t2. With a record that names counties, a result inside one of them, in one of its states,\n7\t   stands.\n8\t3. A result outside them, or no result at all, gives way to the record's place as catalogued\n9\t   today, geocoded in the record's county.\n10\t4. Failing that, a ghost town of the record's name in the record's county, flagged historical.\n11\t5. Failing that, no point: a pin that disagrees with the record is the dangerous kind of answer.\n12\tA record that names no county GeoNames has in its state, as for Alaska's and Connecticut's\n13\tplaces, can't check one: the printed place stands, or where that resolves to nothing, the\n14\trecord's own place, unchecked. Without a record, the printed place stands unchecked too. That's\n15\tso for most papers until 2D asks for the records of the papers it stores (BUILD-PLAN.md).\n...\n39\t\n40\t\n41\tdef paper_place(gazetteer, title, given=None):\n42\t    \"\"\"The GeoNames place a paper was printed in, and what its record (`loc.recorded`) made of\n43\t    it, under \"record\".\"\"\"\n44\t    printed = printed_place(gazetteer, title)\n45\t    if not given or not given.get(\"place\"):\n46\t        return printed | {\"record\": \"none\"}\n47\t    counties, states = (\n48\t        given.get(\"counties\") or [],\n49\t        given.get(\"states\") or [given[\"state\"]],\n50\t    )\n51\t    agrees = gazetteer.same_county(printed, counties, states)\n52\t    if agrees is None:\n53\t        why = (\n54\t            \"can't be checked against GeoNames' counties\"\n55\t            if counties\n56\t            else \"has no county to check\"\n57\t        )\n58\t        if printed[\"place_id\"] is not None:\n59\t            return printed | {\"record\": why}\n...\n65\t    how = (\n66\t        \"replaced the printed place\"\n67\t        if printed[\"place_id\"] is not None\n68\t        else \"found what the printed place didn't\"\n69\t    )\n70\t    for county in counties:\n71\t        catalogued = gazetteer.geocode(given[\"place\"], given[\"state\"], county)\n72\t        if catalogued[\"place_id\"] is not None and gazetteer.same_county(\n73\t            catalogued, counties, states\n74\t        ):\n75\t            return catalogued | {\"record\": how}\n76\t    ghost = gazetteer.ghost(given[\"place\"], given[\"state\"], counties)\n77\t    if ghost:\n78\t        return ghost | {\"record\": \"a ghost town in the record's county\"}\n79\t    return gazetteer.base() | {\n80\t        \"reason\": \"outside the record's county, whose own place isn't in GeoNames\",\n81\t        \"record\": \"disagrees, and its own place isn't in GeoNames\","},"type":"attachment","uuid":"cbf8ded4-4964-42cf-8af3-c7d1bc487c5b","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:00:54.050Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/paperghosts/geo/papers.py changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n1\t\"\"\"Where each paper was printed (decision 34): its printed place geocoded, then checked against\n2\tits loc.gov title record where it has one.\n3\t\n4\t1. The printed place is geocoded in its modern state: the cataloguer's bracketed place first,\n5\t   then the printed one.\n6\t2. With a record that names counties, a result inside one of them, in one of its states,\n7\t   stands.\n8\t3. A result outside them, or no result at all, gives way to the record's place as catalogued\n9\t   today, geocoded in the record's county.\n10\t4. Failing that, a ghost town of the record's name in the record's county, flagged historical.\n11\t5. Failing that, no point: a pin that disagrees with the record is the dangerous kind of answer.\n12\tA record that names no county GeoNames has in its state, as for Alaska's and Connecticut's\n13\tplaces, can't check one: the printed place stands, or where that resolves to nothing, the\n14\trecord's own place, unchecked. Without a record, the printed place stands unchecked too. That's\n15\tso for most papers until 2D asks for the records of the papers it stores (BUILD-PLAN.md).\n...\n39\t\n40\t\n41\tdef paper_place(gazetteer, title, given=None):\n42\t    \"\"\"The GeoNames place a paper was printed in, and what its record (`loc.recorded`) made of\n43\t    it, under \"record\".\"\"\"\n44\t    printed = printed_place(gazetteer, title)\n45\t    if not given or not given.get(\"place\"):\n46\t        return printed | {\"record\": \"none\"}\n47\t    counties, states = (\n48\t        given.get(\"counties\") or [],\n49\t        given.get(\"states\") or [given[\"state\"]],\n50\t    )\n51\t    agrees = gazetteer.same_county(printed, counties, states)\n52\t    if agrees is None:\n53\t        why = (\n54\t            \"can't be checked against GeoNames' counties\"\n55\t            if counties\n56\t            else \"has no county to check\"\n57\t        )\n58\t        if printed[\"place_id\"] is not None:\n59\t            return printed | {\"record\": why}\n...\n65\t    how = (\n66\t        \"replaced the printed place\"\n67\t        if printed[\"place_id\"] is not None\n68\t        else \"found what the printed place didn't\"\n69\t    )\n70\t    for county in counties:\n71\t        catalogued = gazetteer.geocode(given[\"place\"], given[\"state\"], county)\n72\t        if catalogued[\"place_id\"] is not None and gazetteer.same_county(\n73\t            catalogued, counties, states\n74\t        ):\n75\t            return catalogued | {\"record\": how}\n76\t    ghost = gazetteer.ghost(given[\"place\"], given[\"state\"], counties)\n77\t    if ghost:\n78\t        return ghost | {\"record\": \"a ghost town in the record's county\"}\n79\t    return gazetteer.base() | {\n80\t        \"reason\": \"outside the record's county, whose own place isn't in GeoNames\",\n81\t        \"record\": \"disagrees, and its own place isn't in GeoNames\",\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
