{"parentUuid":"c76fea6d-0de7-4702-a738-9a369f7396da","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZ2FFdJPuMARNaDmwU4Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NNkg6hzf7cNk868Vz7ySbo","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef edit(path, pairs):\n    p = Path(path)\n    s = p.read_text()\n    for old, new in pairs:\n        assert s.count(old) == 1, (path, old[:80])\n        s = s.replace(old, new)\n    p.write_text(s)\n\nedit(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\", [\n    ('''- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\", \"Bloomington, Iowa (now Muscatine)\".\n''', '''- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". It names the record's town only where the paper's point is the record's place: \"East Saginaw, Mich. (now Saginaw)\".\n'''),\n])\nedit(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\", [\n    ('''  - Measure any further geocoder fix on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one.\n''', '''  - Measure the record check, and any further geocoder fix, on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one such fix.\n'''),\n])\np = Path(\"eval/results/phase2b/geocoder_expected.json\")\ne = json.loads(p.read_text())\nentry = e[\"papers\"][\"Norfolk and Portsmouth|Virginia\"]\nassert entry[\"note\"] == \"Norfolk day book (Norfolk and Portsmouth Va.): printed in Norfolk\", entry[\"note\"]\nentry[\"note\"] = \"Norfolk day book (Norfolk and Portsmouth Va.): Norfolk, from its title. Its title record gives Portsmouth as its place, and its notes say it was published in both\"\np.write_text(json.dumps(e, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\nPY\ngit diff --stat Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md Docs/BUILD-PLAN.