{"parentUuid":"2d36c9b0-3872-42bf-9a7e-fe654507952d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b997187a-e537-4e1f-b3c7-20b1dfc34455","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KL7vBb5R6UyQfZrAnRNsyM","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 7 of 7 is in progress."}]}]},"uuid":"0e25a406-38ac-402b-b7ab-cf392bec08e1","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:09:11.060Z","toolUseResult":[{"type":"text","text":"Plan updated: step 7 of 7 is in progress."}],"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2d36c9b0-3872-42bf-9a7e-fe654507952d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"rule","ruleSource":"cliArg"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"0e25a406-38ac-402b-b7ab-cf392bec08e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZ2XFcWB8Vt4dcyRi3YF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015t9yn3js151ATmSutb8DbF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.2.md","content":"# Step 2B.2: DONE\n\nOn `phase-2b-data-layer`. I checked origin with `git ls-remote`: it shows `5b606c7`, the same as local.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `ff9f93e` | step 0: BUDGET.md's third scenario, stories per printing from the judged reports |\n| `324dd30` | the title parser, tested on 200 titles checked by hand |\n| `3384621` | the GeoNames geocoder over the US dump, with its manifest |\n| `f309dea` | a parser fix the geocoder's draw found |\n| `6c0dbd7` | loc.gov title records, and the title lookup by LCCN |\n| `2e2fc32` | your review: the PR and VI dumps, ghost towns, and the county check |\n| `c8e01f7` | your review: the lookup keeps each paper's place as its record catalogues it |\n| `7ac574b` | your review: the record check |\n| `e24e2e3` | the check reads all of a record's states, from `location_state` |\n| `4e1db3f` | the display names the record's town only where the check put the point there |\n| `ae066ed` | the accuracy with and without the check, and the lookup's report |\n| `5b606c7` | decision 34, the plan's notes for 2C and 2D, ARCHITECTURE 3.3 and the resume |\n\nNo PR yet. Phase 2B's PR comes at the end of 2B, unless you want one now.\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Tests and lint:** `make test` gives 311 passed, the live `atlas` test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- **Parser:** the 200 hand-checked titles in `tests/fixtures/titles.json` all pass, as does the 1835 Charlestown test (\"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\").\n- **Title records:** asked for only for the 424 LCCNs whose title strings name no place or state. Requests are at least 3.5 s apart, never in parallel, and each record is cached with its URL, date and status.\n  - 423 were found, and 1 got a 404: sn88084224, The Western star (Texas). None failed.\n  - The final build made 327 requests in 39 minutes. The other 97 were cached already.\n- **The 200 pairs' records:** these ran after that fetch, never beside it. 177 requests took 20 minutes. One got a 503, wasn't cached, and was fetched on the next run. All 200 have a record.\n- **GeoNames:** the US, PR and VI dumps of 2026-10-30. `data/geonames/manifest.json` gives each file's URL, size and sha256, and the CC BY 4.0 licence. No title names any other territory.\n- **Accuracy on the 200 pairs**, answers checked by hand (`geocoder_expected.json`, `geocoder.json`):\n\n  | | Right | Resolved, and right | Wrong pins |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | without the record check | 194: 97.0% (93.6–98.6%) | 194 of 195: 99.5% (97.2–99.9%) | 1: Bloomington |\n  | with it | 196: 98.0% (95.0–99.2%) | 196 of 198: 99.0% (96.4–99.7%) | 2: Bloomington, and Norfolk and Portsmouth |\n\n  - Failure kinds without the check, then with it:\n    - merged: 3, then 2\n    - renamed: 1, then 1\n    - two towns named as one place: 1, then 1\n    - ghost town: 1, then 0\n  - What the records made of the 200:\n    - agrees: 177\n    - no county to check: 14\n    - can't be checked: 4\n    - found what the printed place didn't: 1 (East Saginaw)\n    - ghost town: 1 (Clifton)\n    - unchecked record place: 1 (Norfolk and Portsmouth)\n    - disagrees, with no point: 2 (Lardo and New Oregon)\n    - replaced: 0\n- **The 24 reports' story places:**\n  - 3 give a town and a state, and all 3 are right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 give a town only, 8 no town, and 4 are abroad.\n\n## Your review's changes\n\n1. **Title record first.** `paper_place` in `paperghosts/geo/papers.py` checks the printed place against the record's county. It fixes East Saginaw and Clifton. It doesn't catch Bloomington: loc.gov's own record lists Story and Muscatine counties, so Bloomington in Story County agrees.\n   - The display keeps the printed place. It adds the record's town only where the check put the point there: \"East Saginaw, Mich. (now Saginaw)\". A first version compared names alone, and 8 of its 14 \"now\" towns were papers that moved (\"Manchester, Vt. (now Bennington)\"). The fix is `4e1db3f`.\n   - **Merged towns:** only East Saginaw is catalogued under its successor. Lardo's record names Lardo and Roseberry in Idaho County, its county then, and GeoNames files both in Valley County. New Oregon's record names New Oregon. Both stay as no point.\n2. **Measured now:** see the table above.\n3. **2D's record fetch** is in the plan: records only for the papers among stored printings, cached.\n4. **Inputs:** PR.zip and VI.zip are in the inputs and the manifest.\n5. **Ghost towns:** Clifton, S.D. becomes 5763634, flagged historical, in the record's Sully County.\n6. **The story-place rule** is in the plan for 2C and 2D. My count for the paper's state: right for 3 of the 9 town-only stories, all of them local; wrong for 2; nothing for 4. Your note said 1 of 3. The rule stands either way.\n\n## For you\n\n- **Two rules came from these 200, so they're in-sample**, as decision 34 says:\n  - A county GeoNames doesn't have leaves the place unchecked. Seward, Alaska is the case.\n  - The check reads `location_state`, as you specified. I had taken the state from `location_str`, and Zajedničar, which moved from Pennsylvania to Ohio, broke.\n- **Norfolk and Portsmouth: your call.** The record names no county and gives Portsmouth, so the check pins Portsmouth, about 2 km from my expected Norfolk. Its notes say the paper was published in both.\n  - I'd keep the rule: the pin is loc.gov's catalogued place.\n  - The alternative is no point wherever a record has no county and the printed place doesn't resolve.\n- **The title lookup build now loads the gazetteer**, because the display needs the check. It takes 8 s from the cache.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_read_input_tokens":318059,"output_tokens":4531,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2080},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4531,"cache_read_input_tokens":318059,"cache_creation_input_tokens":696,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":696},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_015t9yn3js151ATmSutb8DbF":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.2.md","content":"# Step 2B.2: DONE\n\nOn `phase-2b-data-layer`. I checked origin with `git ls-remote`: it shows `5b606c7`, the same as local.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `ff9f93e` | step 0: BUDGET.md's third scenario, stories per printing from the judged reports |\n| `324dd30` | the title parser, tested on 200 titles checked by hand |\n| `3384621` | the GeoNames geocoder over the US dump, with its manifest |\n| `f309dea` | a parser fix the geocoder's draw found |\n| `6c0dbd7` | loc.gov title records, and the title lookup by LCCN |\n| `2e2fc32` | your review: the PR and VI dumps, ghost towns, and the county check |\n| `c8e01f7` | your review: the lookup keeps each paper's place as its record catalogues it |\n| `7ac574b` | your review: the record check |\n| `e24e2e3` | the check reads all of a record's states, from `location_state` |\n| `4e1db3f` | the display names the record's town only where the check put the point there |\n| `ae066ed` | the accuracy with and without the check, and the lookup's report |\n| `5b606c7` | decision 34, the plan's notes for 2C and 2D, ARCHITECTURE 3.3 and the resume |\n\nNo PR yet. Phase 2B's PR comes at the end of 2B, unless you want one now.\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Tests and lint:** `make test` gives 311 passed, the live `atlas` test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- **Parser:** the 200 hand-checked titles in `tests/fixtures/titles.json` all pass, as does the 1835 Charlestown test (\"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\").\n- **Title records:** asked for only for the 424 LCCNs whose title strings name no place or state. Requests are at least 3.5 s apart, never in parallel, and each record is cached with its URL, date and status.\n  - 423 were found, and 1 got a 404: sn88084224, The Western star (Texas). None failed.\n  - The final build made 327 requests in 39 minutes. The other 97 were cached already.\n- **The 200 pairs' records:** these ran after that fetch, never beside it. 177 requests took 20 minutes. One got a 503, wasn't cached, and was fetched on the next run. All 200 have a record.\n- **GeoNames:** the US, PR and VI dumps of 2026-10-30. `data/geonames/manifest.json` gives each file's URL, size and sha256, and the CC BY 4.0 licence. No title names any other territory.\n- **Accuracy on the 200 pairs**, answers checked by hand (`geocoder_expected.json`, `geocoder.json`):\n\n  | | Right | Resolved, and right | Wrong pins |\n  |---|---|---|---|\n  | without the record check | 194: 97.0% (93.6–98.6%) | 194 of 195: 99.5% (97.2–99.9%) | 1: Bloomington |\n  | with it | 196: 98.0% (95.0–99.2%) | 196 of 198: 99.0% (96.4–99.7%) | 2: Bloomington, and Norfolk and Portsmouth |\n\n  - Failure kinds without the check, then with it:\n    - merged: 3, then 2\n    - renamed: 1, then 1\n    - two towns named as one place: 1, then 1\n    - ghost town: 1, then 0\n  - What the records made of the 200:\n    - agrees: 177\n    - no county to check: 14\n    - can't be checked: 4\n    - found what the printed place didn't: 1 (East Saginaw)\n    - ghost town: 1 (Clifton)\n    - unchecked record place: 1 (Norfolk and Portsmouth)\n    - disagrees, with no point: 2 (Lardo and New Oregon)\n    - replaced: 0\n- **The 24 reports' story places:**\n  - 3 give a town and a state, and all 3 are right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 give a town only, 8 no town, and 4 are abroad.\n\n## Your review's changes\n\n1. **Title record first.** `paper_place` in `paperghosts/geo/papers.py` checks the printed place against the record's county. It fixes East Saginaw and Clifton. It doesn't catch Bloomington: loc.gov's own record lists Story and Muscatine counties, so Bloomington in Story County agrees.\n   - The display keeps the printed place. It adds the record's town only where the check put the point there: \"East Saginaw, Mich. (now Saginaw)\". A first version compared names alone, and 8 of its 14 \"now\" towns were papers that moved (\"Manchester, Vt. (now Bennington)\"). The fix is `4e1db3f`.\n   - **Merged towns:** only East Saginaw is catalogued under its successor. Lardo's record names Lardo and Roseberry in Idaho County, its county then, and GeoNames files both in Valley County. New Oregon's record names New Oregon. Both stay as no point.\n2. **Measured now:** see the table above.\n3. **2D's record fetch** is in the plan: records only for the papers among stored printings, cached.\n4. **Inputs:** PR.zip and VI.zip are in the inputs and the manifest.\n5. **Ghost towns:** Clifton, S.D. becomes 5763634, flagged historical, in the record's Sully County.\n6. **The story-place rule** is in the plan for 2C and 2D. My count for the paper's state: right for 3 of the 9 town-only stories, all of them local; wrong for 2; nothing for 4. Your note said 1 of 3. The rule stands either way.\n\n## For you\n\n- **Two rules came from these 200, so they're in-sample**, as decision 34 says:\n  - A county GeoNames doesn't have leaves the place unchecked. Seward, Alaska is the case.\n  - The check reads `location_state`, as you specified. I had taken the state from `location_str`, and Zajedničar, which moved from Pennsylvania to Ohio, broke.\n- **Norfolk and Portsmouth: your call.** The record names no county and gives Portsmouth, so the check pins Portsmouth, about 2 km from my expected Norfolk. Its notes say the paper was published in both.\n  - I'd keep the rule: the pin is loc.gov's catalogued place.\n  - The alternative is no point wherever a record has no county and the printed place doesn't resolve.\n- **The title lookup build now loads the gazetteer**, because the display needs the check. It takes 8 s from the cache.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"99ea61ef-301c-4dcf-8912-a4d166d6639f","apiBlockIndex":3,"requestId":"req_011CgZ2XEwpP7fknvCaS6NtC","requestRef":"fb0c44a7-3759-49ef-89d5-2a017c9b41fe","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"3a595e8f-697d-4aca-a0d6-1ab5e626d13e","timestamp":"2026-10-30T20:09:29.753Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
