{"parentUuid":"a5ddedfe-4df9-4104-ab40-d1a04b282c51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZ2bzaGTajFhy8WmWmWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2B.2: DONE. I pushed `phase-2b-data-layer` at `5b606c7`, and `ls-remote` shows the same commit. The hand-over note is `step-2B.2.md`. 311 tests and lint pass.\n\nAccuracy on the 200 pairs:\n- **Without the record check:** 194 right, 97.0% (93.6–98.6%), with 1 wrong pin.\n- **With it:** 196 right, 98.0% (95.0–99.2%), with 2 wrong pins.\n\nThe check fixes East Saginaw, and Clifton as a flagged ghost town. It can't catch Bloomington, because loc.gov's own record lists Story County. It adds Portsmouth for Norfolk and Portsmouth, because that record has no county and says the paper was published in both. Keeping that rule is your call. Of the three merged towns, only East Saginaw's record names its successor.\n\nTwo of the check's rules came from these 200, and decision 34 says so: Alaska's uncheckable counties, and reading `location_state` (Zajedničar moved from Pennsylvania to Ohio)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":239,"cache_read_input_tokens":323966,"output_tokens":367,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":239,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":367,"cache_read_input_tokens":323966,"cache_creation_input_tokens":239,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":239},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"64aeb6ae-d5f0-4b21-8243-1582f31c45b7","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZ2byku