{"parentUuid":"4646a659-bf35-4027-86e6-94cb18c99767","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZM1JvJgT7JQC8c99U7s","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WpEWtfqCTHxVPXEjEqcoPd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && grep -n \"^[0-9]*\\. \\*\\*\\|^### \\|^\\*\\*[0-9]\" Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -60","description":"List the numbered decisions"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2369,"cache_read_input_tokens":104931,"output_tokens":166,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2369,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":166,"cache_read_input_tokens":104931,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2369,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2369},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WpEWtfqCTHxVPXEjEqcoPd":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && grep -n \"^[0-9]*\\. \\*\\*\\|^### \\|^\\*\\*[0-9]\" Docs/DECISIONS.md | head -60","description":"List the numbered decisions"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"e154bae9-e25b-4f45-aa68-90276129725e","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZM1J7BqdUxiyBpZHD6r","requestRef":"70ad9552-a686-476d-addc-00536a580f9c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a49f7e50-64a2-4ab5-a234-6a83045b02fc","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:11:16.919Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a49f7e50-64a2-4ab5-a234-6a83045b02fc","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WpEWtfqCTHxVPXEjEqcoPd","type":"tool_result","content":"7:**1. The source is AmericanStories, not the Chronicling America API.**\n10:**2. Read the whole archive (180 year files), not a sample.**\n13:**3. Stream every file and never keep the tarballs.**\n16:**4. Walks is an optional layer on top of search, and it is built last.**\n24:**5. One main tool (Tinker); the others support it. MongoDB Atlas, not Tiger Data. No .tech domain.**\n36:**6. The build runs in five phases with gates, managed by an EM session.**\n39:**7. Static-first site: the core path is prebuilt JSON, and the live API handles search, near me and similar.**\n42:**8. Stories and printings are counted separately.**\n45:**9. Models are selected on a dev split, and the gold set is used only for final evals.**\n48:**10. The investigator's default model is Gemma 4 26B-A4B (QAT), running locally through Ollama. Ultramarine is the comparison run.**\n51:**11. The Halloween look comes from the reading room after dark.**\n54:**12. Config accepts both names for the Ultramarine key.**\n59:**13. `make keys` checks each key with the service's cheapest read, and never prints a value.**\n66:**14. Per-year counts are committed.**\n69:**15. Sentry collects nothing about people, and nothing a local variable holds.**\n75:**16. The smoke activity resumes after its last heartbeat.**\n78:**17. The environment facts measure the download and the parse in one pass, in two processes.**\n81:**18. Crops use the scan's own pixels, and loc.gov names the batch when the record doesn't.**\n88:**19. Lexicon v1 counts the 1850s spirit noises as ghost terms, and reads through common OCR damage.**\n93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n221:**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about half the reports, and lexicon v2 is proposed but not run.**\n272:**31. Lexicon v2 is run. Its spiritualist rules add 185,663 candidates (+17.7%), and 7.0% of them are ghost reports. Its recall is about 84%, but that figure is in-sample.**\n362:**32. Atlas is the serving index, not the archive. It is built to M0's limits and to nine rules.**\n392:**33. The data layer is built: models, validators generated from them, BinData embeddings and `make db-init`. M0's third Search index waits on the owner.**\n450:**34. Every paper's title, place and state as printed, with its state today; and a GeoNames geocoder, checked against each paper's loc.gov title record, which puts 98.0% of papers' places right.**","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"af1bc4c7-bdda-43b4-9c29-503c0e9bc5c2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:11:17.471Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"7:**1. The source is AmericanStories, not the Chronicling America API.**\n10:**2. Read the whole archive (180 year files), not a sample.**\n13:**3. Stream every file and never keep the tarballs.**\n16:**4. Walks is an optional layer on top of search, and it is built last.**\n24:**5. One main tool (Tinker); the others support it. MongoDB Atlas, not Tiger Data. No .tech domain.**\n36:**6. The build runs in five phases with gates, managed by an EM session.**\n39:**7. Static-first site: the core path is prebuilt JSON, and the live API handles search, near me and similar.**\n42:**8. Stories and printings are counted separately.**\n45:**9. Models are selected on a dev split, and the gold set is used only for final evals.**\n48:**10. The investigator's default model is Gemma 4 26B-A4B (QAT), running locally through Ollama. Ultramarine is the comparison run.**\n51:**11. The Halloween look comes from the reading room after dark.**\n54:**12. Config accepts both names for the Ultramarine key.**\n59:**13. `make keys` checks each key with the service's cheapest read, and never prints a value.**\n66:**14. Per-year counts are committed.**\n69:**15. Sentry collects nothing about people, and nothing a local variable holds.**\n75:**16. The smoke activity resumes after its last heartbeat.**\n78:**17. The environment facts measure the download and the parse in one pass, in two processes.**\n81:**18. Crops use the scan's own pixels, and loc.gov names the batch when the record doesn't.**\n88:**19. Lexicon v1 counts the 1850s spirit noises as ghost terms, and reads through common OCR damage.**\n93:**20. The knocking term stays: on its own it keeps 293 candidates of 1850, and 11 of the 18 known knockings articles.**\n98:**21. The prefilter pre-checks folded stems, and keeps a 2,000-article sample of each pool per year.**\n102:**22. The ingest runs each year in a fresh process, and a year is done once its manifest is written.**\n108:**23. A year is skipped only while its cache key and every output's hash match, and a lost attempt stops at its next heartbeat.**\n116:**24. Temporal identities name the process and its role, not the host.**\n119:**25. The full read ran four years at a time, each on one CPU-bound core. A re-read can set its concurrency from these numbers.**\n133:**26. Crops are one per box, fetched once and cached, and the display headline drops only the masthead lines that lead it.**\n152:**27. Eval A: 3.5% of candidates are ghost reports, none of 600 articles from outside them is one, and lexicon v1 stays.**\n190:**28. The display headline drops a date only when it is the issue's own, and a number only beside the paper's title or volume.**\n210:**29. A third of candidates have no batch path, but most of their reels do. AmericanStories' stray boxes stay.**\n221:**30. A flag-word screen of 38,600 more non-candidates found 4 ghost reports, all spiritualist and all saying \"spirit\". Lexicon v1 finds about half the reports, and lexicon v2 is proposed but not run.**\n272:**31. Lexicon v2 is run. Its spiritualist rules add 185,663 candidates (+17.7%), and 7.0% of them are ghost reports. Its recall is about 84%, but that figure is in-sample.**\n362:**32. Atlas is the serving index, not the archive. It is built to M0's limits and to nine rules.**\n392:**33. The data layer is built: models, validators generated from them, BinData embeddings and `make db-init`. M0's third Search index waits on the owner.**\n450:**34. Every paper's title, place and state as printed, with its state today; and a GeoNames geocoder, checked against each paper's loc.gov title record, which puts 98.0% of papers' places right.**","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"e154bae9-e25b-4f45-aa68-90276129725e","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/w