isorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"7636bb84-79b7-4150-8840-c11526cd52ee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015vVxc3M8HXu1k6KSNKDJgJ","type":"tool_result","content":"403:  - **Location:** a printing is located by its member name, as `1910-04-12_p8_sn84022472_0029586686A_1910041201_0396.json` shows. That gives the date, a page token, the LCCN, the reel, the issue (the date and a two-digit edition) and the frame.\n404:    - Every member name parses, and every issue is its date and two digits.\n406:  - **LCCN:** 10,871 records (0.88%) have none, and those take the member's. Every record that has one agrees with its member name.\n407:  - **Page:** the page comes from the scan record only, where it is a number for 19.9% of candidates. It is never taken from the member name's page token.\n408:    - In 1910, the article ID and the member name differ only in that token, for 18,082 of 25,346 candidates (71.3%). Their date, LCCN, reel, issue and frame always agree.\n409:    - In those candidates the member gives a page number that the scan record doesn't confirm: the scan says \"na\" or nothing.\n411:  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396.\n412:    - Example: the member `…_1910021001_0164` and the jp2 `sn82016187/100493962/1910021001/0163.jp2`.\n----\n\"\"\"IIIF crops of article clippings from the Library of Congress page scans, and the cache\nunder data/crops/ that keeps each crop once it is fetched.\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport os\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom time import monotonic, sleep\n\nimport httpx\n\nIIIF = \"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif\"\nBATCH_PATH = re.compile(\n    r\"/data/batches/(?P<batch>[^/]+)/data/(?P<lccn>[^/]+)/(?P<reel>[^/]+)\"\n    r\"/(?P<issue>[^/]+)/(?P<seq>[^/.]+)\\.jp2$\"\n)\n# a faro member: date, page, LCCN, reel (sometimes 'no_reel'), issue and sequence\nMEMBER = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<date>\\d{4}-\\d\\d-\\d\\d)_p[^_]*_(?P<lccn>[^_]+)_(?P<reel>.+)\"\n    r\"_(?P<issue>\\d{10})_(?P<seq>\\d+)(?:\\.json)?$\"\n)\nCROPS = Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"data\" / \"crops\"\nUSER_AGENT = (\n    \"PaperGhosts/0.1 (a Hacktoberfest ghost-story map; github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts)\"\n)\nCLIENT = httpx.Client(timeout=60, follow_redirects=True)\nlast_request = 0.0  # monotonic time of the last request to the Library of Congress\nBUSY = {429, 500, 502, 503, 504, 520, 521, 522, 523, 524}  # 52x: Cloudflare's\n# seconds between requests: loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 a minute and blocks for an hour past\n# that, and its image services allow 150 a minute\nGAPS = {\"www.loc.gov\": 3.5}\n\n\ndef service_id(raw_data_loc: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from the batch path AmericanStories records for its scan.\"\"\"\n    path = BATCH_PATH.search(raw_data_loc)\n    if path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"raw_data_loc is not a Chronicling America batch path\")\n    awardee = path[\"batch\"].split(\"_\")[0]\n    return (\n        f\"service:ndnp:{awardee}:batch_{path['batch']}:data:\"\n        f\"{path['lccn']}:{path['reel']}:{path['issue']}:{path['seq']}\"\n    )\n\n\ndef crop_urls(service: str, boxes: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"One crop per box, in the scan's own pixels at half size, in bbox_list's order, which\n    is the order the article is read in. One crop over every box would take in the columns\n    between them.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        f\"{IIIF}/{service}/{b['x0']},{b['y0']},{b['x1'] - b['x0']},{b['y1'] - b['y0']}\"\n        \"/pct:50/0/default.jpg\"\n        for b in boxes\n    ]\n\n\ndef get(url, **params):\n    \"\"\"A GET to the Library of Congress: at most one a second, or one in 3.5 s to loc.gov's\n    JSON API, naming the project, and asked again after a pause while the server is busy.\n    tile.loc.gov can answer a crop it hasn't made yet with a 503.\"\"\"\n    global last_request\n    gap = GAPS.get(httpx.URL(url).host, 1.0)\n    for pause in (5, 20, None):\n        sleep(max(0.0, last_request + gap - monotonic()))\n        last_request = monotonic()\n        try:\n            response = CLIENT.get(\n                url, params=params, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT}\n            )\n        except httpx.TransportError:\n            if pause is None:\n                raise\n        else:\n            if response.status_code not in BUSY or pause is None:\n                response.raise_for_status()\n                return response\n        sleep(pause)\n\n\ndef page_service(member: str, scan: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from its batch path, or else from the loc.gov item that\n    lists the page, since some scans have no batch path (decision 18).\"\"\"\n    if scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n        return service_id(scan[\"raw_data_loc\"])\n    page = MEMBER.search(member)\n    if page is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"{member} is not a faro page name\")\n    url = f\"https://www.loc.gov/item/{page['lccn']}/{page['date']}/ed-{int(page['issue'][-2:])}/\"\n    try:\n        item = get(url, fo=\"json\").text\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404:\n            raise\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov has no item for {member}\") from exc\n    found = re.search(\n        rf\"service:ndnp:[a-z]+:batch_\\w+?:data:{page['lccn']}:{page['reel']}\"\n        rf\":{page['issue']}:{page['seq']}\",\n        item,\n    )\n    if found is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov lists no IIIF service for {member}\")\n    return found[0]\n\n\ndef batch(service: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The LoC batch that holds the page, from its IIIF service.\"\"\"\n    return re.search(r\":batch_(\\w+?):data:\", service)[1]\n\n\ndef crop(url: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The crop at url, from the cache, which is keyed by the URL, or fetched once into it.\"\"\"\n    path = CROPS / f\"{hashlib.sha256(url.encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}.jpg\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        response = get(url)\n        if not response.headers.get(\"content-type\", \"\").startswith(\"image/\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"tile.loc.gov sent no image for {url}\")\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        partial = path.with_name(f\"{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.partial\")\n        partial.write_bytes(response.content)\n        partial.replace(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef crops_for(member: str, scan: dict, boxes: list[dict], service: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service and its crops, one per box. A batch path can name a batch\n    that LoC has since reissued (ver01 where it now serves ver02), so when a crop from it is\n    missing, loc.gov names the page's current service.\"\"\"\n    service = service or page_service(member, scan)\n    try:\n        return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404 or not scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n            raise\n    service = page_service(member, {})\n    return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4766d3b-45e1-4b2b-8d73-7c6307f1ace9","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:11:25.941Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"403:  - **Location:** a printing is located by its member name, as `1910-04-12_p8_sn84022472_0029586686A_1910041201_0396.json` shows. That gives the date, a page token, the LCCN, the reel, the issue (the date and a two-digit edition) and the frame.\n404:    - Every member name parses, and every issue is its date and two digits.\n406:  - **LCCN:** 10,871 records (0.88%) have none, and those take the member's. Every record that has one agrees with its member name.\n407:  - **Page:** the page comes from the scan record only, where it is a number for 19.9% of candidates. It is never taken from the member name's page token.\n408:    - In 1910, the article ID and the member name differ only in that token, for 18,082 of 25,346 candidates (71.3%). Their date, LCCN, reel, issue and frame always agree.\n409:    - In those candidates the member gives a page number that the scan record doesn't confirm: the scan says \"na\" or nothing.\n411:  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396.\n412:    - Example: the member `…_1910021001_0164` and the jp2 `sn82016187/100493962/1910021001/0163.jp2`.\n----\n\"\"\"IIIF crops of article clippings from the Library of Congress page scans, and the cache\nunder data/crops/ that keeps each crop once it is fetched.\"\"\"\n\nimport hashlib\nimport os\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom time import monotonic, sleep\n\nimport httpx\n\nIIIF = \"https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif\"\nBATCH_PATH = re.compile(\n    r\"/data/batches/(?P<batch>[^/]+)/data/(?P<lccn>[^/]+)/(?P<reel>[^/]+)\"\n    r\"/(?P<issue>[^/]+)/(?P<seq>[^/.]+)\\.jp2$\"\n)\n# a faro member: date, page, LCCN, reel (sometimes 'no_reel'), issue and sequence\nMEMBER = re.compile(\n    r\"(?P<date>\\d{4}-\\d\\d-\\d\\d)_p[^_]*_(?P<lccn>[^_]+)_(?P<reel>.+)\"\n    r\"_(?P<issue>\\d{10})_(?P<seq>\\d+)(?:\\.json)?$\"\n)\nCROPS = Path(__file__).parents[2] / \"data\" / \"crops\"\nUSER_AGENT = (\n    \"PaperGhosts/0.1 (a Hacktoberfest ghost-story map; github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts)\"\n)\nCLIENT = httpx.Client(timeout=60, follow_redirects=True)\nlast_request = 0.0  # monotonic time of the last request to the Library of Congress\nBUSY = {429, 500, 502, 503, 504, 520, 521, 522, 523, 524}  # 52x: Cloudflare's\n# seconds between requests: loc.gov's JSON API allows 20 a minute and blocks for an hour past\n# that, and its image services allow 150 a minute\nGAPS = {\"www.loc.gov\": 3.5}\n\n\ndef service_id(raw_data_loc: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from the batch path AmericanStories records for its scan.\"\"\"\n    path = BATCH_PATH.search(raw_data_loc)\n    if path is None:\n        raise ValueError(\"raw_data_loc is not a Chronicling America batch path\")\n    awardee = path[\"batch\"].split(\"_\")[0]\n    return (\n        f\"service:ndnp:{awardee}:batch_{path['batch']}:data:\"\n        f\"{path['lccn']}:{path['reel']}:{path['issue']}:{path['seq']}\"\n    )\n\n\ndef crop_urls(service: str, boxes: list[dict]) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"One crop per box, in the scan's own pixels at half size, in bbox_list's order, which\n    is the order the article is read in. One crop over every box would take in the columns\n    between them.\"\"\"\n    return [\n        f\"{IIIF}/{service}/{b['x0']},{b['y0']},{b['x1'] - b['x0']},{b['y1'] - b['y0']}\"\n        \"/pct:50/0/default.jpg\"\n        for b in boxes\n    ]\n\n\ndef get(url, **params):\n    \"\"\"A GET to the Library of Congress: at most one a second, or one in 3.5 s to loc.gov's\n    JSON API, naming the project, and asked again after a pause while the server is busy.\n    tile.loc.gov can answer a crop it hasn't made yet with a 503.\"\"\"\n    global last_request\n    gap = GAPS.get(httpx.URL(url).host, 1.0)\n    for pause in (5, 20, None):\n        sleep(max(0.0, last_request + gap - monotonic()))\n        last_request = monotonic()\n        try:\n            response = CLIENT.get(\n                url, params=params, headers={\"User-Agent\": USER_AGENT}\n            )\n        except httpx.TransportError:\n            if pause is None:\n                raise\n        else:\n            if response.status_code not in BUSY or pause is None:\n                response.raise_for_status()\n                return response\n        sleep(pause)\n\n\ndef page_service(member: str, scan: dict) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service, from its batch path, or else from the loc.gov item that\n    lists the page, since some scans have no batch path (decision 18).\"\"\"\n    if scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n        return service_id(scan[\"raw_data_loc\"])\n    page = MEMBER.search(member)\n    if page is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"{member} is not a faro page name\")\n    url = f\"https://www.loc.gov/item/{page['lccn']}/{page['date']}/ed-{int(page['issue'][-2:])}/\"\n    try:\n        item = get(url, fo=\"json\").text\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404:\n            raise\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov has no item for {member}\") from exc\n    found = re.search(\n        rf\"service:ndnp:[a-z]+:batch_\\w+?:data:{page['lccn']}:{page['reel']}\"\n        rf\":{page['issue']}:{page['seq']}\",\n        item,\n    )\n    if found is None:\n        raise LookupError(f\"loc.gov lists no IIIF service for {member}\")\n    return found[0]\n\n\ndef batch(service: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The LoC batch that holds the page, from its IIIF service.\"\"\"\n    return re.search(r\":batch_(\\w+?):data:\", service)[1]\n\n\ndef crop(url: str) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"The crop at url, from the cache, which is keyed by the URL, or fetched once into it.\"\"\"\n    path = CROPS / f\"{hashlib.sha256(url.encode()).hexdigest()[:24]}.jpg\"\n    if not path.exists():\n        response = get(url)\n        if not response.headers.get(\"content-type\", \"\").startswith(\"image/\"):\n            raise ValueError(f\"tile.loc.gov sent no image for {url}\")\n        path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        partial = path.with_name(f\"{path.name}.{os.getpid()}.partial\")\n        partial.write_bytes(response.content)\n        partial.replace(path)\n    return path\n\n\ndef crops_for(member: str, scan: dict, boxes: list[dict], service: str | None = None):\n    \"\"\"The page's IIIF service and its crops, one per box. A batch path can name a batch\n    that LoC has since reissued (ver01 where it now serves ver02), so when a crop from it is\n    missing, loc.gov names the page's current service.\"\"\"\n    service = service or page_service(member, scan)\n    try:\n        return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]\n    except httpx.HTTPStatusError as exc:\n        if exc.response.status_code != 404 or not scan.get(\"raw_data_loc\"):\n            raise\n    service = page_service(member, {})\n    return service, [crop(url) for url in crop_urls(service, boxes)]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"03935a15-e28a-4794-8a67-a789be38fa56","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7636bb84-79b7-4150-8840-c11526cd52ee","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
