ant","uuid":"25e4a97b-f595-43a5-a0cc-1ac8b8ffdc58","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:35:28.020Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"25e4a97b-f595-43a5-a0cc-1ac8b8ffdc58","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01My5jjFaCu6t29aHLwEFaBN","type":"tool_result","content":"# Resume\n\nWhere the build stands, for whoever picks it up next. The spec is `BRIEF.md`, the build order is `BUILD-PLAN.md`, and the reasons behind each choice are in `DECISIONS.md`. Each milestone ends with a STATUS block below, newest first.\n\nHard date: the site must be live on Oct 31.\n\n## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), on branch `phase-2b-data-layer`.\n- **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n  - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.\n  - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.\n- **Step 2B.2 is built with the EM's review changes**, and waits on the gate review (decision 34):\n  - the title parser, the loc.gov title records and the title lookup\n  - the GeoNames geocoder, over the US, Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands dumps\n  - the record check, which checks each paper's place against its title record's county\n- **Step 2B.3,** the reel-to-batch map and the page check, follows.\n- Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31).\n\nNeeds the owner's yes when we get there:\n- the Render deploy\n- domain DNS\n\n## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read, EDA and lexicon v2 (2026-10-30)\n  - **With the record check, 196 are right: 98.0% (95.0–99.2%).** 198 resolve, and 196 of those are right: 99.0% (96.4–99.7%).\n    - The check settles East Saginaw, under Saginaw, and Clifton, as a ghost town.\n    - **It leaves 2 wrong pins, one more than without it:**\n      - Bloomington still. loc.gov's own record puts Bloomington in Story County: it names Story and Muscatine, so the check agrees with the wrong Bloomington. Its record can't catch it.\n      - Norfolk and Portsmouth, which the check adds. The record names no county and gives Portsmouth as its place, so the unchecked rule pins Portsmouth, about 2 km from Norfolk. Its notes say the paper was published in both. I kept my expected answer, Norfolk, from the title.\n    - No printed place that resolved was replaced.\n  - What the records made of the 200:\n\n    | Outcome | Papers |\n    |---|---|\n    | agrees | 177 |\n    | has no county to check: independent cities, D.C., Alaska and Ponce | 14 |\n    | can't be checked: Connecticut's planning regions, and Seward | 4 |\n    | found what the printed place didn't: East Saginaw | 1 |\n    | a ghost town in the record's county: Clifton | 1 |\n    | found what the printed place didn't, unchecked: Norfolk and Portsmouth | 1 |\n    | disagrees, and its own place isn't in GeoNames: Lardo and New Oregon | 2 |\n\n  - Only one of the three merged towns is catalogued under its successor: East Saginaw, under Saginaw.\n    - The Long Valley advocate's record names Lardo and Roseberry, in Idaho County, its county then. GeoNames has Roseberry and McCall in Valley County.\n    - New Oregon's record names New Oregon itself, which GeoNames doesn't have.\n    - Both stay as no point, which is the safe failure.\n  - Some are right under an old name or a merger: Allegheny is Pittsburgh, and Daytona is Daytona Beach. Fort Wrangel, Sumterville, North Yakima and Langston City are old names their towns list.\n  - **The failures, by kind:**\n\n    | Kind | Without the check | With it | Cases |\n    |---|---|---|---|\n    | merged into a town that doesn't list its name | 3 | 2 | East Saginaw into Saginaw, which the check settles; Lardo into McCall; New Oregon into Cresco |\n    | renamed, with its old name now another town's | 1 | 1 | Bloomington, Iowa, Muscatine's name until 1849: a wrong pin either way, on a living Bloomington in Story County |\n    | two towns named as one place | 1 | 1 | \"Norfolk and Portsmouth, Va.\": no point without the check, and a pin on Portsmouth with it |\n    | a ghost town filed outside populated places | 1 | 0 | Clifton, S.D., which GeoNames has as \"Clifton (historical)\" in class S |\n    | outside GeoNames' US dump | 0 | 0 | Ponce, P.R., right since the Puerto Rico dump became an input |\n\n  - **These 200 are in-sample for the check.** Its fixes come from their failures, through the EM's review, and so do two of its rules. 2D measures it, and any further fix, on a fresh draw (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n- **The 24 judged reports' story places,** as their text gives them: an early look at what the reader will extract.\n  - The text gives a town and a state for only 3. The geocoder puts all 3 right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 name a town but no state. Datelines like \"CHICAGO, Jan. 1\" are the usual case.\n  - 8 name no town at all, or only a venue such as \"the National Theater\".\n  - 4 are abroad: Jersey, Peking, Blickling and France.\n  - **For the 9 with a town only, the paper's own state is a poor guess:**\n    - right for 3, the local stories at Middlebury, Waterloo and Chittenden\n109:### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n164:  - `reel.json`: the archive chart\n179:  - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.\n181:  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).\n222:- stories by outcome, precomputed for the reel so that outcome needs no index (rule 4)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"40d72a73-c872-4419-a1e8-ce844b163b31","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:35:29.132Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Resume\n\nWhere the build stands, for whoever picks it up next. The spec is `BRIEF.md`, the build order is `BUILD-PLAN.md`, and the reasons behind each choice are in `DECISIONS.md`. Each milestone ends with a STATUS block below, newest first.\n\nHard date: the site must be live on Oct 31.\n\n## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), on branch `phase-2b-data-layer`.\n- **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n  - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.\n  - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.\n- **Step 2B.2 is built with the EM's review changes**, and waits on the gate review (decision 34):\n  - the title parser, the loc.gov title records and the title lookup\n  - the GeoNames geocoder, over the US, Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands dumps\n  - the record check, which checks each paper's place against its title record's county\n- **Step 2B.3,** the reel-to-batch map and the page check, follows.\n- Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31).\n\nNeeds the owner's yes when we get there:\n- the Render deploy\n- domain DNS\n\n## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read, EDA and lexicon v2 (2026-10-30)\n  - **With the record check, 196 are right: 98.0% (95.0–99.2%).** 198 resolve, and 196 of those are right: 99.0% (96.4–99.7%).\n    - The check settles East Saginaw, under Saginaw, and Clifton, as a ghost town.\n    - **It leaves 2 wrong pins, one more than without it:**\n      - Bloomington still. loc.gov's own record puts Bloomington in Story County: it names Story and Muscatine, so the check agrees with the wrong Bloomington. Its record can't catch it.\n      - Norfolk and Portsmouth, which the check adds. The record names no county and gives Portsmouth as its place, so the unchecked rule pins Portsmouth, about 2 km from Norfolk. Its notes say the paper was published in both. I kept my expected answer, Norfolk, from the title.\n    - No printed place that resolved was replaced.\n  - What the records made of the 200:\n\n    | Outcome | Papers |\n    |---|---|\n    | agrees | 177 |\n    | has no county to check: independent cities, D.C., Alaska and Ponce | 14 |\n    | can't be checked: Connecticut's planning regions, and Seward | 4 |\n    | found what the printed place didn't: East Saginaw | 1 |\n    | a ghost town in the record's county: Clifton | 1 |\n    | found what the printed place didn't, unchecked: Norfolk and Portsmouth | 1 |\n    | disagrees, and its own place isn't in GeoNames: Lardo and New Oregon | 2 |\n\n  - Only one of the three merged towns is catalogued under its successor: East Saginaw, under Saginaw.\n    - The Long Valley advocate's record names Lardo and Roseberry, in Idaho County, its county then. GeoNames has Roseberry and McCall in Valley County.\n    - New Oregon's record names New Oregon itself, which GeoNames doesn't have.\n    - Both stay as no point, which is the safe failure.\n  - Some are right under an old name or a merger: Allegheny is Pittsburgh, and Daytona is Daytona Beach. Fort Wrangel, Sumterville, North Yakima and Langston City are old names their towns list.\n  - **The failures, by kind:**\n\n    | Kind | Without the check | With it | Cases |\n    |---|---|---|---|\n    | merged into a town that doesn't list its name | 3 | 2 | East Saginaw into Saginaw, which the check settles; Lardo into McCall; New Oregon into Cresco |\n    | renamed, with its old name now another town's | 1 | 1 | Bloomington, Iowa, Muscatine's name until 1849: a wrong pin either way, on a living Bloomington in Story County |\n    | two towns named as one place | 1 | 1 | \"Norfolk and Portsmouth, Va.\": no point without the check, and a pin on Portsmouth with it |\n    | a ghost town filed outside populated places | 1 | 0 | Clifton, S.D., which GeoNames has as \"Clifton (historical)\" in class S |\n    | outside GeoNames' US dump | 0 | 0 | Ponce, P.R., right since the Puerto Rico dump became an input |\n\n  - **These 200 are in-sample for the check.** Its fixes come from their failures, through the EM's review, and so do two of its rules. 2D measures it, and any further fix, on a fresh draw (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n- **The 24 judged reports' story places,** as their text gives them: an early look at what the reader will extract.\n  - The text gives a town and a state for only 3. The geocoder puts all 3 right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 name a town but no state. Datelines like \"CHICAGO, Jan. 1\" are the usual case.\n  - 8 name no town at all, or only a venue such as \"the National Theater\".\n  - 4 are abroad: Jersey, Peking, Blickling and France.\n  - **For the 9 with a town only, the paper's own state is a poor guess:**\n    - right for 3, the local stories at Middlebury, Waterloo and Chittenden\n109:### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n164:  - `reel.json`: the archive chart\n179:  - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.\n181:  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).\n222:- stories by outcome, precomputed for the reel so that outcome needs no index (rule 4)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"760874c9-0854-4792-84a0-a66e093c6019","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":4,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":6},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"priva