{"parentUuid":"bc5545a8-1c3c-440b-b329-5f361dd826c9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZNwRmC1q9j7R2dAx1XQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"About 32 answers cached so far, out of roughly 80. Drafting decision 35's map section while it finishes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_read_input_tokens":293272,"output_tokens":1423,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":100},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1524,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1423,"cache_read_input_tokens":293272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1524},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"8edebfe7-fca9-476e-b64d-cfe648c1d91a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZNwQtrSpBQuXBAE9daJ","requestRef":"dc283fd5-576b-4cc5-9d32-75d34703ec85","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d5a2216-0e01-432d-9d2c-2eb29f64f272","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:36:38.496Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"5d5a2216-0e01-432d-9d2c-2eb29f64f272","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZNwRmC1q9j7R2dAx1XQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018DSjDUJ5Hduz3XhM6J4oqz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-map.md","content":"- **The map** (`paperghosts/ingest/reels.py`, built by `scripts/reel_map.py` into `data/reels/map.json`, 10.6 MB): each LCCN and reel, the batches its pages' batch paths name, and the issues each batch holds there.\n  - Its source is the 1,101,110 pages with a batch path, of the 1,586,714 distinct pages among the candidates and samples: 24,620 reels and 742,015 issues. A reel is keyed by its LCCN and reel number, as decision 29 counted.\n  - The batch path's reel and issue file a page, never its member name's.\n  - It asks loc.gov nothing, and takes 26 s.\n- **Coverage, reconciled with decision 31** (`eval/results/phase2b/reels.json`):\n  - From the candidates' batch paths alone, the map reproduces decision 31 exactly: 367,251 of the 395,068 candidates with no batch path (93.0%) sit on a reel it holds, and 27,817 on 1,258 reels don't.\n  - The samples' batch paths add 589 reels. With them, 370,949 are covered (93.9%), and 24,119 on 1,000 reels aren't.\n  - 6,530 of those 24,119 have no reel in their member name (\"no_reel\"), so no reel map can place them.\n- **The rule** (`reels.pick`), for a page with no batch path:\n  - A reel with one batch gives it.\n  - A reel with several gives the batch whose issue is nearest the page's in date. A tie goes to the batch with more of the reel's issues.\n  - A reissued batch stands at its latest version, ver02 over ver01. A version can come without an underscore: one batch is `ncu_frankenver01`.\n  - The batch path wins wherever it exists. The map is only for pages with none.\n- **The hidden-issue check:** every issue on every reel was hidden in turn, all its pages at once, and its batch picked from the rest of its reel.\n  - 740,969 issues could be tested. The 1,046 reels that hold a single issue can't be.\n  - **Overall, 739,317 are right: 99.78% (99.77–99.79%).** Every page on a reel with one batch is right.\n  - **On the 257 flagged reels, 9,616 of 11,268: 85.3% (84.7–86.0%).** By batch name, with a reissue's versions taken as one, 10,594: 94.0% (93.6–94.4%).\n  - All 1,652 misses are on flagged reels. 978 are a reissue's other version, and 674 another batch.\n  - By page, flagged reels' pages are right for 13,439 of 16,324 (82.3%), and their candidates for 11,102 of 13,677 (81.2%).\n  - 173 issues lie in two batches.\n- **Flagged reels: 257**, each in `reels.json` with its batches' date ranges and its candidates with no batch path. 5,232 such candidates sit on them.\n  - 62 are reissues: one batch name, two or more versions. Their versions alternate along the reel. Half their issues (978 of 1,958) have the older version's batch path.\n  - 195 are splits between batch names. 127 are interleaved over the same years, 53 follow one another, and 15 are one batch under two awardee codes (`cohi_` and `ohi_`, such as `cohi_dearfield` and `ohi_dearfield`).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_read_input_tokens":293272,"output_tokens":1423,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":100},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1524,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1423,"cache_read_input_tokens":293272,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1524,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1524},"type":"message