{"parentUuid":"868f48be-81f4-4eaf-8750-1cd6cd8aa846","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZP3MvApC7hSnmZoKF4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Drafting decision 35's code section, which doesn't depend on the measurements, while the last answers come in."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":301658,"output_tokens":914,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":301658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"481e05f1-6a76-4845-9bcd-173e6d5adb7f","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZP3M7ZAon7nfhs23RzZ","requestRef":"f7425e6e-73da-4551-bca4-b1398c719955","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b890214e-1bd2-4c14-8eeb-40a07500c50d","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:38:00.190Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"b890214e-1bd2-4c14-8eeb-40a07500c50d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZP3MvApC7hSnmZoKF4p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014iZBEPUhUi332GQmmj3iGa","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-code.md","content":"- **`page_service`** (`paperghosts/ingest/crops.py`) now finds a page's IIIF service in three ways:\n  1. from its batch path, as before;\n  2. or else from its reel's batch in the map, which asks nothing;\n  3. or else from loc.gov's item for its issue.\n  - The item is asked for once per issue and cached, so the issue's other pages are found without asking. No lookup ran for the 24,119 candidates the map doesn't cover.\n  - A page it locates without a batch path is unchecked. `crops_for` checks it before any crop is fetched.\n- **The cache** (`crops.cached`): every answer from the Library of Congress is cached under `data/loc/requests/`, keyed by its URL, with its URL, retrieval date and status.\n  - A 404 is cached. A server error that outlasts `get`'s retries isn't, so a later run asks again.\n  - `loc.title_record` uses it too, so title records keep their own folder but lose their own copy of the code.\n  - `crops.SENT` counts every request `get` sends, by host, each retry included.\n- **A fix found on the way:** when a batch path's batch has been reissued, `crops_for` asks loc.gov for the page's current service. It used to look for the member's frame there, which differs from the batch path's in 2.5% of candidates (decision 33). It now looks for the batch path's own frame.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":301658,"output_tokens":914,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":264},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":914,"cache_read_input_tokens":301658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014iZBEPUhUi332GQmmj3iGa":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-code.md","content":"- **`page_service`** (`paperghosts/ingest/crops.py`) now finds a page's IIIF service in three ways:\n  1. from its batch path, as before;\n  2. or else from its reel's batch in the map, which asks nothing;\n  3. or else from loc.gov's item for its issue.\n  - The item is asked for once per issue and cached, so the issue's other pages are found without asking. No lookup ran for the 24,119 candidates the map doesn't cover.\n  - A page it locates without a batch path is unchecked. `crops_for` checks it before any crop is fetched.\n- **The cache** (`crops.cached`): every answer from the Library of Congress is cached under `data/loc/requests/`, keyed by its URL, with its URL, retrieval date and status.\n  - A 404 is cached. A server error that outlasts `get`'s retries isn't, so a later run asks again.\n  - `loc.title_record` uses it too, so title records keep their own folder but lose their own copy of the code.\n  - `crops.SENT` counts every request `get` sends, by host, each retry included.\n- **A fix found on the way:** when a batch path's batch has been reissued, `crops_for` asks loc.gov for the page's current service. It used to look for the member's frame there, which differs from the batch path's in 2.5% of candidates (decision 33). It now looks for the batch path's own frame.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"481e05f1-6a76-4845-9bcd-173e6d5adb7f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZP3M7ZAon7nfhs23RzZ","requestRef":"f7425e6e-73da-4551-bca4-b1398c719955","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"760dcb05-289b-48dd-be07-f58fd869040b","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:38:05.709Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
