{"parentUuid":"878080e8-1780-421b-8591-e1d8a5cbbc95","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZPzeS8xaTS6nnux8f7i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SgMPRndc71S3Ug7d4kYyRv","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-frames.md","content":"- **Where a page's member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).** This reverses decision 33's rule for the frame, and changing it is the EM's call.\n  - Calibration drew 20 candidate pages whose member names another frame or reel than their batch path (seed \"2B.3 calibrate\"). 18 differ only in the frame, and 2 in the reel. Each was checked on the page its member names, in its batch path's batch.\n  - All 18 member frames have exactly the scan's recorded size, and the article's words lie inside its boxes on them: 0.31 to 1.00 of its distinct words of five letters or more, 0.78 at the median.\n  - The `frames` run then checked the batch path's own frame for the same 18. None has the recorded size, and the article's words aren't in its boxes: 0 to 0.11.\n  - The size isn't chance. In the 15 batches that hold most of these pages, a page's neighbouring frames never share its size (0 of about 115 pairs of agreeing pages).\n  - It's systematic, batch by batch, and mostly in `dlc_` batches. In `dlc_earl_ver02`, 1,120 of its 1,147 pages have a member frame one above the batch path's. 202 batches hold such pages, and 10 hold 39% of them.\n  - So where they differ, the stored `service` (`printings.py`, from the batch path) names the frame before the article's page. That's up to 20,643 candidates (2.5% of those with both, decision 33).\n  - **Proposed, not done:** take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member. Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the evidence goes the other way: the member's reel holds the member's issue in only 12 of 411 pages, so the batch path's page stands there, checked before its crop is shown.\n  - `crops_for`'s fallback for a reissued batch looks up the member's frame, as it did before.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1370,"cache_read_input_tokens":372787,"output_tokens":1119,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":260},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1370,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1119,"cache_read_input_tokens":372787,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1370,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1370},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SgMPRndc71S3Ug7d4kYyRv":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-frames.md","content":"- **Where a page's member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).** This reverses decision 33's rule for the frame, and changing it is the EM's call.\n  - Calibration drew 20 candidate pages whose member names another frame or reel than their batch path (seed \"2B.3 calibrate\"). 18 differ only in the frame, and 2 in the reel. Each was checked on the page its member names, in its batch path's batch.\n  - All 18 member frames have exactly the scan's recorded size, and the article's words lie inside its boxes on them: 0.31 to 1.00 of its distinct words of five letters or more, 0.78 at the median.\n  - The `frames` run then checked the batch path's own frame for the same 18. None has the recorded size, and the article's words aren't in its boxes: 0 to 0.11.\n  - The size isn't chance. In the 15 batches that hold most of these pages, a page's neighbouring frames never share its size (0 of about 115 pairs of agreeing pages).\n  - It's systematic, batch by batch, and mostly in `dlc_` batches. In `dlc_earl_ver02`, 1,120 of its 1,147 pages have a member frame one above the batch path's. 202 batches hold such pages, and 10 hold 39% of them.\n  - So where they differ, the stored `service` (`printings.py`, from the batch path) names the frame before the article's page. That's up to 20,643 candidates (2.5% of those with both, decision 33).\n  - **Proposed, not done:** take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member. Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the evidence goes the other way: the member's reel holds the member's issue in only 12 of 411 pages, so the batch path's page stands there, checked before its crop is shown.\n  - `crops_for`'s fallback for a reissued batch looks up the member's frame, as it did before.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"69d40cb4-d6c5-4418-96ef-e74b554661ae","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZPzdjiTs8Wbb7GaP6ff","requestRef":"d169e3c8-6fa7-4337-bd7c-16ca69eabdf5","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"ee98d8cd-e694-48cc-9d99-4fcd8254de00","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:50:37.777Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
