0-31T00:50:59.331Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2c61f6dd-5475-4d1b-8d38-8544490f4332","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H4cGGLAemfkdiTN1gGjuKe","type":"tool_result","content":"- **Gold set:**\n  - 150–300 candidates, stratified by decade and lexicon term and including near-miss items.\n  - Frozen before any training: the split and its hash are committed under `eval/gold/`.\n  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\n  - The labelling rules for hard cases (séance reports, reprinted fiction, hoax exposures, humour columns) are written in `eval/gold/POLICY.md` before labelling starts.\n- **Training data:** the teacher labels a separate pool. No gold article, and no reprint of a gold article, may appear in it.\n- **Model selection** happens on a dev split. The gold set is touched only for final evaluations.\n- **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n\n### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n**`reports`:** one document per story.\n- `_id`, which is `r_` plus the primary article ID, and `primary_article_id`, the earliest printing's\n- `printings[]`: compact references (decision 32, rule 6), built by `paperghosts/store/printings.py`. Each has:\n  - article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state and date\n  - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.\n  - page, from the scan record only, when it has one\n  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).\n  - `bbox_list`\n\n  Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own.\n- `headline` and `text`, the OCR of the primary printing, untouched\n  - v2's `data/samples`: 563 MiB\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850 under both lexicons. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the manifest.\n- `make eval-v1` reproduces eval A's v1 record byte for byte, apart from `generated_at`.\n- Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md`, with Temporal UI screenshots from before and after (`kill-test-1-*.png`).\n- Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 is AmericanStories' stray box, recorded as a known limitation (decision 29), and #50 is a 1964 page with no loc.gov item.\n- The EM's spot check of v1, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:\n  - every candidate's term is in its text\n  - none of the 10 non-candidates is a report\n  - 1 of the 20 candidates is a report, in line with 3.5%\n\nRisks and open questions:\n- **The ouija rule stays.** None of its 6 sampled candidates is a report (0–39%). The EM kept it, and 2C's term strata measure it (decision 31).\n- Each new rule's marginal yield rests on 0 to 4 reports, so its interval is wide (decision 31).\n- v2's 84% recall is in-sample. The screen behind both lexicons' recall rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Even with their lexicon terms masked, it would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports.\n- v2's gain rests on 14 reports in 200, 2 of them borderline.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle these cases:\n  - delusions and hallucinations\n  - spirit control and a felt presence of the dead\n  - decision 31's two borderline kinds\n- 27,817 of v2's candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\n- The reader's job is 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's. The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"51319f3b-b3ad-463a-b88d-671d7a253d81","timestamp":"2026-10-31T00:50:59.958Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"- **Gold set:**\n  - 150–300 candidates, stratified by decade and lexicon term and including near-miss items.\n  - Frozen before any training: the split and its hash are committed under `eval/gold/`.\n  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\n  - The labelling rules for hard cases (séance reports, reprinted fiction, hoax exposures, humour columns) are written in `eval/gold/POLICY.md` before labelling starts.\n- **Training data:** the teacher labels a separate pool. No gold article, and no reprint of a gold article, may appear in it.\n- **Model selection** happens on a dev split. The gold set is touched only for final evaluations.\n- **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n\n### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n**`reports`:** one document per story.\n- `_id`, which is `r_` plus the primary article ID, and `primary_article_id`, the earliest printing's\n- `printings[]`: compact references (decision 32, rule 6), built by `paperghosts/store/printings.py`. Each has:\n  - article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state and date\n  - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.\n  - page, from the scan record only, when it has one\n  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).\n  - `bbox_list`\n\n  Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own.\n- `headline` and `text`, the OCR of the primary printing, untouched\n  - v2's `data/samples`: 563 MiB\n- `make ingest YEARS=1850` reproduces 1850 under both lexicons. With its candidates moved aside, a rerun wrote all three outputs byte-identical, with the sha256 in the manifest.\n- `make eval-v1` reproduces eval A's v1 record byte for byte, apart from `generated_at`.\n- Kill-test evidence: `eval/results/phase2a/kill-test-1.md`, with Temporal UI screenshots from before and after (`kill-test-1-*.png`).\n- Both crop-check failures are explained: #21 is AmericanStories' stray box, recorded as a known limitation (decision 29), and #50 is a 1964 page with no loc.gov item.\n- The EM's spot check of v1, seed \"EM spot-check 2A\", read 20 random candidates and 10 random non-candidates against their stored text:\n  - every candidate's term is in its text\n  - none of the 10 non-candidates is a report\n  - 1 of the 20 candidates is a report, in line with 3.5%\n\nRisks and open questions:\n- **The ouija rule stays.** None of its 6 sampled candidates is a report (0–39%). The EM kept it, and 2C's term strata measure it (decision 31).\n- Each new rule's marginal yield rests on 0 to 4 reports, so its interval is wide (decision 31).\n- v2's 84% recall is in-sample. The screen behind both lexicons' recall rests on 4 reports, 2 of them borderline. Even with their lexicon terms masked, it would still catch only 5 of eval A's 7 reports.\n- v2's gain rests on 14 reports in 200, 2 of them borderline.\n- `POLICY.md` (2C) has to settle these cases:\n  - delusions and hallucinations\n  - spirit control and a felt presence of the dead\n  - decision 31's two borderline kinds\n- 27,817 of v2's candidates need loc.gov to name their page's IIIF service, and its JSON API allows 20 requests a minute. 2B looks them up only for reports (decision 29).\n- The reader's job is 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's. The Tinker credit check weighs that before the full pass.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"53792eb9-a4ea-4d58-9862-9a1a7a39837b","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":7},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"2c61f6dd-5475-4d1b-8d38-8544490f4332","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
