{"parentUuid":"7085e418-c03a-464b-934d-b1d4227848d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZQtaXgDgs9PMkV4Z4sm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":385035,"output_tokens":1046,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":211},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":385035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2190,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"19e3f763-6558-47bc-9ec2-c4ff063e95a4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZQtZi4p8E8qkNgevHVV","requestRef":"12327515-c0ac-4d54-8ba3-47acf208dfac","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"2036bc54-0cac-4f38-b324-c368fb954379","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:02:13.877Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"2036bc54-0cac-4f38-b324-c368fb954379","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZQtaXgDgs9PMkV4Z4sm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019sJa9ybqC1iPbbRVQ8UMkF","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-check.md","content":"- **The page check** (`crops.page_check`), for a page located without a batch path, before its crop is shown. `crops_for` runs it, and fetches no crop for a page it rejects.\n  1. The page has to exist: `info.json` answers. A batch that doesn't hold the page answers 404, so a wrong batch is caught here, and loc.gov then names the right one.\n  2. It has to be the scan's recorded size. Where AmericanStories marks the size approximate, which is only the extent of the boxes (decision 18), the boxes have to lie on the page instead. That's 19% of the candidates' pages with no batch path.\n  3. LoC's OCR of the page, its ALTO, has to hold the article's words inside the article's boxes: at least a fifth of its distinct words of five letters or more. An article with fewer than 10 such words can't be checked, and isn't shown.\n  - The ALTO sits beside the image (`tile.loc.gov/storage-services/…/{frame}.xml`), about 1 MB a page. The cache keeps only its words and their boxes.\n- **The text rule came from calibration's 38 pages.**\n  - Words anywhere on the page don't separate the two: 0.37 to 1.0 on the article's page, and up to 0.5 on the frame beside it.\n  - The article's words inside its boxes do: 0.31 to 1.0 on its page, and 0 to 0.11 on the frame beside it. A fifth sits in the gap.\n- **Measuring it** needed a truth the check doesn't decide. The EM's design took pages whose member names another frame as wrong pages, but those turned out to be the article's pages (see the frame finding). So the measurement draws:\n  - 90 other candidate pages whose member and batch path agree, two sources naming one frame: 45 of exact size and 45 approximate (seed \"2B.3 measure\").\n  - Each is checked on its own frame, which should pass, and on the frame beside it in its batch, one up or down at random, which should fail. The article is the same, and so is its scan's recorded size.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_read_input_tokens":385035,"output_tokens":1046,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":211},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1046,"cache_read_input_tokens":385035,"cache_creation_input_tokens":759,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":759},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019sJa9ybqC1iPbbRVQ8UMkF":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b3/decision35-check.md","content":"- **The page check** (`crops.page_check`), for a page located without a batch path, before its crop is shown. `crops_for` runs it, and fetches no crop for a page it rejects.\n  1. The page has to exist: `info.json` answers. A batch that doesn't hold the page answers 404, so a wrong batch is caught here, and loc.gov then names the right one.\n  2. It has to be the scan's recorded size. Where AmericanStories marks the size approximate, which is only the extent of the boxes (decision 18), the boxes have to lie on the page instead. That's 19% of the candidates' pages with no batch path.\n  3. LoC's OCR of the page, its ALTO, has to hold the article's words inside the article's boxes: at least a fifth of its distinct words of five letters or more. An article with fewer than 10 such words can't be checked, and isn't shown.\n  - The ALTO sits beside the image (`tile.loc.gov/storage-services/…/{frame}.xml`), about 1 MB a page. The cache keeps only its words and their boxes.\n- **The text rule came from calibration's 38 pages.**\n  - Words anywhere on the page don't separate the two: 0.37 to 1.0 on the article's page, and up to 0.5 on the frame beside it.\n  - The article's words inside its boxes do: 0.31 to 1.0 on its page, and 0 to 0.11 on the frame beside it. A fifth sits in the gap.\n- **Measuring it** needed a truth the check doesn't decide. The EM's design took pages whose member names another frame as wrong pages, but those turned out to be the article's pages (see the frame finding). So the measurement draws:\n  - 90 other candidate pages whose member and batch path agree, two sources naming one frame: 45 of exact size and 45 approximate (seed \"2B.3 measure\").\n  - Each is checked on its own frame, which should pass, and on the frame beside it in its batch, one up or down at random, which should fail. The article is the same, and so is its scan's recorded size.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"19e3f763-6558-47bc-9ec2-c4ff063e95a4","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZQtZi4p8E8qkNgevHVV","requestRef":"12327515-c0ac-4d54-8ba3-47acf208dfac","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a9176c5b-747d-4471-be86-2d64c79c4850","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:02:21.332Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
