icle's words inside its boxes do: 0.31 to 1.0 on its page, and 0 to 0.11 on the frame beside it. A fifth sits in the gap.\n- **Measuring it** needed a truth the check doesn't decide. The EM's design took pages whose member names another frame as wrong pages, but those turned out to be the article's pages (see the frame finding). So the measurement draws:\n  - 90 other candidate pages whose member and batch path agree, two sources naming one frame: 45 of exact size and 45 approximate (seed \"2B.3 measure\").\n  - Each is checked on its own frame, which should pass, and on the frame beside it in its batch, one up or down at random, which should fail. The article is the same, and so is its scan's recorded size.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a9176c5b-747d-4471-be86-2d64c79c4850","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
