{"parentUuid":"bee9f140-3549-40ab-b71b-53f27e38ef41","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RhVx6pd9J5CZ4SnEUTAYdp","type":"tool_result","content":"     563 Docs/DECISIONS.md\n\n    | Kind | Without the check | With it | Cases |\n    |---|---|---|---|\n    | merged into a town that doesn't list its name | 3 | 2 | East Saginaw into Saginaw, which the check settles; Lardo into McCall; New Oregon into Cresco |\n    | renamed, with its old name now another town's | 1 | 1 | Bloomington, Iowa, Muscatine's name until 1849: a wrong pin either way, on a living Bloomington in Story County |\n    | two towns named as one place | 1 | 1 | \"Norfolk and Portsmouth, Va.\": no point without the check, and a pin on Portsmouth with it |\n    | a ghost town filed outside populated places | 1 | 0 | Clifton, S.D., which GeoNames has as \"Clifton (historical)\" in class S |\n    | outside GeoNames' US dump | 0 | 0 | Ponce, P.R., right since the Puerto Rico dump became an input |\n\n  - **These 200 are in-sample for the check.** Its fixes come from their failures, through the EM's review, and so do two of its rules. 2D measures it, and any further fix, on a fresh draw (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n- **The 24 judged reports' story places,** as their text gives them: an early look at what the reader will extract.\n  - The text gives a town and a state for only 3. The geocoder puts all 3 right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 name a town but no state. Datelines like \"CHICAGO, Jan. 1\" are the usual case.\n  - 8 name no town at all, or only a venue such as \"the National Theater\".\n  - 4 are abroad: Jersey, Peking, Blickling and France.\n  - **For the 9 with a town only, the paper's own state is a poor guess:**\n    - right for 3, the local stories at Middlebury, Waterloo and Chittenden\n    - a wrong place for 2: Adamsville lands in Pennsylvania, and Easton in Indiana matches West Newton, which lists Easton as an alternate name\n    - nothing for 4: Chicago in Connecticut, Kansas and Utah papers, and Bordentown in a Michigan one\n  - **So a story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved, and it never falls back on the paper's state** (the EM's review). 2C measures the rule on its gold set, and 2D applies it (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"34f2c0d0-b77a-4d2c-a65d-fce6eb3ec1fd","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:24:13.076Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"     563 Docs/DECISIONS.md\n\n    | Kind | Without the check | With it | Cases |\n    |---|---|---|---|\n    | merged into a town that doesn't list its name | 3 | 2 | East Saginaw into Saginaw, which the check settles; Lardo into McCall; New Oregon into Cresco |\n    | renamed, with its old name now another town's | 1 | 1 | Bloomington, Iowa, Muscatine's name until 1849: a wrong pin either way, on a living Bloomington in Story County |\n    | two towns named as one place | 1 | 1 | \"Norfolk and Portsmouth, Va.\": no point without the check, and a pin on Portsmouth with it |\n    | a ghost town filed outside populated places | 1 | 0 | Clifton, S.D., which GeoNames has as \"Clifton (historical)\" in class S |\n    | outside GeoNames' US dump | 0 | 0 | Ponce, P.R., right since the Puerto Rico dump became an input |\n\n  - **These 200 are in-sample for the check.** Its fixes come from their failures, through the EM's review, and so do two of its rules. 2D measures it, and any further fix, on a fresh draw (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).\n- **The 24 judged reports' story places,** as their text gives them: an early look at what the reader will extract.\n  - The text gives a town and a state for only 3. The geocoder puts all 3 right (43.8–100%).\n  - 9 name a town but no state. Datelines like \"CHICAGO, Jan. 1\" are the usual case.\n  - 8 name no town at all, or only a venue such as \"the National Theater\".\n  - 4 are abroad: Jersey, Peking, Blickling and France.\n  - **For the 9 with a town only, the paper's own state is a poor guess:**\n    - right for 3, the local stories at Middlebury, Waterloo and Chittenden\n    - a wrong place for 2: Adamsville lands in Pennsylvania, and Easton in Indiana matches West Newton, which lists Easton as an alternate name\n    - nothing for 4: Chicago in Connecticut, Kansas and Utah papers, and Bordentown in a Michigan one\n  - **So a story place that is only a town resolves from a county or state the text gives, or from its dateline. Otherwise it stays unresolved, and it never falls back on the paper's state** (the EM's review). 2C measures the rule on its gold set, and 2D applies it (`BUILD-PLAN.md`).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"c413fedb-298f-4981-81e6-9458203f885c","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":8},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bee9f140-3549-40ab-b71b-53f27e38ef41","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
