) instead drew:","+  - 90 other candidate pages whose member and batch path agree, so two sources name the one frame: 45 of exact size and 45 approximate.","+  - Each was checked on its own frame, which should pass. It was also checked on the frame beside it in its batch, one up or down at random, which should fail. The article was the same, and so was its scan's recorded size.","+- **The page check's errors** (`eval/results/phase2b/page_check.json`, `summary`):","+  - **False accepts: 0 of 90 (0–4.1%).** 31 of the frames beside don't exist, and of the 59 that do, the check accepts none (0–6.1%).","+  - **Size alone isn't enough:**","+    - It would accept 2 of the 36 exact-size frames beside that exist (5.6%, 1.5–18.1%), more than a few percent.","+    - It would accept all 23 approximate ones, whose boxes fit.","+    - The text check rejected all 25.","+  - **False rejects: 2 of the 85 own frames that exist (2.4%, 0.6–8.2%).** That's 0 of 41 of exact size and 2 of 44 approximate.","+    - Both are the article's page, by their crops, and LoC's OCR of them is garbled: \"he ceptisady gifted. Be ad r p enlmto crew4de\" where the article reads \"…ceptionally gifted. He had performed to crowded…\". The failure is the safe kind, since no crop is shown.","+    - One of them, the Caledonian's 1856 letter, also has AmericanStories' stray box (decision 29): its first box is the paper's masthead.","+  - 5 of the 90 own frames' batches no longer serve them (`info.json` 404s). `crops_for` sends those to loc.gov.","+  - All 41 own frames of exact size have the recorded size.","+  - The rule's margin: own frames' words in their boxes are 0.87 at the median, and the lowest after the two garbled ones is 0.23. The frames beside reach 0.13.","+- **`page_service`** now finds a page's IIIF service in three ways:","+  1. from its batch path, as before;","+  2. or else from its reel's first batch in the map, which asks nothing;","+  3. or else from loc.gov's item for its issue.","+  - The item is asked for once per issue and cached, so the issue's other pages are found without asking.","+  - A page it locates without a batch path is unchecked, so crops come through `crops_for`, which checks the page.","+  - A reissued batch's fallback in `crops_for` looks up the member's frame, as before.","+- **The cache** (`crops.cached`): every answer from the Library of Congress is cached under `data/loc/requests/`, keyed by its URL, with its URL, retrieval date and status.","+  - A 404 is cached. A server error that outlasts `get`'s retries isn't, so a later run asks again.","+  - `loc.title_record` uses it too. Title records keep their own folder, and their copy of the caching code is gone.","+  - `crops.SENT` counts every request `get` sends, by host, each retry included.","+- **Requests: 549 in all, against the 600 planned,** all to tile.loc.gov, one at a time and at least 3.5 s apart. None failed, and they took about 37 minutes.","+","+  | Run | Requests | Minutes |","+  |---|---|---|","+  | probes: `info.json` and the ALTO's place | 4 | |","+  | calibrate | 77 | 6.6 |","+  | frames | 36 | 2.0 |","+  | measure | 326 | 20.8 |","+  | look: two crops | 2 | |","+  | reels | 104 | 7.0 |","+","+  - The script spaces tile.loc.gov 3.5 s apart, as this step asked. `crops.get`'s default for image services stays 1 s (decision 29).","+- **For 2D:** the check costs 2 requests and about 1 MB of ALTO for each page with no batch path whose crop is shown. At 5% reports, that's about 20,000 pages: 11 hours at 1 s a request, and about 20 GB."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"76bdbd59-5916-42cb-b59b-cf877b7b0eee","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"stat