page.** That's up to 20,643 candidates (2.5% of those with both, decision 33).","   - **Proposed, not done:** take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member.","-    - Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the evidence is thin. The map has the member's issue on the member's reel for only 12 of the 411 such pages, and both sampled ones were missing from the batch path's batch. So the batch path's page would stand there, checked before its crop is shown.","+    - Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the evidence is thin. The map has the member's issue on the member's reel for only 12 of the 411 such pages, and for both sampled ones the batch path's batch holds no page at the member's place. So the batch path's page would stand there, checked before its crop is shown."," - **The page check** (`crops.page_check`), for a page located without a batch path, before its crop is shown. `crops_for` runs it, and fetches no crop for a page it rejects.","   1. The page has to exist: `info.json` answers.","   2. It has to be the scan's recorded size."]},{"oldStart":620,"oldLines":7,"newStart":620,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - **The text rule came from calibration's 38 pages** (the 20 drawn and the 18 batch path frames):","   - The article's words anywhere on the page don't separate right from wrong: 0.37 to 1.0 on the article's page, and up to 0.5 on the frame beside it.","   - Its words inside its boxes do: 0.31 to 1.0 on its page, and 0 to 0.11 on the frame beside it. A fifth sits in the gap.","-- **Measuring the check needed a truth the check doesn't decide.** Your design took pages whose member names another frame as wrong pages, but those turned out to be the article's pages. So the measurement (seed \"2B.3 measure\") instead drew:","+- **Measuring the check needed a truth the check doesn't decide.** The EM's design took pages whose member names another frame as wrong pages, but those turned out to be the article's pages. So the measurement (seed \"2B.3 measure\") instead drew:","   - 90 other candidate pages whose member and batch path agree, so two sources name the one frame: 45 of exact size and 45 approximate.","   - Each was checked on its own frame, which should pass. It was also checked on the frame beside it in its batch, one up or down at random, which should fail. The article was the same, and so was its scan's recorded size."," - **The page check's errors** (`eval/results/phase2b/page_check.json`, `summary`):"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"2499f8f9-5d9d-4851-8c0a-b5c1a92a15be","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":8},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"822ac923-f686-4be2-84cc-3dd23ab121e9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
