{"parentUuid":"d3014ee2-bee3-4d72-90ba-f3646518e6bd","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"eb4299df-98e8-4a21-a6f8-2c287186b7f2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G4vvWnYBmc1y5ttZgZMqBw","type":"tool_result","content":"edited\nresume ok\n Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |  3 +-\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |  8 +++--\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 98 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n Docs/RESUME.md       | 12 ++++---\n 4 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), on branch `phase-2b-data-layer`.\n- **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n  - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.\n  - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.\n- **Step 2B.2 passed the EM's review** (decision 34): the title parser and lookup, the GeoNames geocoder and the record check. Norfolk and Portsmouth's rule stays.\n- **Step 2B.3 is built and waits on the gate review** (decision 35):\n  - the reel-to-batch map, its hidden-issue check, and the 257 flagged reels\n  - the page check, for a page with no batch path, before its crop is shown\n  - `page_service`'s cache\n  - **The EM's call:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member.\n- Phase 2B's PR comes when 2B closes.\n- Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31).\n\nNeeds the owner's yes when we get there:\n- the Render deploy\n- domain DNS\n\n## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read, EDA and lexicon v2 (2026-10-30)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"2063b807-ff07-4e9e-950c-ce8c5501af83","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:25:22.217Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"edited\nresume ok\n Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |  3 +-\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |  8 +++--\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 98 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n Docs/RESUME.md       | 12 ++++---\n 4 files changed, 112 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)\n## Next step\n\n**Phase 2B: schemas and data layer** (`BUILD-PLAN.md` section 4), on branch `phase-2b-data-layer`.\n- **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.\n  - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.\n  - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.\n- **Step 2B.2 passed the EM's review** (decision 34): the title parser and lookup, the GeoNames geocoder and the record check. Norfolk and Portsmouth's rule stays.\n- **Step 2B.3 is built and waits on the gate review** (decision 35):\n  - the reel-to-batch map, its hidden-issue check, and the 257 flagged reels\n  - the page check, for a page with no batch path, before its crop is shown\n  - `page_service`'s cache\n  - **The EM's call:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member.\n- Phase 2B's PR comes when 2B closes.\n- Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31).\n\nNeeds the owner's yes when we get there:\n- the Render deploy\n- domain DNS\n\n## STATUS: Phase 2A, archive read, EDA and lexicon v2 (2026-10-30)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":178,"oldLines":7,"newStart":178,"newLines":8,"lines":["   - article ID, LCCN, paper title, publication place, state and date","   - edition, reel, issue and frame, from its member name. The issue is the date and a two-digit edition.","   - page, from the scan record only, when it has one","-  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path, or else only once a check confirms the page, because a member name can point one frame off (decision 33).","+  - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path (decision 33). A page with none gets its batch from the reel-to-batch map or loc.gov, and is shown only once the page check confirms it (decision 35).","+    - Where the member name and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18 checked (decision 35). Which one the stored service follows is the EM's call.","   - `bbox_list`"," ","   Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":87,"oldLines":15,"newStart":87,"newLines":16,"lines":["   - Sample per candidate as well as per cluster. Eval A's check drew clusters uniformly, so 11 of its 20 pairs came from clusters of 2 printings, and none of the 157 clusters of 50 or more was checked.","   - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same."," - The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):","-  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 367,000 of lexicon v2's candidates (decision 31).","+  - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 367,000 of lexicon v2's candidates (decision 31), and 370,949 with the samples' batch paths (decision 35).","   - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back.","   - Flag every reel that maps to more than one batch, such as a reissued ver01 and ver02.","   - Check a page located without a batch path before its crop is shown, and measure the check's error in the validation. One way is the scan's height and width against the IIIF `info.json`, and another is its OCR.","     - The check is needed because a member name can point at the wrong page. Where a candidate has both, its member's frame differs from its batch path's in 2.5% of them, and its reel in 396 (decision 33).","     - The batch path wins wherever it exists.","-- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 27,817 candidates whose reels the map doesn't cover. At 20 a minute they would take about a day, and most won't be reports.","+    - Decision 35 found the opposite for the frame: where the two differ, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member is the EM's call.","+- No loc.gov lookups yet for the 24,119 candidates on the 1,000 reels the map doesn't cover (decision 35). At 20 a minute they would take most of a day, and most won't be reports.","   - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.","-  - Cache each answer, which `page_service` doesn't do yet, so no page is looked up twice.","+  - `page_service` caches each answer, one per issue, so no page is looked up twice (decision 35)."," "," **Gate**"," - Schema tests pass, and `make db-init` can run twice."]},{"oldStart":138,"oldLines":6,"newStart":139,"newLines":7,"lines":["   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.","   - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.","   - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.","+  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page with no batch path before its crop is shown, by its size and its OCR (decision 35).","   - Measure the record check, and any further geocoder fix, on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one such fix.","   - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever."," - `make db-verify` runs geo, fuzzy and vector queries and checks their expected results and latencies."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":10,"oldLines":11,"newStart":10,"newLines":13,"lines":[" - **Step 2B.1 passed the EM's review** (decisions 32 and 33): the models and validators, the BinData check, `make db-init` and `BUDGET.md`.","   - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.","   - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner.","-- **Step 2B.2 is built with the EM's review changes**, and waits on the gate review (decision 34):","-  - the title parser, the loc.gov title records and the title lookup","-  - the GeoNames geocoder, over the US, Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands dumps","-  - the record check, which checks each paper's place against its title record's county","-- **Step 2B.3,** the reel-to-batch map and the page check, follows.","+- **Step 2B.2 passed the EM's review** (decision 34): the title parser and lookup, the GeoNames geocoder and the record check. Norfolk and Portsmouth's rule stays.","+- **Step 2B.3 is built and waits on the gate review** (decision 35):","+  - the reel-to-batch map, its hidden-issue check, and the 257 flagged reels","+  - the page check, for a page with no batch path, before its crop is shown","+  - `page_service`'s cache","+  - **The EM's call:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member.","+- Phase 2B's PR comes when 2B closes."," - Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31)."," "," Needs the owner's yes when we get there:"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"5f2f06a6-d89a-4dc4-b373-3e8dbf31ad95","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":6,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":8},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d3014ee2-bee3-4d72-90ba-f3646518e6bd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
