{"parentUuid":"cb49a231-169a-4606-a17c-db215a244be3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZSiriiqfXfPeMsHC7hq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MkTxU7tk8NtjtNomoxt6QX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nA page with no batch path gets its batch from the map, and is checked before its crop is shown\n\n- page_service: the batch path, or else the reel's first batch in the map,\n  or else loc.gov's item for the issue, asked once per issue and cached.\n- crops.cached: every answer from the Library of Congress is cached with its\n  URL, date and status; a 404 is cached and a server error isn't.\n  loc.title_record uses it too.\n- crops.page_check: the page has to exist, be the scan's size (or hold the\n  boxes, where the size is approximate), and its ALTO has to hold the\n  article's words inside the article's boxes. crops_for runs it, tries the\n  reel's batches in turn, then loc.gov, and fetches no crop for a page it\n  rejects (decision 35).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1 && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add scripts/page_check.py tests/test_page_check.py eval/results/phase2b/page_check.json && git diff --cached --stat && git diff --cached > $S/b3/commit3.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/b3/commit3.diff && echo \"machine-name matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/b3/commit3.diff)\"","description":"Commit the page check, then stage and scan the measurement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":449982,"output_tokens":669,"output_token