{"parentUuid":"df0c941b-96eb-4713-a36b-14db67c4c6fe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZSqrU2tjCwtDxmtqEtB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Each of the three commits passes its own tests, with one skip apiece for the Atlas test, which needs a `.env` a worktree lacks. The branch tip passes all 339 and matches the remote at `dc3224f`; I'm writing the hand-over note now.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":455366,"output_tokens":2717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":628},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2717,"cache_read_input_tokens":455366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"91dec1fb-4059-4d14-816e-6cf2c040509a","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZSqqP3WFy6ZrmQSTA5j","requestRef":"6fa5164f-cb0e-4f59-85c4-1063e409db2c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"48ce0d95-19ea-4a81-b398-ea5799bc4deb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:27:55.013Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"48ce0d95-19ea-4a81-b398-ea5799bc4deb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZSqrU2tjCwtDxmtqEtB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01U8xhmvgcqgUn3NNDMD9WR3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.3.md","content":"# Step 2B.3: DONE\n\nOn `phase-2b-data-layer`. I checked origin with `git ls-remote`: it shows `dc3224f`, the same as local.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `9d52d89` | the reel-to-batch map, checked with every issue hidden in turn |\n| `28c1a08` | `page_service` takes a page's batch from the map; every loc.gov answer is cached; the page check runs before a crop is shown |\n| `40586b0` | the page check's measurement, and which batch serves a flagged reel's page |\n| `dc3224f` | decision 35, and the plan's, architecture's and resume's notes |\n\nEach commit's tests pass on its own in a clean worktree. No PR: it comes when 2B closes.\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Tests and lint:** `make test` gives 339 passed, the live `atlas` test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- **The map** (`paperghosts/ingest/reels.py`, `scripts/reel_map.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/reels.json`):\n  - From the candidates alone, it reproduces decision 31 exactly: 367,251 of the 395,068 candidates with no batch path covered (93.0%), and 27,817 on 1,258 reels not.\n  - With the samples' batch paths: 370,949 covered (93.9%), and 24,119 on 1,000 reels not. 6,530 of those have no reel in their member name.\n- **Hidden issues** (every issue hidden in turn, all its pages at once):\n  - Overall: 739,317 of 740,969 issues right, 99.78% (99.77–99.79%).\n  - Flagged reels: 9,616 of 11,268, 85.3% (84.7–86.0%), and 94.0% (93.6–94.4%) by batch name.\n  - 1,046 reels can't be tested: each holds one issue.\n- **Flagged reels:** all 257 are in `reels.json`, each with its batches' date ranges: 62 reissues and 195 splits.\n- **Which batch serves** (`info.json` on every batch, for one page with no batch path on each of 50 drawn reels):\n  - The rule's first batch serves 42, 84.0% (71.5–91.7%).\n  - Trying the reel's batches in turn serves 46, 92.0% (81.2–96.8%).\n  - 4 need loc.gov.\n  - **The rule:** the batch whose issue is nearest in date, each name's latest version first. `info.json` decides, and on a 404 the next batch, then loc.gov.\n- **The page check** (90 pages whose member and batch path agree, each checked on its own frame and on the frame beside it):\n  - **False accepts:** 0 of 90, 0.0% (0–4.1%); 0 of the 59 frames beside that exist (0–6.1%).\n  - **False rejects:** 2 of the 85 own frames that exist, 2.4% (0.6–8.2%). Both are the right page, by their crops, with LoC's OCR garbled.\n  - 5 own frames' batches no longer serve them. `crops_for` sends those to loc.gov.\n  - **Size alone** accepts 2 of 36 exact-size frames beside (5.6%, 1.5–18.1%), and all 23 approximate ones. So I added the text check: the article's words inside its boxes in LoC's ALTO, at least a fifth of them.\n- **Requests:** 549 of the 600 planned, all to tile.loc.gov, one at a time, 3.5 s apart, each cached with its URL, date and status. None failed, and they took about 37 minutes. No lookups ran for the 24,119.\n- **Decision 35** is written.\n\n## For you\n\n1. **Where a member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).**\n   - All 18 member frames have the scan's recorded size, and the article's words are inside its boxes: 0.78 at the median.\n   - None of the 18 batch path frames has the recorded size, and their scores are 0 to 0.11.\n   - It's systematic, batch by batch, mostly in `dlc_`: in `dlc_earl_ver02`, 1,120 of 1,147 pages are off by one.\n   - So the stored `service` (`printings.py`, from the batch path) names the frame before the article's page for up to 20,643 candidates.\n   - **Your call.** I'd take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member. Where the reel differs too (396 candidates), I'd keep the batch path's page and check it before its crop is shown.\n   - I haven't changed it, because your brief says the batch path wins.\n2. **Item 4's design changed because of 1.** The pages you named as ones it should reject (member differs) turned out to be right pages. So the \"should reject\" set is the frame beside each agreeing page, and the \"should accept\" set is that page itself.\n3. **The text rule's threshold (a fifth) came from calibration's 38 pages.** The 90 measured pairs are fresh: the frames beside scored at most 0.13, and own frames, apart from the two garbled ones, at least 0.23.\n4. **`page_service` now prefers the map over loc.gov.** A page it locates without a batch path is unchecked. Crops should come through `crops_for`, which checks the page. `load_skeleton.py` still builds crop URLs from `page_service` directly. It's Phase 1's, and it isn't re-run.\n5. **Cost for 2D:** 2 requests and about 1 MB of ALTO per page with no batch path whose crop is shown. That's about 20,000 pages at 5% reports: 11 hours at 1 s a request.\n6. **tile.loc.gov at 3.5 s was this step's rule, set in the script.** `crops.get`'s default for image services stays 1 s (decision 29). Say if it should be 3.5 s everywhere.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_read_input_tokens":455366,"output_tokens":2717,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":628},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2717,"cache_read_input_tokens":455366,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1022,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1022},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01U8xhmvgcqgUn3NNDMD9WR3":{"file_path":"/Users/hotragn/Library/Application Support/Claude/side-session-notes/local_98906164-c8d6-46c4-b1d0-192cf333434e/step-2B.3.md","content":"# Step 2B.3: DONE\n\nOn `phase-2b-data-layer`. I checked origin with `git ls-remote`: it shows `dc3224f`, the same as local.\n\n| Commit | What |\n|---|---|\n| `9d52d89` | the reel-to-batch map, checked with every issue hidden in turn |\n| `28c1a08` | `page_service` takes a page's batch from the map; every loc.gov answer is cached; the page check runs before a crop is shown |\n| `40586b0` | the page check's measurement, and which batch serves a flagged reel's page |\n| `dc3224f` | decision 35, and the plan's, architecture's and resume's notes |\n\nEach commit's tests pass on its own in a clean worktree. No PR: it comes when 2B closes.\n\n## Gate\n\n- **Tests and lint:** `make test` gives 339 passed, the live `atlas` test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- **The map** (`paperghosts/ingest/reels.py`, `scripts/reel_map.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/reels.json`):\n  - From the candidates alone, it reproduces decision 31 exactly: 367,251 of the 395,068 candidates with no batch path covered (93.0%), and 27,817 on 1,258 reels not.\n  - With the samples' batch paths: 370,949 covered (93.9%), and 24,119 on 1,000 reels not. 6,530 of those have no reel in their member name.\n- **Hidden issues** (every issue hidden in turn, all its pages at once):\n  - Overall: 739,317 of 740,969 issues right, 99.78% (99.77–99.79%).\n  - Flagged reels: 9,616 of 11,268, 85.3% (84.7–86.0%), and 94.0% (93.6–94.4%) by batch name.\n  - 1,046 reels can't be tested: each holds one issue.\n- **Flagged reels:** all 257 are in `reels.json`, each with its batches' date ranges: 62 reissues and 195 splits.\n- **Which batch serves** (`info.json` on every batch, for one page with no batch path on each of 50 drawn reels):\n  - The rule's first batch serves 42, 84.0% (71.5–91.7%).\n  - Trying the reel's batches in turn serves 46, 92.0% (81.2–96.8%).\n  - 4 need loc.gov.\n  - **The rule:** the batch whose issue is nearest in date, each name's latest version first. `info.json` decides, and on a 404 the next batch, then loc.gov.\n- **The page check** (90 pages whose member and batch path agree, each checked on its own frame and on the frame beside it):\n  - **False accepts:** 0 of 90, 0.0% (0–4.1%); 0 of the 59 frames beside that exist (0–6.1%).\n  - **False rejects:** 2 of the 85 own frames that exist, 2.4% (0.6–8.2%). Both are the right page, by their crops, with LoC's OCR garbled.\n  - 5 own frames' batches no longer serve them. `crops_for` sends those to loc.gov.\n  - **Size alone** accepts 2 of 36 exact-size frames beside (5.6%, 1.5–18.1%), and all 23 approximate ones. So I added the text check: the article's words inside its boxes in LoC's ALTO, at least a fifth of them.\n- **Requests:** 549 of the 600 planned, all to tile.loc.gov, one at a time, 3.5 s apart, each cached with its URL, date and status. None failed, and they took about 37 minutes. No lookups ran for the 24,119.\n- **Decision 35** is written.\n\n## For you\n\n1. **Where a member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).**\n   - All 18 member frames have the scan's recorded size, and the article's words are inside its boxes: 0.78 at the median.\n   - None of the 18 batch path frames has the recorded size, and their scores are 0 to 0.11.\n   - It's systematic, batch by batch, mostly in `dlc_`: in `dlc_earl_ver02`, 1,120 of 1,147 pages are off by one.\n   - So the stored `service` (`printings.py`, from the batch path) names the frame before the article's page for up to 20,643 candidates.\n   - **Your call.** I'd take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member. Where the reel differs too (396 candidates), I'd keep the batch path's page and check it before its crop is shown.\n   - I haven't changed it, because your brief says the batch path wins.\n2. **Item 4's design changed because of 1.** The pages you named as ones it should reject (member differs) turned out to be right pages. So the \"should reject\" set is the frame beside each agreeing page, and the \"should accept\" set is that page itself.\n3. **The text rule's threshold (a fifth) came from calibration's 38 pages.** The 90 measured pairs are fresh: the frames beside scored at most 0.13, and own frames, apart from the two garbled ones, at least 0.23.\n4. **`page_service` now prefers the map over loc.gov.** A page it locates without a batch path is unchecked. Crops should come through `crops_for`, which checks the page. `load_skeleton.py` still builds crop URLs from `page_service` directly. It's Phase 1's, and it isn't re-run.\n5. **Cost for 2D:** 2 requests and about 1 MB of ALTO per page with no batch path whose crop is shown. That's about 20,000 pages at 5% reports: 11 hours at 1 s a request.\n6. **tile.loc.gov at 3.5 s was this step's rule, set in the script.** `crops.get`'s default for image services stays 1 s (decision 29). Say if it should be 3.5 s everywhere.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"91dec1fb-4059-4d14-816e-6cf2c040509a","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZSqqP3WFy6ZrmQSTA5j","requestRef":"6fa5164f-cb0e-4f59-85c4-1063e409db2c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"96fd2a1a-331c-4c06-84f1-48db6c6534f1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:28:10.339Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
