{"parentUuid":"ec6f0aed-e5ee-40be-a10d-ba594a46c335","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZStLBxYy9vntQTBf66J","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"2B.3: DONE. I pushed `phase-2b-data-layer` at `dc3224f`, and `ls-remote` shows the same commit. The hand-over note is `step-2B.3.md`. 339 tests and lint pass.\n\n- **Map:** built from the candidates alone, it reproduces decision 31 exactly. With the samples added, it covers 370,949 candidates (93.9%), leaving 24,119 on 1,000 reels.\n- **Hidden issues:** 99.78% (99.77–99.79%) get the right batch. On the 257 flagged reels it's 85.3% (84.7–86.0%).\n- **Which batch serves:** the rule's first batch serves 42 of 50 sampled pages. Trying the reel's batches in turn finds 46.\n- **Page check:** 0 false accepts of 90 (0–4.1%), and 2 false rejects of 85 (2.4%). Size alone wasn't enough, so the article's words must also sit inside its boxes in LoC's OCR.\n- **Frames:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18. That makes up to 20,643 stored services one frame off. I haven't changed it, because your brief says the batch path wins.\n- **Requests:** 549 of the 600 planned."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_read_input_tokens":459197,"output_tokens":433,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":459197,"cache_creation_input_tokens":908,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":908},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"c3e77286-7554-4f28-8d79-da2d6bd02857","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZStKNbBRymJVqB6vhLE","requestRef":"b6803152-449f-4721-b5c9-deab1f2aadc7","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"53f18424-df9b-4d3d-83a3-cb18e0c24668","timestamp":"2026-10-31T01:28:25.434Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
