ing the reader reads per cluster, and the reader's job after clustering (from 1,236,122).\n6. BUDGET.md's third scenario takes the new clusters' stories per printing.\n\nGate: tests and lint pass; the frozen set's hash; precision and recall measured; every chained large cluster explained and its fix measured; decisions 35 and 36; pushed and checked with `ls-remote`.\n\nThen close 2B: write the STATUS block and open the PR into main. I'll review and merge it once CI, secret scan included, is green.","hostInjected":true},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":42},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
