{"parentUuid":"bc7e8c2e-a744-48e4-8253-8f11c0307b75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZTjX5Qq3qJxW8HUDGxU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SbHxuAjjNrtmGoxfRXyoak","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n    (\"  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396.\\n\",\n     \"  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396. For the frame, decision 35 supersedes this.\\n\"),\n    (\"Where a member and its batch path name different frames, the member's was the page.**\\n\",\n     \"Where a member and its batch path name different frames, the member's was the page, and the stored service now takes it.**\\n\"),\n    (\"- **Where a page's member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).** This goes against decision 33's rule for the frame. Changing it is the EM's call.\\n\",\n     \"- **Where a page's member and its batch path name different frames, the member's frame was the page: 18 of 18 (82.4–100%).** So the EM changed decision 33's rule for the frame.\\n\"),\n    (\"  - **So where the two differ, the stored `service`, which `printings.py` takes from the batch path, names the frame before the article's page.** That's up to 20,643 candidates (2.5% of those with both, decision 33).\\n\",\n     \"  - **So where the two differed, the stored `service`, which `printings.py` took from the batch path, named a frame beside the article's page.** That was up to 20,643 candidates (2.5% of those with both, decision 33).\\n\"),\n    (\"  - **Proposed, not done:** take the batch from the batch path and the frame from the member.\\n    - Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the evidence is thin. The map has the member's issue on the member's reel for only 12 of the 411 such pages, and for both sampled ones the batch path's batch holds no page at the member's place. So the batch path's page would stand there, checked before its crop is shown.\\n\",\n     \"  - **The EM's call (2026-10-30), which supersedes decision 33's frame rule** (`crops.batch_path_service`, used by `printings.py`, `page_service` and `crops_for`):\\n\"\n     \"    - Where only the frame differs, the page is the batch path's batch with the member's frame.\\n\"\n     \"    - Where the member's reel differs too (396 candidates), the batch path's page stands. The evidence for the member is thin there: the map has the member's issue on the member's reel for only 12 of the 411 such pages, and for both sampled ones the batch path's batch holds no page at the member's place.\\n\"\n     \"    - Either way, the page is checked before its crop is shown, as a page with no batch path is. A page goes unchecked only where its member and batch path agree.\\n\"\n     \"  - **It changes the stored service of 20,247 candidates, on 17,545 pages in 187 batches** (`reels.json`, `frame_rule`). That's decision 33's 20,643 with another frame, less the 396 with another reel. The most are in `dlc_earl_ver02` (1,163), `dlc_dutch_ver02` (1,032), `dlc_abe_ver01` (964), `dlc_chester_ver02` (929) and `dlc_braniff_ver01` (872).\\n\"),\n    (\"  1. from its batch path, as before;\\n\",\n     \"  1. from its batch path: its batch, with the member's frame where only the frame differs;\\n\"),\n    (\"  - A reissued batch's fallback in `crops_for` looks up the member's frame, as before.\\n\",\n     \"  - A page whose member and batch path agree is shown unchecked. Where its batch has been reissued, loc.gov names its current service, at the same place.\\n\"),\n    (\"- **For 2D:** the check costs 2 requests and about 1 MB of ALTO for each page with no batch path whose crop is shown. At 5% reports, that's about 20,000 pages: 11 hours at 1 s a request, and about 20 GB.\\n\",\n     \"- **For 2D:** the check costs 2 requests and about 1 MB of ALTO download for each page it checks. At 5% reports, that's about 20,000 pages with no batch path, and about 1,000 more whose member and batch path disagree: 12 hours at 1 s a request.\\n\"\n     \"  - **On disk,** the cache keeps a page's ALTO words at 187 KiB, the median of the 197 cached, so about 21,000 checks take about 4.0 GB. Gzipped, they'd take 1.3 GB (61 KB at the median). Keeping only the check's result would take almost nothing. The plan keeps it inside the 10 GB data budget.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:80]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\ns = s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + '''- **The EM's calls on this step (2026-10-30):**\n  - The frame rule changes, as above.\n  - The page check's design change stands, and its text rule's fifth is frozen. 2D records each check's score and reason, so the numbers sheet can count rejections.\n  - `scripts/load_skeleton.py` stays as it is. 3B's crops come only through `crops_for`.\n  - **Request rates:** loc.gov's \"Working Within Limits\" page (https://www.loc.gov/apis/json-and-yaml/working-within-limits/, read 2026-10-30) gives these limits, each blocking for an hour past them:\n\n    | Service | Requests a minute |\n    |---|---|\n    | the JSON/YAML API | 20 |\n    | image services | 150 |\n    | text services | 150 |\n    | `/storage-services/` | 150 |\n\n    - So tile.loc.gov stays at one request a second, and www.loc.gov at one in 3.5 s.\n    - The page warns that under heavy load you may meet \"429 status codes or HTML pages with CAPTCHAs\" even below those rates.\n    - So an HTML answer that isn't a 404 is busy, since every request the project makes expects JSON, XML or an image (`crops.captcha`). `get` pauses and asks again. A CAPTCHA page still there after the pauses raises `crops.Busy`, and `cached` never caches it.\n'''\np.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF","description":"Record the EM's calls in decision 35 and point decision 33 at it"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1268,"cache_read_input_tokens":502303,"output_tokens":3498,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1179},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1268,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3498,"cache_read_input_tokens":502303,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1268,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1268},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SbHxuAjjNrtmGoxfRXyoak":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n    (\"  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396.\\n\",\n     \"  - **Service:** the IIIF service comes only from the scan's batch path, which 68.0% of candidates have. Where a candidate has both, the batch path's frame differs from its member's in 20,643 (2.5%), and the reel in 396. For the frame, decision 35 supersedes this.\\n\"),\n    (\"Where a member and its batch path