{"parentUuid":"cc23bf28-6750-45da-818b-880d83c8d383","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZTnWGPae13HJqENRNSd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017wEc9YZF7murLhK13sGENr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n    (\"    - Decision 35 found the opposite for the frame: where the two differ, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member is the EM's call.\\n\",\n     \"    - Decision 35 found the opposite for the frame. Where only the frame differs, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18, and the stored service now takes it (the EM's call). Any page whose member and batch path disagree is checked before its crop is shown.\\n\"),\n    (\"  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page with no batch path before its crop is shown, by its size and its OCR (decision 35).\\n\",\n     \"  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page by its size and its OCR before its crop is shown, wherever its member and batch path don't agree (decision 35).\\n\"\n     \"    - Record each check's score and reason, so the numbers sheet can count rejections.\\n\"\n     \"    - The cache keeps about 187 KiB of ALTO words a page, so about 21,000 checks would take about 4 GB. Fit it inside the 10 GB data budget: gzip those entries (about 1.3 GB), or keep only each check's result.\\n\"),\n    (\"- `export_static`, plus the cached crops for the front page and the top cases.\\n\",\n     \"- `export_static`, plus the cached crops for the front page and the top cases.\\n\"\n     \"- Crops come only through `crops_for`, which checks a page before its crop is shown (decision 35).\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\na = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\"); s = a.read_text()\nold = \"    - Where the member name and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18 checked (decision 35). Which one the stored service follows is the EM's call.\\n\"\nnew = \"    - Where only the frame differs, the service takes the member's frame, which was the page in 18 of 18. Where the reel differs too, the batch path's page stands. Either way the page is checked before its crop is shown (decision 35).\\n\"\nassert s.count(old) == 1; a.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\nr = Path(\"Docs/RESUME.md\"); s = r.read_text()\nold = '''- **Step 2B.3 is built and waits on the gate review** (decision 35):\n  - the reel-to-batch map, its hidden-issue check, and the 257 flagged reels\n  - the page check, for a page with no batch path, before its crop is shown\n  - `page_service`'s cache\n  - **The EM's call:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member.\n'''\nnew = '''- **Step 2B.3 passed the EM's review** (decision 35): the reel-to-batch map, the page check and `page_service`'s cache.\n  - The EM's call: where only the frame differs, the stored service takes the member's frame. That changes 20,247 candidates' service.\n- **Step 2B.4,** the reprint clustering and its evaluation set (decision 36), is under way.\n'''\nassert s.count(old) == 1; r.write_text(s.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat","description":"Update the plan, architecture and resume for the EM's calls"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1443,"cache_read_input_tokens":507076,"output_tokens":1297,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"servi