e and a two-digit edition.","   - page, from the scan record only, when it has one","   - the page's IIIF `service`. It comes from the scan's batch path (decision 33). A page with none gets its batch from the reel-to-batch map or loc.gov, and is shown only once the page check confirms it (decision 35).","-    - Where the member name and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18 checked (decision 35). Which one the stored service follows is the EM's call.","+    - Where only the frame differs, the service takes the member's frame, which was the page in 18 of 18. Where the reel differs too, the batch path's page stands. Either way the page is checked before its crop is shown (decision 35).","   - `bbox_list`"," ","   Crop URLs are derived from `service` and `bbox_list` when a printing is read, never stored, and a printing keeps no text of its own."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":93,"oldLines":7,"newStart":93,"newLines":7,"lines":["   - Check a page located without a batch path before its crop is shown, and measure the check's error in the validation. One way is the scan's height and width against the IIIF `info.json`, and another is its OCR.","     - The check is needed because a member name can point at the wrong page. Where a candidate has both, its member's frame differs from its batch path's in 2.5% of them, and its reel in 396 (decision 33).","     - The batch path wins wherever it exists.","-    - Decision 35 found the opposite for the frame: where the two differ, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member is the EM's call.","+    - Decision 35 found the opposite for the frame. Where only the frame differs, the member's frame was the page in 18 of 18, and the stored service now takes it (the EM's call). Any page whose member and batch path disagree is checked before its crop is shown."," - No loc.gov lookups yet for the 24,119 candidates on the 1,000 reels the map doesn't cover (decision 35). At 20 a minute they would take most of a day, and most won't be reports.","   - Resolve only the ones the reader makes reports, through `crops.get` at one request every 3.5 s.","   - `page_service` caches each answer, one per issue, so no page is looked up twice (decision 35)."]},{"oldStart":139,"oldLines":7,"newStart":139,"newLines":9,"lines":["   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.","   - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked.","   - Story places follow 2C's rule: a county or state the text gives, or the dateline, and never the paper's state.","-  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page with no batch path before its crop is shown, by its size and its OCR (decision 35).","+  - A crop is fetched through `crops_for`, which checks a page by its size and its OCR before its crop is shown, wherever its member and batch path don't agree (decision 35).","+    - Record each check's score and reason, so the numbers sheet can count rejections.","+    - The cache keeps about 187 KiB of ALTO words a page, so about 21,000 checks would take about 4 GB. Fit it inside the 10 GB data budget: gzip those entries (about 1.3 GB), or keep only each check's result.","   - Measure the record check, and any further geocoder fix, on a fresh draw of papers, never on decision 34's 200. The first of two towns joined by \"and\" is one such fix.","   - The title lookup by LCCN (decision 34) holds each paper's place and state once. Whether it replaces every printing's copy is `BUDGET.md`'s lever."," - `make db-verify` runs geo, fuzzy and vector queries and checks their expected results and latencies."]},{"oldStart":170,"oldLines":6,"newStart":172,"newLines":7,"lines":[" **Persona:** software engineer."," - FastAPI endpoints from `SRS.md` section 6, with contract tests, Sentry, the privacy tests and latency measurements."," - `export_static`, plus the cached crops for the front page and the top cases.","+- Crops come only through `crops_for`, which checks a page before its crop is shown (decision 35)."," "," **Gate**"," - Tests are green, and the OpenAPI document is generated."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":11,"oldLines":11,"newStart":11,"newLines":9,"lines":["   - **Pending:** `places_search`. `sample_mflix` holds M0's third Search slot, and freeing it is the owner's call.","   - **The owner's call:** what to do if the reader's real count needs more storage than M0 has (`BUDGET.md`). The EM takes both to the owner."," - **Step 2B.2 passed the EM's review** (decision 34): the title parser and lookup, the GeoNames geocoder and the record check. Norfolk and Portsmouth's rule stays.","-- **Step 2B.3 is built and waits on the gate review** (decision 35):","-  - the reel-to-batch map, its hidden-issue check, and the 257 flagged reels","-  - the page check, for a page with no batch path, before its crop is shown","-  - `page_service`'s cache","-  - **The EM's call:** where the member and the batch path name different frames, the member's was the page in 18 of 18. Whether the stored service takes its frame from the member.","+- **Step 2B.3 passed the EM's review** (decision 35): the reel-to-batch map, the page check and `page_service`'s cache.","+  - The EM's call: where only the frame differs, the stored service takes the member's frame. That changes 20,247 candidates' service.","+- **Step 2B.4,** the reprint clustering and its evaluation set (decision 36), is under way."," - Phase 2B's PR comes when 2B closes."," - Lexicon v2 keeps all five rules (decision 31)."," "]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/RESUME.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"7cbd059c-8125-4899-867c-9622b9b532eb","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":8,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"357aa0c2-5e6f-44e9-a661-a7845549afd3","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
