{"parentUuid":"c78ae1f0-be0d-46fe-bcfe-1ea12f4ab354","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZTq9nB2d5rvzVesBSCm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011VBUpauEPt3B8ohZYK9fQ2","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nWhere only the frame differs, a page takes its member's frame; and a CAPTCHA page is busy\n\nThe EM's calls on 2B.3 (decision 35):\n- crops.batch_path_service: the batch path's batch with the member's frame\n  where only the frame differs, and the batch path's page where the reel\n  differs too. printings.py, page_service and crops_for use it, and\n  crops_for checks every page whose member and batch path don't agree.\n  It changes the stored service of 20,247 candidates in 187 batches\n  (reels.json, frame_rule): decision 33's 20,643, less the 396 whose reel\n  differs.\n- An HTML answer that isn't a 404 is busy, as loc.gov's Working Within Limits\n  warns: get pauses and asks again, and a CAPTCHA page still there raises\n  crops.Busy, which cached never caches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add Docs/ && git diff --cached > $S/b3/commit6.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/b3/commit6.diff && echo \"machine-name matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/b3/commit6.diff)\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nDecision 35: the EM's calls, loc.gov's limits, and the plan's notes for 2D and 3B\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3 && git push origin phase-2b-data-layer 2>&1 | grep -v -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" | tail -2 && git ls-remote origin refs/heads/phase-2b-data-layer && git rev-parse HEAD","description":"Commit the code and the docs, push, and verify with ls-remote","timeout":120000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":913,"cache_read_input_tokens":510125,"output_tokens":859,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":913,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":859,"cache_read_input_tokens":510125,"cache_creation_input_tokens":913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":913},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011VBUpauEPt3B8ohZYK9fQ2":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nWhere only the frame differs, a page takes its member's frame; and a CAPTCHA page is busy\n\nThe EM's calls on 2B.3 (decision 35):\n- crops.batch_path_service: the batch path's batch with the member's frame\n  where only the frame differs, and the batch path's page where the reel\n  differs too. printings.py, page_service and crops_for use it, and\n  crops_for checks every page whose member and batch path don't agree.\n  It changes the stored service of 20,247 candidates in 187 batches\n  (reels.json, frame_rule): decision 33's 20,643, less the 396 whose reel\n  differs.\n- An HTML answer that isn't a 404 is busy, as loc.gov's Working Within Limits\n  warns: get pauses and asks again, and a CAPTCHA page still there raises\n  crops.Busy, which cached never caches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad &