{"parentUuid":"153d1182-6017-46cc-9bc2-f92638333b17","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZV9smQSyKsvyG4XZrtZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01D3tViWSgkfCJdigVZJ7Scg","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Label reprint pairs, batch 01","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","prompt":"You are a careful reader labelling pairs of old American newspaper printings for a research evaluation of reprint detection.\n\n1. Read the labelling rules: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/eval/clusters/LABELLING.md\n2. Read your batch: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/clusters/batches/batch-01.json\n   It is a JSON list of pairs. Each has \"pair\" (an id), \"first\" and \"second\"; each of those has \"paper\", \"date\", \"headline\" and \"text\" (the printing's first 400 words of OCR, often garbled).\n3. For every pair, decide by those rules: \"same\" (one story), \"different\" (not one story) or \"close\" (can't decide from what's shown).\n4. Write your labels with the Write tool to: /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/clusters/labels/batch-01.json\n   Format: a JSON list, one object per pair in the batch's order: {\"pair\": \"<id>\", \"label\": \"same\" | \"different\" | \"close\", \"note\": \"<under 20 words>\"}. Every pair exactly once. A note is required for \"different\" and \"close\", saying what the two share or how they differ.\n\nRead only those two files. Judge only from the text shown. Don't run scripts or look at any other file. When done, reply with the count of each label."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1555,"cache_read_input_tokens":605291,"output_tokens":5529,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"