{"parentUuid":"4b4b0c1a-140a-4b11-84be-2d079e283895","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZVJ98c5Jdb75STfEpku","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`budget_stories.py` is sizing each judged report's cluster using eval A's clusters, and will switch to the cached features once tuning sets a threshold. I'm drafting decision 36's design section in the meantime.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":627280,"output_tokens":1671,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":469},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1671,"cache_read_input_tokens":627280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":2,"thinkingDisplay":"updates","serverClassifierRequest":"9643a742-975f-41ab-adae-0647629ddb55","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZVJ8Emi4oRLtpVvZesV","requestRef":"93171f8f-fbb0-495d-bffc-b7d0dca7ca7c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c669f2ea-952a-4930-9b25-f3115fae1e6f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:00:04.090Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"c669f2ea-952a-4930-9b25-f3115fae1e6f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZVJ98c5Jdb75STfEpku","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011bx6FdeehKipQkgNZy2uWQ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-design.md","content":"**36. Reprint clusters become stories: eval A's links stay, but a printing joins a story only by matching the story's first printing directly, so no chain joins stories that share nothing. [results in the title once measured]**\n- **What makes two printings one story:** one is the other's text printed again.\n  - It allows OCR errors, cuts, a new or missing headline, a credit line, and paragraphs added or dropped at either end.\n  - An advertisement or notice printed again word for word is one story too.\n- **What doesn't:**\n  - shared boilerplate: stock phrases, an advertisement's standard wording, a legal form, a masthead\n  - a quoted passage: a verse, a poem or a quotation inside otherwise different articles\n  - a serial's other instalments\n  - a standing column or department with other content\n  - a template with other particulars, such as testimonials quoting different people\n  - the same event told in different words\n  - `eval/clusters/LABELLING.md` is the reading agents' version.\n- **Eval A's clusters (decision 27) and what changes:**\n  - Eval A joins two candidates when they share a pair among their six smallest sampled seven-word runs, from their first 120 words. A pair held by more than 1,000 candidates is boilerplate.\n  - It joins every linked pair, so a chain of links joins stories that share nothing. That gives v2's 91,301 clusters holding 30.3% of candidates, and its 952,591 distinct stories.\n  - The links stay as they are, as the blocking. A pair of candidates the links don't join can't be one story, so a new cluster always sits inside one of eval A's. That's what lets an evaluation set drawn from eval A's clusters, before any tuning, cover every link the new method can make.\n- **The stories** (`paperghosts/cluster/reprints.py`, `stories`):\n  1. The printings are taken earliest first, ties by article id.\n  2. Each looks at the stories of the printings it's linked to.\n  3. It joins the one whose first printing it matches best, provided at least the threshold of the shorter's shingles are the other's. Otherwise it starts a story of its own.\n  - Every member matches its story's first printing directly, so nothing chains.\n  - **The shingles** (`shingles`): five-word runs of 3+ letters in the first 600 words, one in four kept by its own hash. They're shorter than the links' seven-word runs, so they weather OCR errors better, and they cover five times as much of the text.\n  - The share is taken of the shorter printing, so a cut reprint is held whole in its original.\n- **Stable ids:** a story's id is its first printing's article id. The same candidates give the same stories and the same ids on every run, which 2C's split by cluster needs.\n- **The cost of a false merge:** if the reader reads one printing per story, a report merged into another story is never read.\n  - So the threshold is chosen with a false merge costing five false splits.\n  - **The reader also reads every member at least 25% longer than its story's first printing**, since the extra text might hold another story. A first version counted members with less than 80% of their shingles in the first printing. That flagged OCR noise, not added text: 166,717 members, against 19,416 by length.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_read_input_tokens":627280,"output_tokens":1671,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":469},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1671,"cache_read_input_tokens":627280,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1392,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1392},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011bx6FdeehKipQkgNZy2uWQ":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-design.md","content":"**36. Reprint clusters become stories: eval A's links stay, but a printing joins a story only by matching the story's first printing directly, so no chain joins stories that share nothing. [results in the title once measured]**\n- **What makes two printings one story:** one is the other's text printed again.\n  - It allows OCR errors, cuts, a new or missing headline, a credit line, and paragraphs added or dropped at either end.\n  - An advertisement or notice printed again word for word is one story too.\n- **What doesn't:**\n  - shared boilerplate: stock phrases, an advertisement's standard wording, a legal form, a masthead\n  - a quoted passage: a verse, a poem or a quotation inside otherwise different articles\n  - a serial's other instalments\n  - a standing column or department with other content\n  - a template with other particulars, such as testimonials quoting different people\n  - the same event told in different words\n  - `eval/clusters/LABELLING.md` is the reading agents' version.\n- **Eval A's clusters (decision 27) and what changes:**\n  - Eval A joins two candidates when they share a pair among their six smallest sampled seven-word runs, from their first 120 words. A pair held by more than 1,000 candidates is boilerplate.\n  - It joins every linked pair, so a chain of links joins stories that share nothing. That gives v2's 91,301 clusters holding 30.3% of candidates, and its 952,591 distinct stories.\n  - The links stay as they are, as the blocking. A pair of candidates the links don't join can't be one story, so a new cluster always sits inside one of eval A's. That's what lets an evaluation set drawn from eval A's clusters, before any tuning, cover every link the new method can make.\n- **The stories** (`paperghosts/cluster/reprints.py`, `stories`):\n  1. The printings are taken earliest first, ties by article id.\n  2. Each looks at the stories of the printings it's linked to.\n  3. It joins the one whose first printing it matches best, provided at least the threshold of the shorter's shingles are the other's. Otherwise it starts a story of its own.\n  - Every member matches its story's first printing directly, so nothing chains.\n  - **The shingles** (`shingles`): five-word runs of 3+ letters in the first 600 words, one in four kept by its own hash. They're shorter than the links' seven-word runs, so they weather OCR errors better, and they cover five times as much of the text.\n  - The share is taken of the shorter printing, so a cut reprint is held whole in its original.\n- **Stable ids:** a story's id is its first printing's article id. The same candidates give the same stories and the same ids on every run, which 2C's split by cluster needs.\n- **The cost of a false merge:** if the reader reads one printing per story, a report merged into another story is never read.\n  - So the threshold is chosen with a false merge costing five false splits.\n  - **The reader also reads every member at least 25% longer than its story's first printing**, since the extra text might hold another story. A first version counted members with less than 80% of their shingles in the first printing. That flagged OCR noise, not added text: 166,717 members, against 19,416 by length.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"9643a742-975f-41ab-adae-0647629ddb55","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZVJ8Emi4oRLtpVvZesV","requestRef":"93171f8f-fbb0-495d-bffc-b7d0dca7ca7c","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"12bb1211-cf8f-4810-96d2-e2cc15cbd2eb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:00:13.908Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"12bb1211-cf8f-4810-96d2-e2cc15cbd2eb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e9ec6031-6d70-425a-a94b-94b6c6cc5b96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011bx6FdeehKipQkgNZy2uWQ","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-design.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"54ecc555-d0aa-479f-afe4-ccd4d7a6f8b2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:00:13.934Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-design.md","content":"**36. Reprint clusters become stories: eval A's links stay, but a printing joins a story only by matching the story's first printing directly, so no chain joins stories that share nothing. [results in the title once measured]**\n- **What makes two printings one story:** one is the other's text printed again.\n  - It allows OCR errors, cuts, a new or missing headline, a credit line, and paragraphs added or dropped at either end.\n  - An advertisement or notice printed again word for word is one story too.\n- **What doesn't:**\n  - shared boilerplate: stock phrases, an advertisement's standard wording, a legal form, a masthead\n  - a quoted passage: a verse, a poem or a quotation inside otherwise different articles\n  - a serial's other instalments\n  - a standing column or department with other content\n  - a template with other particulars, such as testimonials quoting different people\n  - the same event told in different words\n  - `eval/clusters/LABELLING.md` is the reading agents' version.\n- **Eval A's clusters (decision 27) and what changes:**\n  - Eval A joins two candidates when they share a pair among their six smallest sampled seven-word runs, from their first 120 words. A pair held by more than 1,000 candidates is boilerplate.\n  - It joins every linked pair, so a chain of links joins stories that share nothing. That gives v2's 91,301 clusters holding 30.3% of candidates, and its 952,591 distinct stories.\n  - The links stay as they are, as the blocking. A pair of candidates the links don't join can't be one story, so a new cluster always sits inside one of eval A's. That's what lets an evaluation set drawn from eval A's clusters, before any tuning, cover every link the new method can make.\n- **The stories** (`paperghosts/cluster/reprints.py`, `stories`):\n  1. The printings are taken earliest first, ties by article id.\n  2. Each looks at the stories of the printings it's linked to.\n  3. It joins the one whose first printing it matches best, provided at least the threshold of the shorter's shingles are the other's. Otherwise it starts a story of its own.\n  - Every member matches its story's first printing directly, so nothing chains.\n  - **The shingles** (`shingles`): five-word runs of 3+ letters in the first 600 words, one in four kept by its own hash. They're shorter than the links' seven-word runs, so they weather OCR errors better, and they cover five times as much of the text.\n  - The share is taken of the shorter printing, so a cut reprint is held whole in its original.\n- **Stable ids:** a story's id is its first printing's article id. The same candidates give the same stories and the same ids on every run, which 2C's split by cluster needs.\n- **The cost of a false merge:** if the reader reads one printing per story, a report merged into another story is never read.\n  - So the threshold is chosen with a false merge costing five false splits.\n  - **The reader also reads every member at least 25% longer than its story's first printing**, since the extra text might hold another story. A first version counted members with less than 80% of their shingles in the first printing. That flagged OCR noise, not added text: 166,717 members, against 19,416 by length.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"12bb1211-cf8f-4810-96d2-e2cc15cbd2eb","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
