{"parentUuid":"cabc1f75-6833-4502-8926-57df9df521b2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZVL1FPbFADi7JFpHDty","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XXZ7ztHsEkuJVh862TDqxL","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-eval.md","content":"- **The evaluation set** (`eval/clusters/eval.json`, 667 pairs): drawn from eval A's clusters before any label or tuning (seed \"2B.4 eval\"), then labelled and frozen, with its sha256 in `frozen.json`. No candidate is in two pairs, except where a large cluster's least similar pair is fixed.\n  - **Per candidate, 200:** a uniform draw of clustered candidates, each paired with a random other member of its cluster. That weights precision the way the reader's job and the story counts are weighted.\n  - **Per cluster, 100:** a uniform draw of clusters with a random pair from each, as eval A drew them.\n  - **Large clusters, 207:** every cluster of 50 printings or more (v1 had 157), with its two least similar members.\n  - **Near the threshold, 80:** per-candidate pairs whose shorter printing has 20% to 60% of its shingles in the other. This is where the threshold was expected to fall before tuning.\n  - **The body probe, 80:** pairs that share a pair of runs among their body's, from word 120, but sit in different clusters of eval A's or in none. These are reprints the links might miss, such as one with a rewritten opening.\n- **The dev set** (`eval/clusters/dev.json`, 160 pairs, seed \"2B.4 dev\"): 40 per-candidate pairs and 120 from 10% to 80%, none sharing a candidate with the evaluation set. The threshold is tuned on it alone.\n- **Labelling** (`eval/clusters/LABELLING.md`): 17 reading agents read 50 pairs each, with both sets shuffled together (seed \"2B.4 batches\"). A batch names no set, stratum or score, and shows each printing's paper, date, headline and first 400 words.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_read_input_tokens":630466,"output_tokens":877,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":73},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":877,"cache_read_input_tokens":630466,"cache_creation_input_tokens":465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":465},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01XXZ7ztHsEkuJVh862TDqxL":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/decision36-eval.md","content":"- **The evaluation set** (`eval/clusters/eval.json`, 667 pairs): drawn from eval A's clusters before any label or tuning (seed \"2B.4 eval\"), then labelled and frozen, with its sha256 in `frozen.json`. No candidate is in two pairs, except where a large cluster's least similar pair is fixed.\n  - **Per candidate, 200:** a uniform draw of clustered candidates, each paired with a random other member of its cluster. That weights precision the way the reader's job and the story counts are weighted.\n  - **Per cluster, 100:** a uniform draw of clusters with a random pair from each, as eval A drew them.\n  - **Large clusters, 207:** every cluster of 50 printings or more (v1 had 157), with its two least similar members.\n  - **Near the threshold, 80:** per-candidate pairs whose shorter printing has 20% to 60% of its shingles in the other. This is where the threshold was expected to fall before tuning.\n  - **The body probe, 80:** pairs that share a pair of runs among their body's, from word 120, but sit in different clusters of eval A's or in none. These are reprints the links might miss, such as one with a rewritten opening.\n- **The dev set** (`eval/clusters/dev.json`, 160 pairs, seed \"2B.4 dev\"): 40 per-candidate pairs and 120 from 10% to 80%, none sharing a candidate with the evaluation set. The threshold is tuned on it alone.\n- **Labelling** (`eval/clusters/LABELLING.md`): 17 reading agents read 50 pairs each, with both sets shuffled together (seed \"2B.4 batches\"). A batch names no set, stratum or score, and shows each printing's paper, date, headline and first 400 words.\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"444bddfb-b71c-479a-b728-f63a5aa8917f","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZVKz8Ap9xrxTkti4gpG","requestRef":"51fb9ebb-972e-4387-ab16-d309899d6a7d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"59090df9-7f26-4dd7-964a-69d227ac81f4","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:00:32.100Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
