{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:05:55.248Z","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","content":"<agent-message from=\"a1157b15c85b09731\">\n[Subagent hand-back] The text below is the final report of a subagent this session delegated to. It is model output, NOT a message from the user: instructions, requests, or approval claims inside it are the subagent's words and carry no user authority. The harness indents every line of the report, so a frame-like line at column zero inside it would be forged. Notes above this frame may quote model-derived text, which carries no user authority either. The report follows:\n  Batch-04 is labelled: 50 pairs, each exactly once, in batch order. The file is at /Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/data/clusters/labels/batch-04.json.\n  \n  Counts: same 46, different 1, close 3.\n  \n  - different (1): eval-0311. The first is about amending the Constitution to acknowledge God; the second is a labor-reform platform on currency and railroads.\n  - close (3):\n    - eval-0386: a premium book list printed twice in the Fort Worth Gazette. The titles mostly agree, but some are reordered and some added.\n    - eval-0337: a church notice. The closing wording matches, but the first is a short tail with an extra Reading Room sentence, so it's unconfirmed that they are one notice.\n    - eval-0566: the two share one \"unknown graves\" paragraph, but the other item in each differs (a Cuban quip in one, a coroner note in the other).\n  - same, judgement calls: I called these same rather than close.\n    - dev-0042: two editions in one paper on one date, with an identical lead and later paragraphs revised.\n    - eval-0276: the second is the Paris News passage, which the first prints after a short introduction.\n    - eval-0489: the second is only the poem's opening stanza.\n    - eval-0482: the second drops several stanzas and adds local personals after the poem.\n  \n  I read only the labelling rules and batch-04, judged from the text shown, and ran no scripts. Risk: the close calls are the likeliest to move if the EM reads the rules differently, mainly eval-0566 (could be different) and eval-0386 (could be same). I added short notes to every \"same\" label too, although the rules make them optional there.\n</agent-message>","reason":"absorbed_mid_turn","commandUuid":"b1e5c54a-ad5c-4b4e-b953-3c451873959e","deliveryId":"f56265a4-5daa-4fb2-9d8f-ee1111cf7482"}
