knoE IL nu y II he made g. Caste Asths basfu iom among a. and Of the lsvelest spots in the West --lseuuuel Fairfield, Iowa.\n=== eval-0478\n  first: The Butler weekly times. (Butler, Mo.) 1881-1918 1903-07-30 | Queer SuperstitiOns.\n    The following are some curious su, perstitions that are still extant among English-speaking people: Ii you XIII frogs your COWS will ''go dry\" Tickling a baby will cause thechild to SHUTTER. To thank a person for combing your hair will bring bad luck. To killa ghost it must be shot with bullet made OF silver coin. To dream OF a live snake means enemies at large; OF a dead snake, enemies dead or powerless. To dream Of unbroken eggs signi fies trouble to come; il the eggs art broken the trouble is past. Ifyou boast Of your good health strike\n  second: Vernon County censor. [volume] (Viroqua, Wis.) 186 1904-01-20 | SOUTHERN SUPERSTlTlONS.\n    If you kill frogs, your COWS win go dry\" Tickling a baby viii cause the child to stutter. To throw hair cOmblngs out Of the window is bad luck. To thank a person for combing yoIT hair viii bring bad luck No person who touches IA dead body will be haunted by is spirit Cut a dogs \"dew claws\" and it via not die from poisonous snake bite. To kill Il ghost It must be Shot with a bullet made Ct a silver quarter dollar. To dream Of a live snake means enc mics at large; of dead snake enemies\n=== eval-0441\n  first: The Daily bulletin. [volume] (Honolulu [Hawaii]) 1 1886-06-25 | Great Excitement in Wales\nabout a Marvellous Cure.\n\nLiving Six Years w\n    Al heard related what seemed to me either fabulous story or q marvellous cure. The story was that poor sufferer who had not been able to lie down in bed for six long years, given up 10 die by all the Doctors, had been speedily cured by some Patent Medicine. IL was related with the more implicit confidence from the circumstance, rs was said, that the Vicar of Llanrysiyd was familiar with the facts, and could vOuch for the truth of the report Having 