e Of the New York Tribune.] COLUMBIA, s. c.. May %. Jefferson Davis arrived here on Tuesday OH business connected with the life Insurance. company Of which he Is president. l was in PRODUCED to him yesterday in a lawyers Office, where he was holding an Informal reception, aud had a half-llonr's conversation. Mr.. Davis bears little resemblance 10 the pictures With which every BODY was familiar during the war, and he might walk the streets OF any Northern city without a chance of being known by peo~ pie VIII have seen only his photographs. Ia / found seated conspicnously\n=== eval-0593\n  first: Daily national Republican. [volume] (Washington, D 1866-01-23 | \n    Patent 0tAes ga naaarasnsai o. shs Iutsrior. Service Friday evenings d sunset, and Sab. bath mornings Al -. m. rrlnrps' MEETING HOUSE. Orthodox, No. ass North Ninth street, two doors south 81 , street, west sids. Sabbath Services at IL O. m Nam. o.. Meeting House, North street (porth sids), between Eighteenth sand Ninstssnth streets west. Meeting every Sabbath at ii a. m. . a LUTHERAN. ..t.. .. . German Evangelical Congregation OF Trim ity, Unalterod Augsburg Confession, Fourth street west, corner Of x street north. Pastor Rev. +. M. Busrger. Service morning, after noon, and night. .....H ....f. German\n  second: Daily national Republican. [volume] (Washington, D 1866-01-06 | \n    trest, vest sids, second squsrs north Of the Patent OeRc. sod p..>rk-.sat Of he Interior. Service Friday evenings n sunset, and Sab. bath morning. al 8 O. N. pRrsxps' urrfua HOUSE. Orthodox, No. tb3 North Ninth street, two doors south Of street, west aide. Sabbath services at IL .. IN. Meeting Houss, NORTH street north sidel between Eighteenth and Nineteenth streets west. Meeting every Sabbath at II .. m. LUTHERAN. German Evangelical Congregation OF Trim ity, Unaltered Augsburg Confession, Fourth street west, corner Of x street north. Pastor Rev &. N. Buergsr. Service morning, after. noon, and night. German Evangelical,\n=== eval