-08-18 | NINE. JEANETT.\n    EGYPTIAN PALMIST. CLAIRvOYANT. Guaranteed to read your enti-o life, past present and future. SGe asks no questions. but before you utter / word she tells what you call for, names of friends. enemies !: tells how to gain success In business, health, courtship. marriage. divorce. tells you what part OF the world will be sue cessful for YOU; advises you\n=== eval-0407  [large cluster, least similar pair; agent: close — First is the comet poem's opening stanzas; second is its later stanzas; no shared text shown.; sim [0, 0.0, 0.0]]\n  first: The daily dispatch. [volume] (Richmond [Va.]) 1850 1853-09-02 | \n    THE CoMET-The comet he is ON his wav And singing as he flies; The whizzing planets shrink before The spectre of the skies Ali well may regal orbs burn blue, And satellites turn pale, Ten million cubic miles of head, Ten billion leagues of tail\n  second: Shepherdstown register. [volume] (Shepherdstown, V 1857-05-30 | \n    One spurn from his demonIac heel Away, away they fly, Where darkness might be bottled up, And sold for \"Tyrean dye\" And what would happen 10 the land, And how wolld look the sea, If, in the bearded devils path, Our earth should chance 10 be Full hot and high the sea would boil, Full red the forests CLEAN !\n=== eval-0409  [large cluster, least similar pair; agent: different — Same markets-by-telegraph column; different days (April 23 vs March 1) with different figures.; sim [0, 0.0, 0.0]]\n  first: The Cincinnati daily star. [volume] ([Cincinnati,  1878-04-23 | MARKETS by TELEGRAPH.\n    WILMINGTON. April 23.-spirits of turpentine steady at 81 &c, BosroN, April 23-Flour steady and unchanged. Corn dull and unchanged. Oats dull and un. changed. INDIANAPOLIS, April 23-Flour quiet: fancy, Sc @6 5o family $S9S 50 Wasat quiet; No No 2Psd SAC. Provisions quiet. NEW ORLEANS, April 23.-Hay frmer: choice, S17. Pork dull and lower at $40 25 Bran easier at\n  second: The Cincinnati daily star. [volume] ([Cincinnati,  1878-03-0