{"parentUuid":"6c550198-5bb4-4736-9f1c-32e69b86d39d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZX2vardcqEB18Xjkc1p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MVAKMA9CwQRoLRsnygdmfh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && S=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad && git add paperghosts/cluster/reprints.py tests/test_reprints.py && git diff --cached > $S/b4/c1.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/b4/c1.diff && echo \"machine-name matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/b4/c1.diff)\" && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nStories: a printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly\n\nEval A's links stay as the blocking (two shared runs among each candidate's\nsix smallest in its opening), but each printing, earliest first, joins the\nstory whose first printing it matches best, where at least the threshold of\nthe shorter's shingles are the other's, or starts its own. Every member\nmatches its story's first printing, so no chain of links joins stories that\nshare nothing (decision 36). Shingles are five-word runs of 3+ letters from\nthe first 600 words, one in four kept by its hash; keys can now sample the\nbody as well as the opening, for the recall probe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\nls eval/clusters/ && git add scripts/clusters.py tests/test_clusters.py eval/clusters/ && git diff --cached --stat && git diff --cached > $S/b4/c2.diff && uv run python $S/scan_staged.py .env $S/b4/c2.diff && echo \"machine-name matches: $(grep -c -i -F \"$(hostname -s)\" $S/b4/c2.diff)\"","description":"Commit the method, then stage and scan the sets"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens"