 added:** 2A.8's 14 and 3 of the screen's 4 have 12 stories of 1 printing, then 2, 2, 2, 3 and 10. That's 0.820 stories per printing, so 21,176 printings give {v2:,} stories.\\n\"),\n (\"| As stored | the judged reports' ratio | 458.8 MB | no | **yes** | 47,330 / 67,436 |\\n\", \"| As stored | the judged reports' ratio | 461.8 MB | no | **yes** | 47,361 / 67,481 |\\n\"),\n (\"| int8 embedding | the judged reports' ratio | 387.4 MB | no | yes | 56,050 / 79,860 |\\n\", \"| int8 embedding | the judged reports' ratio | 389.9 MB | no | yes | 56,094 / 79,922 |\\n\"),\n (\"| The three | the judged reports' ratio | 441.5 MB | no | yes | 49,181 / 70,095 |\\n\", \"| The three | the judged reports' ratio | 444.4 MB | no | yes | 49,204 / 70,126 |\\n\"),\n (\"| The three, with int8 | the judged reports' ratio | 370.1 MB | no | yes | 58,676 / 83,627 |\\n\", \"| The three, with int8 | the judged reports' ratio | 372.5 MB | no | yes | 58,708 / 83,672 |\\n\"),\n (\"At the judged ratio nothing does: the smallest form needs 370.1 MB of the 350.5 MB free.\", \"At the judged ratio nothing does: the smallest form needs 372.5 MB of the 350.5 MB free.\"),\n (\"| Variant | v1's ratio | The judged reports' ratio (32,761 stories) | One story per printing |\\n\", \"| Variant | v1's ratio | The judged reports' ratio (33,024 stories) | One story per printing |\\n\"),\n (\"| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 242.3 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |\\n\", \"| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 244.1 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |\\n\"),\n (\"| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 233.4 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |\\n\", \"| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 235.2 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert t.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    t = t.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(t); print(\"BUDGET.md updated\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat Docs/BUDGET.md","description":"Update BUDGET.md's third scenario with the new stories"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_read_input_tokens":825271,"output_tokens":3034,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1241},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3034,"cache_read_input_tokens":825271,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1670,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1670},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0116zUq6LGtWDKJxQNwJT6vE":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\ns = json.load(open(\"eval/results/phase2b/budget_stories.json\"))\npools = s[\"pools\"]\nv1 = pools[\"v1's candidates\"][\"stories\"][\"top\"]; v2 = pools[\"the candidates v2 added\"][\"stories\"][\"top\"]\nprint(\"v1 stories\", v1, \"v2 stories\", v2, \"top\", s[\"top_of_the_range\"][\"stories\"], \"point\", s[\"point\"][\"stories\"])\np = Path(\"Docs/BUDGET.md\"); t = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"- **The judged reports' ratio, by pool,** gives 61,960 stories (`scripts/budget_stories.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/budget_stories.json`).\\n  - Each judged report counts as 1/k of a story when its v2 reprint cluster holds k printings.\\n\",\n  \"- **The judged reports' ratio, by pool,** gives 62,402 stories (`scripts/budget_stories.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/budget_stories.json`).\\n  - Each judged report counts as 1/k of a story when its story holds k printings: decision 36's stories, at its 