One story per printing |\\n\"),\n (\"| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 242.3 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |\\n\", \"| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 244.1 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |\\n\"),\n (\"| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 233.4 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |\\n\", \"| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 235.2 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert t.count(old) == 1, old[:70]\n    t = t.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(t); print(\"BUDGET.md updated\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat Docs/BUDGET.md","description":"Update BUDGET.md's third scenario with the new stories"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"350e67e0-4347-4ef4-a9b8-d835d238ad85","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZYFbLwjHcc3f6UzMh1F","requestRef":"f81fe716-754f-45ae-b584-907609c0da91","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"dd3b2bed-9949-4df3-bf5a-e0baba3ebae1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:39:06.764Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"dd3b2bed-9949-4df3-bf5a-e0baba3ebae1","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e9ec6031-6d70-425a-a94b-94b6c6cc5b96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0116zUq6LGtWDKJxQNwJT6vE","type":"tool_result","content":"v1 stories 45046 v2 stories 17356 top 62402 point 33024\nBUDGET.md updated\n Docs/BUDGET.md | 24 ++++++++++++------------\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3c39aaf5-c46d-4871-8c6c-0a41e915ddf2","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:39:08.085Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"v1 stories 45046 v2 stories 17356 top 62402 point 33024\nBUDGET.md updated\n Docs/BUDGET.md | 24 ++++++++++++------------\n 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 12 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUDGET.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":83,"oldLines":36,"newStart":83,"newLines":36,"lines":[" "," The top of decisions 30 and 31's intervals is 74,027 + 21,176 = **95,203 report printings**. Three scenarios:"," - **v1's ratio** of 22,300 stories to 36,766 printings (decision 27) gives 57,744 stories.","-- **The judged reports' ratio, by pool,** gives 61,960 stories (`scripts/budget_stories.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/budget_stories.json`).","-  - Each judged report counts as 1/k of a story when its v2 reprint cluster holds k printings.","-  - **v1's candidates:** eval A's 7 have clusters of 1, 1, 1, 13, 30, 1 and 7, so 0.608 stories per printing. That's decision 27's ratio again: 74,027 printings give 44,978 stories.","-  - **The candidates v2 added:** 2A.8's 14 and 3 of the screen's 4 have 12 clusters of 1, then 2, 2, 3, 5 and 10. That's 0.802 stories per printing: 21,176 printings give 16,982 stories.","+- **The judged reports' ratio, by pool,** gives 62,402 stories (`scripts/budget_stories.py`, `eval/results/phase2b/budget_stories.json`).","+  - Each judged report counts as 1/k of a story when its story holds k printings: decision 36's stories, at its tuned threshold. Eval A's clusters gave 61,960.","+  - **v1's candidates:** eval A's 7 have stories of 1, 1, 1, 12, 30, 1 and 7 printings, so 0.609 stories per printing, decision 27's ratio again. 74,027 printings give 45,046 stories.","+  - **The candidates v2 added:** 2A.8's 14 and 3 of the screen's 4 have 12 stories of 1 printing, then 2, 2, 2, 3 and 10. That's 0.820 stories per printing, so 21,176 printings give 17,356 stories.","   - The spiritualist reports v2 adds are reprinted less often, so the same printings make more stories."," - **The worst case** is one story per printing: 95,203 stories."," "," | Variant | Scenario | Needs | Fits with `sample_mflix` (350.5 MB) | Fits without it (499.4 MB) | Stories that fit, with / without |"," |---|---|---|---|---|---|"," | As stored | v1's ratio | 430.5 MB | no | **yes** | 47,007 / 66,975 |","-| As stored | the judged reports' ratio | 458.8 MB | no | **yes** | 47,330 / 67,436 |","+| As stored | the judged reports' ratio | 461.8 MB | no | **yes** | 47,361 / 67,481 |"," | As stored | one story per printing | 681.8 MB | no | no | 48,941 / 69,732 |"," | int8 embedding | v1's ratio | 364.0 MB | no | yes | 55,597 / 79,215 |","-| int8 embedding | the judged reports' ratio | 387.4 MB | no | yes | 56,050 / 79,860 |","+| int8 embedding | the judged reports' ratio | 389.9 MB | no | yes | 56,094 / 79,922 |"," | int8 embedding | one story per printing | 572.1 MB | no | no | 58,324 / 83,100 |"," | The three | v1's ratio | 413.4 MB | no | yes | 48,947 / 69,761 |","-| The three | the judged reports' ratio | 441.5 MB | no | yes | 49,181 / 70,095 |","+| The three | the judged reports' ratio | 444.4 MB | no | yes | 49,204 / 70,126 |"," | The three | one story per printing | 662.6 MB | no | no | 50,333 / 71,737 |"," | The three, with int8 | v1's ratio | 346.9 MB | yes, with 3.6 MB to spare | yes | 58,343 / 83,152 |","-| The three, with int8 | the judged reports' ratio | 370.1 MB | no | yes | 58,676 / 83,627 |","+| The three, with int8 | the judged reports' ratio | 372.5 MB | no | yes | 58,708 / 83,672 |"," | The three, with int8 | one story per printing | 552.9 MB | no | no | 60,323 / 85,974 |"," ","-**The judged reports' ratio changes one conclusion.** At v1's ratio, every lever, int8 included, just fits beside `sample_mflix`. At the judged ratio nothing does: the smallest form needs 370.1 MB of the 350.5 MB free. Without `sample_mflix`, every form fits, as before.","+**The judged reports' ratio changes one conclusion.** At v1's ratio, every lever, int8 included, just fits beside `sample_mflix`. At the judged ratio nothing does: the smallest form needs 372.5 MB of the 350.5 MB free. Without `sample_mflix`, every form fits, as before."," "," At the point estimates, the needs are much smaller: 36,766 + 12,996 = 49,762 printings, so 30,183 stories at v1's ratio."," ","-| Variant | v1's ratio | The judged reports' ratio (32,761 stories) | One story per printing |","+| Variant | v1's ratio | The judged reports' ratio (33,024 stories) | One story per printing |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 242.3 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |","-| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 233.4 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |","+| As stored | 225.0 MB: fits either way | 244.1 MB: fits either way | 356.4 MB: fits only without `sample_mflix` |","+| The three | 216.3 MB: fits either way | 235.2 MB: fits either way | 346.5 MB: fits either way |"," "," **Not in these figures:**"," - **Places, cases and stats.** They aren't built yet, but they are small. The tests' example documents are 251 bytes for a place, 272 for a stat and 1,774 for a case. So even 20,000 places, with their 2dsphere index, take a few MB."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUDGET.md"]}},"serverClassifierCon