{"parentUuid":"b2dcf53c-1a86-4053-8ff0-b6f0a08a48d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZYRGfpm9je8915pmgzA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RpEFBmsWsxRkfoMUNFMRuQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 109,116p Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same.\\n\",\n  \"  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same.\\n\"\n  \"  - Decision 36 builds the stories: eval A's links, but each printing must match its story's first printing directly. It's measured on a frozen set of 667 pairs.\\n\"),\n (\"- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\\n\",\n  \"- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\\n\"\n  \"  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure two changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\\n\"\n  \"    - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.\\n\"\n  \"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n# 2C: the split by story id\nold = \"1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\\n\"\nnew = (\"1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\\n\"\n       \"   - Gold, dev and train split by story id, a story's first printing's article id (decision 36). The reader reads each story's first printing, and its members at least 25% longer.\\n\")\nassert s.count(old) == 1; s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\na = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\"); t = a.read_text()\nold = \"| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingles + MinHash, plus a date window | Pipeline |\\n\"\nnew = \"| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingle links as blocking. Each printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly, so nothing chains (decision 36) | Pipeline |\\n\"\nassert t.count(old) == 1; a.write_text(t.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat Docs/","description":"Add the clustering notes to the plan and the architecture"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1996,"cache_read_input_tokens":839009,"output_tokens":986,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1996,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":986,"cache_read_input_tokens":839009,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1996,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1996},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RpEFBmsWsxRkfoMUNFMRuQ":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 109,116p Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same.\\n\",\n  \"  - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same.\\n\"\n  \"  - Decision 36 builds the stories: eval A's links, but each printing must match its story's first printing directly. It's measured on a frozen set of 667 pairs.\\n\"),\n (\"- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\\n\",\n  \"- Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.\\n\"\n  \"  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure two changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:\\n\"\n  \"    - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.\\n\"\n  \"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\n# 2C: the split by story id\nold = \"1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\\n\"\nnew = (\"1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.\\n\"\n       \"   - Gold, dev and train split by story id, a story's first printing's article id (decision 36). The reader reads each story's first printing, and its members at least 25% longer.\\n\")\nassert s.count(old) == 1; s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s)\na = Path(\"Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md\"); t = a.read_text()\nold = \"| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingles + MinHash, plus a date window | Pipeline |\\n\"\nnew = \"| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingle links as blocking. Each printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly, so nothing chains (decision 36) | Pipeline |\\n\"\nassert t.count(old) == 1; a.write_text(t.replace(old, new))\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat Docs/","description":"Add the clustering notes to the plan and the architecture"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d2ce9363-d1f5-40cf-b633-450ef30323c4","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZYRFuvYpp7CkW21YErw","requestRef":"d7d97242-deca-4039-98e7-b2ccca4d383e","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"aa00b614-04b6-4793-9dfd-b6ed78317e1e","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:41:03.963Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"aa00b614-04b6-4793-9dfd-b6ed78317e1e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e9ec6031-6d70-425a-a94b-94b6c6cc5b96","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RpEFBmsWsxRkfoMUNFMRuQ","type":"tool_result","content":"### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its place as its loc.gov title record catalogues it today, where the record was fetched\n  - its state today\n- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". It names the record's town only where the paper's point is the record's place: \"East Saginaw, Mich. (now Saginaw)\".\nok\n Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |   2 +-\n Docs/BUDGET.md       |  24 ++++++------\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |   5 +++\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 125 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"374b0817-c917-48d0-8063-9bbd7b86a8c0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:41:04.816Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load\n- Places are resolved against GeoNames. Every location records its precision (town, street or building) and its source. Street or building coordinates exist only when a source supplies them.\n- The title lookup by LCCN (`scripts/titles.py`, decision 34) holds:\n  - each paper's title, place and state as printed\n  - what the cataloguer supplied\n  - its place as its loc.gov title record catalogues it today, where the record was fetched\n  - its state today\n- The site shows the printed place, with what has changed since: \"Charlestown, Va. (now W.Va.)\". It names the record's town only where the paper's point is the record's place: \"East Saginaw, Mich. (now Saginaw)\".\nok\n Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md |   2 +-\n Docs/BUDGET.md       |  24 ++++++------\n Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md   |   5 +++\n Docs/DECISIONS.md    | 107 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++\n 4 files changed, 125 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":64,"oldLines":7,"newStart":64,"newLines":7,"lines":[" | Reader | Classify each candidate and extract fields, each with a verbatim quote | Qwen 4B student with a LoRA trained on Tinker from teacher labels | Full pass on Tinker sampling; also runs locally offline |"," | Quote verifier | Keep a field only if its quote is found in the OCR text, allowing for OCR noise | `rapidfuzz`, threshold calibrated on the gold set | Pipeline and investigator |"," | Geocoder | Publication place from the LCCN title; article places from the reader | GeoNames `cities1000`, offline, with a manifest | Pipeline |","-| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingles + MinHash, plus a date window | Pipeline |","+| Reprint clustering | Group printings of the same story across papers (syndication was common) | Shingle links as blocking. Each printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly, so nothing chains (decision 36) | Pipeline |"," | Embedder | Vectors for \"ghosts like this one\" | An open embedding model through Ollama; dimensions chosen to fit the Atlas budget | Pipeline only; the site reuses stored vectors |"," | Atlas loader | Upsert reports, places, cases and stats; create indexes | PyMongo | Pipeline |"," | Follow-up harvest | Second streaming pass over only the years the top cases need: follow-ups, death notices, inquests, debunkings | The ingest code with per-case patterns | Temporal workflow |"]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":86,"oldLines":6,"newStart":86,"newLines":7,"lines":[" - The reprint-clustering design, and its evaluation set:","   - Sample per candidate as well as per cluster. Eval A's check drew clusters uniformly, so 11 of its 20 pairs came from clusters of 2 printings, and none of the 157 clusters of 50 or more was checked.","   - Hand-check the largest clusters for chaining, where shared runs join stories that aren't the same.","+  - Decision 36 builds the stories: eval A's links, but each printing must match its story's first printing directly. It's measured on a frozen set of 667 pairs."," - The reel-to-batch map (decision 29):","   - Build it from the batch paths in the candidates and samples, so a page with no batch path gets its IIIF service from local data. That's about 367,000 of lexicon v2's candidates (decision 31), and 370,949 with the samples' batch paths (decision 35).","   - Validate it: hide the batch on pages that have one, and count how often the map gets it back."]},{"oldStart":107,"oldLines":6,"newStart":108,"newLines":7,"lines":[" ### 2C: the reader"," **Persona:** ML specialist."," 1. Write `POLICY.md`, build the gold set, freeze it and hash it.","+   - Gold, dev and train split by story id, a story's first printing's article id (decision 36). The reader reads each story's first printing, and its members at least 25% longer.","    - The gold set's term strata include each of lexicon v2's five rules. That's how ouija, kept with 0 reports in its 6 sampled candidates, gets measured (decision 31).","    - `POLICY.md` settles delusions and hallucinations with one rule. Eval A counts a 1904 defendant pointing at an \"imaginary\" spectre in court as a report, and a 1909 lunacy hearing's spooks as other. Its interval barely moves either way.","    - It also settles claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found."]},{"oldStart":135,"oldLines":6,"newStart":137,"newLines":9,"lines":[" ### 2D: load, cluster and harvest"," **Persona:** data engineer."," - Geocode, cluster, embed, and load Atlas.","+  - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure two changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:","+    - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.","+    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.","   - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.","   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.","   - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked."]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/ARCHITECTURE.md","/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md"]}},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"d2ce9363-d1f5-40cf-b633-450ef30323c4","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2b-data-layer","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":false,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":5,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":2},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"aa00b614-04b6-4793-9dfd-b6ed78317e1e","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
