{"parentUuid":"a5d4706b-0fba-42b6-af35-739fe37d0cc7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZYdRsJECLdNfvvqcqco","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every new commit passes on its own. I pushed at `42c96c2`, and `ls-remote` shows the same commit. Now 2B's PR into `main`, as the EM asked and as the owner's workflow has it. Writing the body first."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":848576,"output_tokens":2628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":732,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2628,"cache_read_input_tokens":848576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":732},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"serverClassifierRequest":"d77a0e68-23fc-4099-a05e-d9a7efff6a9b","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CgZYdQctXDPgW2cZCZGCr","requestRef":"70d2bb52-023d-4144-82da-74cfe6172c2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"a0d8be6b-f8ab-441e-b279-71cdc9977498","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:44:03.352Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"a0d8be6b-f8ab-441e-b279-71cdc9977498","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZYdRsJECLdNfvvqcqco","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NhLmdXw4P3v1QS75xJjZtS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/pr-body.md","content":"Phase 2B: schemas and the data layer, in four steps on `phase-2b-data-layer`. The EM reviewed each step. Decisions 32 to 36 record them, and `Docs/RESUME.md` ends with the phase's STATUS block.\n\n- **2B.1** (decisions 32 and 33):\n  - Pydantic models, with the Atlas validators generated from them\n  - BinData embeddings\n  - `make db-init`, which can be re-run safely\n  - `BUDGET.md`, built from real document sizes\n- **2B.2** (decision 34): the LCCN title parser, the loc.gov title records and the title lookup, the GeoNames geocoder, and the record check.\n  - The parser is tested on 200 titles checked by hand, and the records are cached.\n  - The geocoder covers the US, Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands dumps, with its manifest.\n  - **98.0% (95.0–99.2%) of 200 papers' places are right.**\n- **2B.3** (decision 35):\n  - **The reel-to-batch map** gives 93.9% of candidates with no batch path a batch from local data. It gets 99.78% of hidden issues right.\n  - **The page check runs before a crop is shown.** It accepted 0 of 90 wrong frames and rejected 2 of 85 right ones.\n  - **`page_service` caches** every Library of Congress answer, and a CAPTCHA page counts as busy.\n  - **The EM's frame rule:** where only the frame differs, the member's frame is the page. That changes 20,247 candidates' service.\n- **2B.4** (decision 36): reprint stories, in which a printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly.\n  - A 667-pair evaluation set was labelled and frozen before tuning, and pushed at `f86021f` with its sha256.\n  - **Precision per candidate is 100% (97.7–100%), and recall is 84.7% (79.0–89.1%).** The chaining in 51 of the 54 chained large clusters is split.\n\n**Checks**\n- `make test` gives 355 passed, the live Atlas test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- Each commit's tests pass on its own in a clean worktree.\n- Each commit's staged diff was scanned against `.env`'s values, by name only, before it was made.\n\n**For the owner**\n- `places_search` needs a free Search slot, and `sample_mflix` holds M0's third (decision 33).\n- At the top of the range, the stories fit on M0 only without `sample_mflix` (`BUDGET.md`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_read_input_tokens":848576,"output_tokens":2628,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1209},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":732,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2628,"cache_read_input_tokens":848576,"cache_creation_input_tokens":732,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":732},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NhLmdXw4P3v1QS75xJjZtS":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-hotragn-Documents-Claude-Code-HacktoberFest-week4-Paperghosts/1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b/scratchpad/b4/pr-body.md","content":"Phase 2B: schemas and the data layer, in four steps on `phase-2b-data-layer`. The EM reviewed each step. Decisions 32 to 36 record them, and `Docs/RESUME.md` ends with the phase's STATUS block.\n\n- **2B.1** (decisions 32 and 33):\n  - Pydantic models, with the Atlas validators generated from them\n  - BinData embeddings\n  - `make db-init`, which can be re-run safely\n  - `BUDGET.md`, built from real document sizes\n- **2B.2** (decision 34): the LCCN title parser, the loc.gov title records and the title lookup, the GeoNames geocoder, and the record check.\n  - The parser is tested on 200 titles checked by hand, and the records are cached.\n  - The geocoder covers the US, Puerto Rico and Virgin Islands dumps, with its manifest.\n  - **98.0% (95.0–99.2%) of 200 papers' places are right.**\n- **2B.3** (decision 35):\n  - **The reel-to-batch map** gives 93.9% of candidates with no batch path a batch from local data. It gets 99.78% of hidden issues right.\n  - **The page check runs before a crop is shown.** It accepted 0 of 90 wrong frames and rejected 2 of 85 right ones.\n  - **`page_service` caches** every Library of Congress answer, and a CAPTCHA page counts as busy.\n  - **The EM's frame rule:** where only the frame differs, the member's frame is the page. That changes 20,247 candidates' service.\n- **2B.4** (decision 36): reprint stories, in which a printing joins a story only by matching its first printing directly.\n  - A 667-pair evaluation set was labelled and frozen before tuning, and pushed at `f86021f` with its sha256.\n  - **Precision per candidate is 100% (97.7–100%), and recall is 84.7% (79.0–89.1%).** The chaining in 51 of the 54 chained large clusters is split.\n\n**Checks**\n- `make test` gives 355 passed, the live Atlas test included, and `make lint` exits 0.\n- Each commit's tests pass on its own in a clean worktree.\n- Each commit's staged diff was scanned against `.env`'s values, by name only, before it was made.\n\n**For the owner**\n- `places_search` needs a free Search slot, and `sample_mflix` holds M0's third (decision 33).\n- At the top of the range, the stories fit on M0 only without `sample_mflix` (`BUDGET.md`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d77a0e68-23fc-4099-a05e-d9a7efff6a9b","apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CgZYdQctXDPgW2cZCZGCr","requestRef":"70d2bb52-023d-4144-82da-74cfe6172c2d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b913dc75-bb93-4a4f-991d-999e6b177a1c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T02:44:11.544Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2b-data-layer","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
