{"parentUuid":"6c420e36-c5b4-46f2-b81b-ae7844c29652","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85c09507-e1dc-4ee2-9bb2-d7c89f179db7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01J3KfD16HKHcjdf377BYHVg","type":"tool_result","content":"From https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts\n   718de62..e350721  main       -> origin/main\ne350721 Merge pull request #4 from Hotragn/phase-2b-data-layer\ne350721 Merge pull request #4 from Hotragn/phase-2b-data-layer\n42c96c2 Decision 36, the plan's notes for 2C and 2D, and Phase 2B's STATUS block\n31:| RDR-1 | The gold set has 150–300 articles, stratified by decade and term. It is frozen and hashed before training, and the split is committed. | `eval/gold/split.json` and `eval/gold/HASH`, unchanged in git history after the freeze |\n32:| RDR-2 | The label schema covers: `kind` (report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other); place, people, seen and outcome (unexplained, explained, hoax, unknown); and, for walks, specific place, place type (house, church, cemetery, inn or hotel, road or bridge, public building, ship, other) and precision. Each value carries a verbatim quote. | Schema tests |\n33:| RDR-3 | `eval/gold/POLICY.md` holds the rules for hard cases and is written before any labelling. | Git history order |\n34:| RDR-4 | Training data is disjoint from the gold set, including reprints of gold stories. | `scripts/check_leakage.py` exits 0 |\n35:| RDR-5 | LoRA training runs on Tinker. The configs, checkpoints and seeds are recorded. | `eval/results/reader_runs.json` |\n36:| RDR-6 | Eval B compares base 4B, tuned 4B and the teacher on the gold set. It reports metrics with bootstrap 95% intervals, cost per 10,000 articles, and p50 and p95 latency. | `eval/results/reader_eval.json`, plus charts |\n37:| RDR-7 | Every ablation in section 7.2 is run, or its absence is explained. | Ablation JSON and charts |\n38:| RDR-8 | The edge-case suite in section 7.3 is reported slice by slice. | `eval/results/reader_edge_cases.json` |\n39:| RDR-9 | The quote verifier's threshold is calibrated on the gold set. A field whose quote doesn't verify becomes \"not stated\". | Calibration curve, plus unit tests |\n40:| RDR-10 | The tuned student runs locally with no network, on at least 200 articles, and its agreement with the Tinker-served outputs is reported. A guard in the runner blocks sockets, so system network settings are never touched. | `scripts/offline_proof.py` output |\n41:| RDR-11 | The full reader pass covers every triaged candidate, and its outputs are versioned. | Counts in eval A and B |\n42:| RDR-12 | At least one failure the eval exposed is logged, with what changed because of it. | `DECISIONS.md`, and the README failure log |\n210:| RDR-*, eval B | 2C | `eval/results/reader_*.json`, `eval/MODEL_CARD.md` |","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"5f391e49-32d3-4ad9-b898-6a2983fb135a","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:00:15.136Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"From https://github.com/Hotragn/Paperghosts\n   718de62..e350721  main       -> origin/main\ne350721 Merge pull request #4 from Hotragn/phase-2b-data-layer\ne350721 Merge pull request #4 from Hotragn/phase-2b-data-layer\n42c96c2 Decision 36, the plan's notes for 2C and 2D, and Phase 2B's STATUS block\n31:| RDR-1 | The gold set has 150–300 articles, stratified by decade and term. It is frozen and hashed before training, and the split is committed. | `eval/gold/split.json` and `eval/gold/HASH`, unchanged in git history after the freeze |\n32:| RDR-2 | The label schema covers: `kind` (report, fiction, idiom, religious, advert, other); place, people, seen and outcome (unexplained, explained, hoax, unknown); and, for walks, specific place, place type (house, church, cemetery, inn or hotel, road or bridge, public building, ship, other) and precision. Each value carries a verbatim quote. | Schema tests |\n33:| RDR-3 | `eval/gold/POLICY.md` holds the rules for hard cases and is written before any labelling. | Git history order |\n34:| RDR-4 | Traini