"update_plan","type":"assistant","uuid":"cffefa7b-c847-42e6-b417-202a0c8ce296","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:00:19.301Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"cffefa7b-c847-42e6-b417-202a0c8ce296","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85c09507-e1dc-4ee2-9bb2-d7c89f179db7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TSdgEJ2zbsVBm9ujXoAaNk","type":"tool_result","content":"|---|---|---|\n| ING-1 | All 180 year files are streamed without ever storing a tarball. Ingest outputs total at most 10 GB on disk. | Per-year manifests, and a disk-use line in eval A |\n| ING-2 | Each year file is one Temporal activity, with heartbeats and a retry policy. Outputs are idempotent. | The Temporal UI history, and kill test 1 |\n| ING-3 | The lexicon is versioned in code, covers common OCR variants, and each candidate records the terms it matched. | Unit tests, including OCR-variant cases |\n| ING-4 | Each year records its pages, articles and candidates, by state and by term. | `eval/results/archive_read.json` |\n| ING-5 | Each year writes a random non-candidate sample and a near-miss pool. | Files exist, and eval A has a recall section |\n| ING-6 | The crop builder handles single-column and multi-column articles (`bbox_list`). It is checked on 50 random candidates spread across as many batches as the sample allows. | `eval/results/crop_check.json`, plus a contact sheet image |\n\n### 2.2 Reader (RDR)\n| ID | Requirement | Verified by |\n|---|---|---|\n5:## 1. Definitions\n16:## 2. Functional requirements\n18:### 2.1 Ingest (ING)\n28:### 2.2 Reader (RDR)\n44:### 2.3 Places (GEO)\n51:### 2.4 Data layer (DB)\n61:### 2.5 Investigator (INV)\n75:### 2.6 API (API)\n84:### 2.7 Web (WEB)\n98:### 2.8 Walks (WALK, P2)\n105:## 3. Non-functional requirements\n120:## 4. Constraints\n126:## 5. Data requirements\n136:## 6. API contract (read-only)\n152:## 7. Evaluation specifications\n155:### 7.1 Evals A to D\n171:### 7.2 Reader ablations\n187:### 7.3 Edge-case suite\n204:## 8. Traceability\n### 3.2 Gold set and reader\n- **Gold set:**\n  - 150–300 candidates, stratified by decade and lexicon term and including near-miss items.\n  - Frozen before any training: the split and its hash are committed under `eval/gold/`.\n  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\n  - The labelling rules for hard cases (séance reports, reprinted fiction, hoax exposures, humour columns) are written in `eval/gold/POLICY.md` before labelling starts.\n- **Training data:** the teacher labels a separate pool. No gold article, and no reprint of a gold article, may appear in it.\n- **Model selection** happens on a dev split. The gold set is touched only for final evaluations.\n- **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n\n### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3fbae678-54c2-40cb-b4cd-299b9d586a8c","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:00:20.088Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"|---|---|---|\n| ING-1 | All 180 year files are streamed without ever storing a tarball. Ingest outputs total at most 10 GB on disk. | Per-year manifests, and a disk-use line in eval A |\n| ING-2 | Each year file is one Temporal activity, with heartbeats and a retry policy. Outputs are idempotent. | The Temporal UI history, and kill test 1 |\n| ING-3 | The lexicon is versioned in code, covers common OCR variants, and each candidate records the terms it matched. | Unit tests, including OCR-variant cases |\n| ING-4 | Each year records its pages, articles and candidates, by state and by term. | `eval/results/archive_read.json` |\n| ING-5 | Each year writes a random non-candidate sample and a near-miss pool. | Files exist, and eval A has a recall section |\n| ING-6 | The crop builder handles single-column and multi-column articles (`bbox_list`). It is checked on 50 random candidates spread across as many batches as the sample allows. | `eval/results/crop_check.json`, plus a contact sheet image |\n\n### 2.2 Reader (RDR)\n| ID | Requirement | Verified by |\n|---|---|---|\n5:## 1. Definitions\n16:## 2. Functional requirements\n18:### 2.1 Ingest (ING)\n28:### 2.2 Reader (RDR)\n44:### 2.3 Places (GEO)\n51:### 2.4 Data layer (DB)\n61:### 2.5 Investigator (INV)\n75:### 2.6 API (API)\n84:### 2.7 Web (WEB)\n98:### 2.8 Walks (WALK, P2)\n105:## 3. Non-functional requirements\n120:## 4. Constraints\n126:## 5. Data requirements\n136:## 6. API contract (read-only)\n152:## 7. Evaluation specifications\n155:### 7.1 Evals A to D\n171:### 7.2 Reader ablations\n187:### 7.3 Edge-case suite\n204:## 8. Traceability\n### 3.2 Gold set and reader\n- **Gold set:**\n  - 150–300 candidates, stratified by decade and lexicon term and including near-miss items.\n  - Frozen before any training: the split and its hash are committed under `eval/gold/`.\n  - The build agent labels it before seeing any model output, from the OCR text and the scan crop where the OCR is unclear.\n  - The labelling rules for hard cases (séance reports, reprinted fiction, hoax exposures, humour columns) are written in `eval/gold/POLICY.md` before labelling starts.\n- **Training data:** the teacher labels a separate pool. No gold article, and no reprint of a gold article, may appear in it.\n- **Model selection** happens on a dev split. The gold set is touched only for final evaluations.\n- **Full pass:** the tuned student reads every triaged candidate and writes `data/reader/{year}.jsonl.zst`. Every field either passes the quote verifier or becomes \"not stated\".\n\n### 3.3 Geocode, cluster, embed, load","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"038184ad-61a9-4ca4-9069-5b25c147c6a7","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":