{"parentUuid":"3fbae678-54c2-40cb-b4cd-299b9d586a8c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZZuDN2kR8uNr7ZyGKRz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q18ipRKXvjJ7ExvbirmaR8","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 5,16p Docs/SRS.md && sed -n 152,204p Docs/SRS.md","description":"Read the SRS's definitions and evaluation specifications"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1343,"cache_read_input_tokens":870222,"output_tokens":162,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1343,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":162,"cache_read_input_tokens":870222,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1343,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1343},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Q18ipRKXvjJ7ExvbirmaR8":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && sed -n 5,16p Docs/SRS.md && sed -n 152,204p Docs/SRS.md","description":"Read the SRS's definitions and evaluation specifications"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"ff2f94ef-d996-4b40-b98e-727fbcaa3472","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZZuCe8BaHmRyk2wrTZ7","requestRef":"467c9a94-c982-4492-a89a-dcd6fa47849d","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"55de0834-0b60-49d3-83ca-e6ced1195ce0","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:00:22.953Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"parentUuid":"55de0834-0b60-49d3-83ca-e6ced1195ce0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"85c09507-e1dc-4ee2-9bb2-d7c89f179db7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q18ipRKXvjJ7ExvbirmaR8","type":"tool_result","content":"## 1. Definitions\n- **Article:** one article region from AmericanStories, with its text, headline, bounding boxes and page.\n- **Printing:** one article as printed in one paper on one date.\n- **Story:** a cluster of printings of the same text. Syndicated stories were reprinted in many papers.\n- **Candidate:** an article that hit the lexicon.\n- **Report:** a candidate the reader classified as `kind = report`.\n- **Case:** a report the investigator worked on.\n- **Clipping:** the crop of the page scan for one article.\n- **Verified quote:** a quote the verifier found in the source text, within the calibrated fuzzy threshold.\n- **Precision:** how exactly a location is known: town, street or building.\n\n## 2. Functional requirements\n## 7. Evaluation specifications\nResults are saved as JSON plus a chart under `eval/results/`, and each is produced by one command.\n\n### 7.1 Evals A to D\n- **A, the archive read:**\n  - pages and articles read, and candidates per year\n  - reports per million articles, by year and by state\n  - the term mix and an OCR-quality distribution\n  - prefilter recall: a random-sample upper bound (rule of three when no misses are found) and the misses found in the near-miss pool, with the lexicon changes they caused\n- **B, the reader:**\n  - kind accuracy and macro-F1, and report precision, recall and F1\n  - field match rates, and the share of quotes verified\n  - the hallucinated-quote rate\n  - cost per 10,000 articles and latency\n  - bootstrap 95% intervals throughout\n  - the headline is the accuracy gap and the cost per 10,000 articles\n- **C, the investigations:** case files written, named deaths found, cases explained or exposed, then-and-now differences, the claim-verification rate and dropped claims, and Gemma against Ultramarine on the same cases (claims, verification rate, cost, latency).\n- **D, the app:** Lighthouse on mobile, axe, contrast, e2e on phone and desktop in both modes, and the walks counts if walks are built.\n\n### 7.2 Reader ablations\n| ID | What changes | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | Base 4B, tuned 4B, teacher | The headline comparison |\n| B2 | Training set size (a learning curve of at least 3 points) | Whether more teacher labels would help |\n| B3 | LoRA rank and learning rate (a small grid, within credits) | Picks the trained model |\n| B4 | Output format: fields with quotes against kind only | The cost of grounding |\n| B5 | Quote verifier on and off, plus a threshold sweep | Precision of the fields shown |\n| B6 | Triage on and off | Reports lost against cost saved |\n| B7 | Slices by OCR quality | Robustness to rough scans |\n| B8 | Slices by decade | Language drift from 1774 to 1963 |\n| B9 | Base 4B zero-shot against few-shot | Makes the baseline fair |\n| B10 | Reprint leakage removed, or not | Proves the scores aren't inflated |\n\nModel selection uses a dev split. The gold set is used only for these final runs.\n\n### 7.3 Edge-case suite\nEach slice uses at least 5 gold items where the archive has them:\n- E1: sermons and hymns about the Holy Ghost\n- E2: idioms (\"ghost of a chance\", \"gave up the ghost\", \"not the ghost of a\")\n- E3: ghost stories as fiction, serials and Christmas stories\n- E4: theatre and illusion adverts (Pepper's ghost), patent medicine and real estate\n- E5: spiritualist séances and rappings (`POLICY.md` decides their kind)\n- E6: hoax exposures and pranksters caught\n- E7: humour and joke columns\n- E8: phantom ships, trains and lights\n- E9: one story reprinted under different datelines\n- E10: badly garbled OCR\n- E11: segmentation errors, where several items are merged into one article\n- E12: non-English text\n- E13: \"Ghost\" as a surname or a place name\n- E14: political figures of speech (\"the ghost of the tariff\")\n\n## 8. Traceability","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"f3d6f27a-6ce0-43a1-8663-c83dde09ae1f","timestamp":"2026-10-31T03:00:23.426Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 1. Definitions\n- **Article:** one article region from AmericanStories, with its text, headline, bounding boxes and page.\n- **Printing:** one article as printed in one paper on one date.\n- **Story:** a cluster of printings of the same text. Syndicated stories were reprinted in many papers.\n- **Candidate:** an article that hit the lexicon.\n- **Report:** a candidate the reader classified as `kind = report`.\n- **Case:** a report the investigator worked on.\n- **Clipping:** the crop of the page scan for one article.\n- **Verified quote:** a quote the verifier found in the source text, within the calibrated fuzzy threshold.\n- **Precision:** how exactly a location is known: town, street or building.\n\n## 2. Functional requirements\n## 7. Evaluation specifications\nResults are saved as JSON plus a chart under `eval/results/`, and each is produced by one command.\n\n### 7.1 Evals A to D\n- **A, the archive read:**\n  - pages and articles read, and candidates per year\n  - reports per million articles, by year and by state\n  - the term mix and an OCR-quality distribution\n  - prefilter recall: a random-sample upper bound (rule of three when no misses are found) and the misses found in the near-miss pool, with the lexicon changes they caused\n- **B, the reader:**\n  - kind accuracy and macro-F1, and report precision, recall and F1\n  - field match rates, and the share of quotes verified\n  - the hallucinated-quote rate\n  - cost per 10,000 articles and latency\n  - bootstrap 95% intervals throughout\n  - the headline is the accuracy gap and the cost per 10,000 articles\n- **C, the investigations:** case files written, named deaths found, cases explained or exposed, then-and-now differences, the claim-verification rate and dropped claims, and Gemma against Ultramarine on the same cases (claims, verification rate, cost, latency).\n- **D, the app:** Lighthouse on mobile, axe, contrast, e2e on phone and desktop in both modes, and the walks counts if walks are built.\n\n### 7.2 Reader ablations\n| ID | What changes | Why it matters |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | Base 4B, tuned 4B, teacher | The headline comparison |\n| B2 | Training set size (a learning curve of at least 3 points) | Whether more teacher labels would help |\n| B3 | LoRA rank and learning rate (a small grid, within credits) | Picks the trained model |\n| B4 | Output format: fields with quotes against kind only | The cost of grounding |\n| B5 | Quote verifier on and off, plus a threshold sweep | Precision of the fields shown |\n| B6 | Triage on and off | Reports lost against cost saved |\n| B7 | Slices by OCR quality | Robustness to rough scans |\n| B8 | Slices by decade | Language drift from 1774 to 1963 |\n| B9 | Base 4B zero-shot against few-shot | Makes the baseline fair |\n| B10 | Reprint leakage removed, or not | Proves the scores aren't inflated |\n\nModel selection uses a dev split. The gold set is used only for these final runs.\n\n### 7.3 Edge-case suite\nEach slice uses at least 5 gold items where the archive has them:\n- E1: sermons and hymns about the Holy Ghost\n- E2: idioms (\"ghost of a chance\", \"gave up the ghost\", \"not the ghost of a\")\n- E3: ghost stories as fiction, serials and Christmas stories\n- E4: theatre and illusion adverts (Pepper's ghost), patent medicine and real estate\n- E5: spiritualist séances and rappings (`POLICY.md` decides their kind)\n- E6: hoax exposures and pranksters caught\n- E7: humour and joke columns\n- E8: phantom ships, trains and lights\n- E9: one story reprinted under different datelines\n- E10: badly garbled OCR\n- E11: segmentation errors, where several items are merged into one article\n- E12: non-English text\n- E13: \"Ghost\" as a surname or a place name\n- E14: political figures of speech (\"the ghost of the tariff\")\n\n## 8. Traceability","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"ff2f94ef-d996-4b40-b98e-727fbcaa3472","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"55de0834-0b60-49d3-83ca-e6ced1195ce0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
