n 36's frozen set:\n142:    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\nDocs/RESUME.md:52:  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories, and the reader's job is 1,002,205 printings.\nDocs/RESUME.md:80:- **The reader** reads 974,399 first printings and 27,806 longer members. The Tinker credit check weighs that before 2C's full pass.\nDocs/DECISIONS.md:788:- **For 2C:** split gold, dev and train by story id. The reader reads each story's first printing and its longer members.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"serverClassifierContext":{"request":"998867a3-92e5-4374-a1c2-ce08c153c78a","context":{"git_state":{"cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","root":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","branch":"phase-2c-reader","default_branch":null,"status":{"clean":true,"counts":{"staged":0,"modified":0,"untracked":null,"untracked_normal":0},"porcelain":null,"truncated":false},"visibility":{"origin":{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"},"push_remote":"origin","remotes":[{"name":"origin","host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}],"visibility_cache":[{"host":"github.com","remote":"Hotragn/Paperghosts","visibility":"private"}]}},"live_cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","platform":"macos"}},"sandboxed":false,"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4f0362d2-9021-44dd-a4d0-f21f6ff15a3d","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"classifier"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","id":"6fa640a2-3287-40ae-918b-ede541c24920","timestamp":"2026-10-31T06:34:30.990Z","version":"2.1.309","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"7b35af0d1ba22d1b1b7d4c91038d50b583ea5d544dd1607adac5368903cb8a35","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","dangerous-tool-use-2026-09-03","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","afk-mode-2026-01-31","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"max"}},"base":"5a75bace-5278-4d79-9f1e-9a93625d528b","keep":631,"tail":["c1e1ab3299409578d4668c8543e5e9c3e11c579b63f053390f4b6b368114012f","c30c8593ae27c25c4dafef13ee4b9f1dc65eae390cf76f077ac4558131d421ce"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",632,"content",0],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"363ed643dfcbfd1c4b6e36ad0485809c788a981f8534c4cc198a32f104e31c55"}
{"parentUuid":"75b22b0a-2c3a-40bc-b66a-7d1756891b8b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgZrEWYXyuEJroypSCpG4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YAj7bp1Rv5GXFeVjRa7tK5","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"- **For 2C:** split gold, dev and train by story id. The reader reads each story's first printing and its longer members.\\n\"\nnew = old + '''- **The EM's calls on this step (2026-10-31):**\n  - **The stories stand**, as recommended. Adding the body's links to them is measured in 2D, on a fresh draw.\n  - **The reader reads every triaged candidate, not the job above** (RDR-11, ARCHITECTURE 3.2). This supersedes this decision's reader rule and its \"for 2C\" note.\n    - The skip rule would leave 233,917 printings unread, and 38,127 of them run past the 600 words the shingles see.\n    - \"One story\" allows paragraphs added at either end, so a local paragraph or a different ending in a skipped member would never be read.\n    - Stories stay the unit for display and for counts.\n    - A member whose reading differs from its first printing's becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It differs if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person. 2D counts these members, and they double as false-merge candidates.\n    - If 2C's Tinker credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, the step stops. The EM gets the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings. That trade-off is the owner's.\n  - **2C splits gold, dev and train by the most inclusive grouping, not by story id.** That's connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's 55,711 links (decision 37). Chaining only makes a split safer.\n  - **A limitation, and the EM's check:** the reading agents saw 400 words of each printing.\n    - 184 of the 318 pairs the stories join, in the per-candidate, per-cluster and near-threshold strata, have a printing longer than that (`scripts/clusters.py unseen`, `eval/results/phase2b/clusters_unseen.json`).\n    - Where both printings run at least 50 words past it (127 pairs), the check compares the two tails' unsampled five-word runs with the openings'.\n    - The EM read five low pairs: `eval-0040`, `0052`, `0217`, `0261` and `0576`. I read the four others among this ranking's lowest eight: `eval-0100`, `0251`, `0255` and `0509`.\n    - All nine are one text. What lowers their tails is cuts, OCR noise, shifted article boundaries, and items glued on by segmentation. `eval-0040` is two overlapping windows of one instalment.\n    - 2D's fresh draw shows its readers the full texts.\n  - **For 2D: digits in the shingles,** measured on the fresh draw. `eval-0508`, ocean-freight columns a year apart, has 0.267 of the shorter's shingles in the other, above the threshold, because the tokens drop the figures that tell the two apart.\n  - My calls on the hard cases stand, and so does the mapping of decision 30's protocol.\n'''\nassert s.count(old) == 1; s = s.replace(old, new); p.write_text(s)\n\nb = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\"); s = b.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"   - Gold, dev and train split by story id, a story's first printing's article id (decision 36). The reader reads each story's first printing, and its members at least 25% longer.\\n\",\n  \"   - Gold, dev and train split by the most inclusive grouping: connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's links (decisions 36 and 37). `scripts/check_leakage.py` compares whole texts too, and the training pool takes at most one printing per story.\\n\"),\n (\"   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\\n\",\n  \"   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\\n\"\n  \"   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.\\n\"\n  \"   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\\n\"),\n (\"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\",\n  \"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\"\n  \"    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.\\n\"\n  \"  - Count the members whose reading differs from their first printing's. Each is shown as a report of its own, and is a false-merge candidate.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nb.write_text(s)\n\nr = Path(\"Docs/RESUME.md\"); s = r.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories, and the reader's job is 1,002,205 printings.\\n\",\n  \"  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories. Decision 36's skip rule would have made the reader's job 1,002,205 printings, but the EM's call keeps the reader on every triaged candidate.\\n\"),\n (\"- **The reader** reads 974,399 first printings and 27,806 longer members. The Tinker credit check weighs that before 2C's full pass.\\n\",\n  \"- **The reader reads every triaged candidate, 1,236,122** (the EM's call on decision 36). Stories stay the unit for display and counts. The Tinker credit check weighs the job before 2C's full pass, and a shortfall goes to the EM and the owner.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nr.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat","description":"Record the EM's calls in decision 36 and fix the plan and STATUS"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2567,"cache_read_input_tokens":940727,"output_tokens":2303,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2567,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2303,"cache_read_input_tokens":940727,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2567,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2567},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01YAj7bp1Rv5GXFeVjRa7tK5":{"command":"cd \"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts\" && uv run python - <<'EOF'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np = Path(\"Docs/DECISIONS.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"- **For 2C:** split gold, dev and train by story id. The reader reads each story's first printing and its longer members.\\n\"\nnew = old + '''- **The EM's calls on this step (2026-10-31):**\n  - **The stories stand**, as recommended. Adding the body's links to them is measured in 2D, on a fresh draw.\n  - **The reader reads every triaged candidate, not the job above** (RDR-11, ARCHITECTURE 3.2). This supersedes this decision's reader rule and its \"for 2C\" note.\n    - The skip rule would leave 233,917 printings unread, and 38,127 of them run past the 600 words the shingles see.\n    - \"One story\" allows paragraphs added at either end, so a local paragraph or a different ending in a skipped member would never be read.\n    - Stories stay the unit for display and for counts.\n    - A member whose reading differs from its first printing's becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It differs if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person. 2D counts these members, and they double as false-merge candidates.\n    - If 2C's Tinker credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, the step stops. The EM gets the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings. That trade-off is the owner's.\n  - **2C splits gold, dev and train by the most inclusive grouping, not by story id.** That's connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's 55,711 links (decision 37). Chaining only makes a split safer.\n  - **A limitation, and the EM's check:** the reading agents saw 400 words of each printing.\n    - 184 of the 318 pairs the stories join, in the per-candidate, per-cluster and near-threshold strata, have a printing longer than that (`scripts/clusters.py unseen`, `eval/results/phase2b/clusters_unseen.json`).\n    - Where both printings run at least 50 words past it (127 pairs), the check compares the two tails' unsampled five-word runs with the openings'.\n    - The EM read five low pairs: `eval-0040`, `0052`, `0217`, `0261` and `0576`. I read the four others among this ranking's lowest eight: `eval-0100`, `0251`, `0255` and `0509`.\n    - All nine are one text. What lowers their tails is cuts, OCR noise, shifted article boundaries, and items glued on by segmentation. `eval-0040` is two overlapping windows of one instalment.\n    - 2D's fresh draw shows its readers the full texts.\n  - **For 2D: digits in the shingles,** measured on the fresh draw. `eval-0508`, ocean-freight columns a year apart, has 0.267 of the shorter's shingles in the other, above the threshold, because the tokens drop the figures that tell the two apart.\n  - My calls on the hard cases stand, and so does the mapping of decision 30's protocol.\n'''\nassert s.count(old) == 1; s = s.replace(old, new); p.write_text(s)\n\nb = Path(\"Docs/BUILD-PLAN.md\"); s = b.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"   - Gold, dev and train split by story id, a story's first printing's article id (decision 36). The reader reads each story's first printing, and its members at least 25% longer.\\n\",\n  \"   - Gold, dev and train split by the most inclusive grouping: connected components over eval A's links and the body probe's links (decisions 36 and 37). `scripts/check_leakage.py` compares whole texts too, and the training pool takes at most one printing per story.\\n\"),\n (\"   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\\n\",\n  \"   - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.\\n\"\n  \"   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.\\n\"\n  \"   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings.\\n\"),\n (\"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\",\n  \"    - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.\\n\"\n  \"    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.\\n\"\n  \"  - Count the members whose reading differs from their first printing's. Each is shown as a report of its own, and is a false-merge candidate.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nb.write_text(s)\n\nr = Path(\"Docs/RESUME.md\"); s = r.read_text()\nedits = [\n (\"  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories, and the reader's job is 1,002,205 printings.\\n\",\n  \"  - v2 has 974,399 distinct stories. Decision 36's skip rule would have made the reader's job 1,002,205 printings, but the EM's call keeps the reader on every triaged candidate.\\n\"),\n (\"- **The reader** reads 974,399 first printings and 27,806 longer members. The Tinker credit check weighs that before 2C's full pass.\\n\",\n  \"- **The reader reads every triaged candidate, 1,236,122** (the EM's call on decision 36). Stories stay the unit for display and counts. The Tinker credit check weighs the job before 2C's full pass, and a shortfall goes to the EM and the owner.\\n\"),\n]\nfor old, new in edits:\n    assert s.count(old) == 1, old[:60]\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\nr.write_text(s)\nprint(\"ok\")\nEOF\ngit diff --stat","description":"Record the EM's calls in decision 36 and fix the plan and STATUS"}},"serverClassifierRequest":"d166d4e0-3c3c-47ab-812b-49e3d8c26cd0","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgZrEVTokqGciJaUi2C5w","requestRef":"6fa640a2-3287-40ae-918b-ede541c24920","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7658da0a-ba33-4201-9daa-ef924fc99abb","timestamp":"2026-10-31T06:34:49.432Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sess