s claims of spirit control and of a felt presence of the dead. Decision 30 counts two such articles as borderline reports, and they are half of the reports it found."]},{"oldStart":126,"oldLines":6,"newStart":126,"newLines":8,"lines":[" 9. The local export and the offline proof."," 10. The full pass over all triaged candidates.","    - Lexicon v2 makes the reader's job 1,236,122 candidates, 17.7% more than v1's (decision 31). The Tinker credit check weighs that before the pass starts.","+   - **Every triaged candidate is read** (the EM's call, decision 36). A member that reads differently from its story's first printing becomes a report of its own, shown as printed inside its story. It counts as different if it's a report where the first printing isn't one, or if it gives another place, date or person.","+   - If the credit check finds that every candidate doesn't fit, stop. Bring the EM the shortfall, and the skip rule's loss, measured on a seeded draw of skipped members read beside their first printings."," "," **Gate**"," - The gold hash hasn't changed since the freeze, and the leakage check passes."]},{"oldStart":140,"oldLines":6,"newStart":142,"newLines":8,"lines":["   - Cluster with decision 36's stories at its tuned 0.25. Before loading, measure two changes on a fresh draw, never on decision 36's frozen set:","     - the body's links added to the blocking. Its probe found 76 of 80 such pairs to be one story, outside eval A's links.","     - a floor on the share of the longer printing. Three large clusters still join two texts that each hold a short first printing.","+    - digits in the shingles. `eval-0508`, freight columns a year apart, passes the threshold because the tokens drop their figures.","+  - Count the members whose reading differs from their first printing's. Each is shown as a report of its own, and is a false-merge candidate.","   - Before choosing int8 embeddings over float32, measure their neighbours against float32's on real embeddings. Decision 33's check used synthetic vectors.","   - The places autocomplete index, `places_search`, needs a free Search slot (decision 33). `make db-init` creates it once there is one.","   - Fetch the loc.gov title records only for the LCCNs among stored printings, as decision 29 does for pages, cached (`paperghosts/geo/loc.py`). A paper's place is checked against its record (decision 34), and without one it stands unchecked."]}]},{"filePath":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts/Docs/DECISIONS.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":786,"oldLines":3,"newStart":786,"newLines":20,"lines":["   - **Proposed for the EM, not done:** add the body's links to the blocking, with the direct-match rule keeping them from chaining, and measure it on a fresh draw. Adopting it now would mean tuning on the frozen set."," - **BUDGET.md's third scenario** now takes the stories' sizes (`scripts/budget_stories.py`): 0.609 stories per printing in v1's candidates and 0.820 in those v2 added. That gives 62,402 stories at the top of the range, against 61,960, needing 461.8 MB as stored and 372.5 MB with every lever. The conclusions stand: nothing fits beside `sample_mflix`, and everything fits without it."," - **For 2C:** split gold, dev and train by story id. The reader reads each story's first printing and its longer members.","+- **The EM's calls on this step (2026-10-31):**","+  - **The stories stand**, as recommended. Adding the body's links to them is measured in 2D, on a fresh draw.","+  - **The reader reads every triaged candidate, not the job above** (RDR-11, ARCHITECTURE 3.2). This supersedes this decision's reader rule and its \"for 2C\" note.","+    - The skip rule would leave 233,917 printings unread, and 38,127 of them run past the 600 words the shingles see.","+    - \"One story\" allows paragraphs added at either end, so a local paragraph or a different ending in a skipped member would never be read.","+    - Stories stay the unit for display and for counts.","